1
00:00:01,368 --> 00:00:03,237
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:06,473
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:09,477
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,713
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:12,747 --> 00:00:15,683
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:18,653
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:18,687 --> 00:00:21,688
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:21,722 --> 00:00:23,492
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:26,027
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:28,228 --> 00:00:31,298
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:31,332 --> 00:00:34,568
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:34,602 --> 00:00:37,472
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:37,505 --> 00:00:40,708
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:40,742 --> 00:00:43,678
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:43,712 --> 00:00:46,948
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:46,982 --> 00:00:50,218
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:50,252 --> 00:00:52,453
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:54,822 --> 00:00:56,690
LET'S GO.

19
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:57,992
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:00:58,025 --> 00:00:59,293
HI, GIRL.

21
00:00:59,327 --> 00:01:01,095
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:02,663
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:05,800
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:09,037
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:12,007
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,908
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:17,778
♪ FOR... ♪

28
00:01:31,292 --> 00:01:33,628
HI EVERYBODY, WELCOME TO
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

29
00:01:33,662 --> 00:01:35,830
I'M JOEL ROBINSON.
OH LOOK, HERE COMES

30
00:01:35,863 --> 00:01:38,265
- TOM SERVO, CROW T. ROBOT.
- HELLO.

31
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:40,100
- EVENING.
- HEY, COME ON
UP HERE, YOU GUYS.

32
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:41,702
I WANNA SHOW YOU
THIS TOOTHPICK SCULPTURE

33
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:44,072
I'VE BEEN WORKING ON
FOR THE LAST THREE YEARS.

34
00:01:44,105 --> 00:01:46,073
YOU'VE BEEN WORKING
THREE YEARS ON THAT?

35
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:48,442
- WELL, YEAH,
AND NIGHTS AND WEEKENDS.
- IT'S NOT VERY GOOD.

36
00:01:48,475 --> 00:01:50,143
- SHH.
- I MEAN, UH, WHAT IS IT?

37
00:01:50,177 --> 00:01:52,580
IT'S A SCALE
REPRODUCTION MODEL

38
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:54,848
OF MONTICELLO
RENDERED IN TOOTHPICK.

39
00:01:54,882 --> 00:01:56,550
I GOT THE IDEA
OFF THE NICKEL, SEE?

40
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:58,787
IT'S BEAUTIFUL-- WHERE'D YOU
GET ALL THE TOOTHPICKS?

41
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,522
WHAT, ARE YOU KIDDING?
WE'RE ON A SPACESHIP.

42
00:02:00,555 --> 00:02:01,990
THIS PLACE IS CRAWLING
WITH TOOTHPICKS.

43
00:02:02,023 --> 00:02:03,457
WELL, IT REALLY IS COOL, JOEL.

44
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:05,560
OF COURSE, YOU KNOW
WE'LL HAVE TO BREAK IT.

45
00:02:05,593 --> 00:02:07,562
IT'S NOTHING PERSONAL,
YOU UNDERSTAND.

46
00:02:07,595 --> 00:02:09,897
IT'S JUST A THING
WE HAVE TO DO.

47
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:12,233
- YEAH.
- OKAY.
- HUH?

48
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,500
SURE, GO AHEAD,
THAT'S WHY I MADE IT.

49
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:15,370
SMASH AWAY.
NO-NO-NO, JOEL!

50
00:02:15,403 --> 00:02:18,072
- YOU'RE RUINING IT FOR ME!
- YEAH, I FEEL DIRTY.

51
00:02:18,105 --> 00:02:20,642
COMMERCIAL SIGN IN
FIVE SECONDS.

52
00:02:20,675 --> 00:02:22,077
SURE SEEMS LIKE A WASTE,

53
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:25,145
IT BEING ALL TOOTHPICKY
AND FRAGILE AND ALL.

54
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:26,547
COMMERCIAL SIGN NOW.

55
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,382
I'M JUST GONNA
LEAVE IT HERE.

56
00:02:28,415 --> 00:02:30,285
UNATTENDED.

57
00:02:30,318 --> 00:02:32,087
TO DRY.

58
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:34,322
UH, WE'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

59
00:02:34,355 --> 00:02:36,023
[BOTS SCREAM]

60
00:02:44,798 --> 00:02:46,300
SO HOW WAS IT FOR YOU?

61
00:02:46,333 --> 00:02:47,502
WELL, AS FAR AS
BREAKING STUFF GOES,

62
00:02:47,535 --> 00:02:49,537
IT WAS GOOD, NOT GREAT.

63
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:52,340
YEAH, NOT AS GOOD AS
THAT CERAMIC BELL COLLECTION.

64
00:02:52,373 --> 00:02:55,008
OH, MILAVETZ AND ASSOCIATES
ARE CALLING.

65
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,747
OKAY, AND THIS?

66
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:02,483
OH, LET ME SEE, OH--
[LAUGHS]

67
00:03:02,517 --> 00:03:05,287
THAT'S MY OLD HEAD.

68
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,588
JUST FILE THAT UNDER
FRANK'S FIRST HEAD, OKAY?

69
00:03:07,622 --> 00:03:08,923
RIGHT.

70
00:03:08,957 --> 00:03:10,925
OH, HI, JOEL, UH.

71
00:03:10,958 --> 00:03:14,062
LOOK, WE'RE WAY TOO BUSY TO EVEN
DO AN INVENTION THIS WEEK.

72
00:03:14,095 --> 00:03:15,263
WE'RE BEING AUDITED.

73
00:03:15,297 --> 00:03:19,100
YOU GO RIGHT AHEAD, THOUGH.

74
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:21,002
IT'S A DAKTARI STOOL.

75
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:23,503
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

76
00:03:23,537 --> 00:03:25,807
DAKTARI STOOL?

77
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,575
WHATEVER. ANYWAY, JOEL,

78
00:03:27,608 --> 00:03:29,443
IT'S A MADHOUSE DOWN HERE.

79
00:03:29,477 --> 00:03:32,613
WE'RE BEING AUDITED BY THE
FRATERNAL ORDER OF MAD SCIENCE.

80
00:03:32,647 --> 00:03:34,948
YOU KNOW, ONE OF THOSE
"ARE YOU REALLY MAD ENOUGH"

81
00:03:34,982 --> 00:03:37,052
- SORT OF THINGS--
- FRANK.

82
00:03:37,085 --> 00:03:39,220
THREE JARVIK SEVENS.

83
00:03:39,253 --> 00:03:40,988
PUT 'EM IN THE JUNK DRAWER,
JEEZ.

84
00:03:41,022 --> 00:03:43,692
DIDN'T THE TEMP AGENCY
TEST YOU ON ANY OF THIS STUFF?

85
00:03:43,725 --> 00:03:45,125
WELL, I'M A LITTLE
OFF MY GAME.

86
00:03:45,158 --> 00:03:48,763
I'M NOT NORMALLY REQUIRED
TO WEAR LEG-IRON LIKE THIS.

87
00:03:48,797 --> 00:03:52,167
SAY, WHAT IS THE DEAL WITH
THIS GUY AND THOSE CUTE ROBOTS?

88
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:54,702
LISTEN, MR. $4.25 AN HOUR.

89
00:03:54,735 --> 00:03:57,272
YOU STICK WITH THE BOXES,
AND I'LL HANDLE THE EXPERIMENT.

90
00:03:57,305 --> 00:04:00,442
IS THAT ALL RIGHT WITH YOU?

91
00:04:00,475 --> 00:04:01,742
FRANK, CAN I SEE YOU
A MINUTE?

92
00:04:01,775 --> 00:04:03,310
SURE THING, DR. F.

93
00:04:03,343 --> 00:04:04,945
SAY, STEVE, THIS TEMP STUFF

94
00:04:04,978 --> 00:04:06,480
IS WORKING OUT GREAT,
DON'T YOU THINK?

95
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:07,915
WELL, I'M SO GLAD
YOUR LITTLE FRIEND

96
00:04:07,948 --> 00:04:09,683
IS WORKING OUT
SO NICELY, FRANK.

97
00:04:09,717 --> 00:04:11,418
NOW WHAT ABOUT SENDING JOEL
THE MOVIE, YOU BOOB?

98
00:04:11,452 --> 00:04:13,520
OH, THE MOVIE,
THE MOVIE, THE MOVIE.

99
00:04:13,553 --> 00:04:15,022
OH, FOR THE LOVE OF...

100
00:04:15,055 --> 00:04:17,225
THE MOVIE...

101
00:04:17,258 --> 00:04:19,960
[FORRESTER GROANS]

102
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:22,830
OH, FRANK, LOOK. REMEMBER?

103
00:04:22,863 --> 00:04:24,698
THE DOUBLE-BUTT GRAFT.

104
00:04:24,732 --> 00:04:26,667
MY SCIENCE PROJECT
FROM EVILOS.

105
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,470
I GRAFTED THE BUTT OF A DOG
ONTO THE BUTT OF A CAT.

106
00:04:29,503 --> 00:04:30,872
SURE, THEY ALL LAUGHED.

107
00:04:30,905 --> 00:04:33,107
DR. F, THE MOVIE. THE MOVIE.

108
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,843
OH, RIGHT, UH. HERE IT IS.

109
00:04:35,877 --> 00:04:37,945
MITCHELL, STARRING
JOE DON BAKER.

110
00:04:37,978 --> 00:04:39,947
YOU GUYS WATCH
JOE DON BAKER MOVIES?

111
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,817
OH, LOOK, JUST GET
BACK TO WORK, TEMP BOY.

112
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:45,118
- ALL RIGHT.
- WELL, HERE IT COMES, JOEL.

113
00:04:45,152 --> 00:04:46,720
MITCHELL. IT'S A...

114
00:04:46,753 --> 00:04:48,857
SUPER-SECRET SPY...

115
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:50,692
HAS A MOTORCYCLE...

116
00:04:50,725 --> 00:04:52,093
MAROONED IN SPACE...

117
00:04:52,127 --> 00:04:54,762
MEETS HERCULES OR NOT.

118
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:55,997
[FORRESTER GROANS]

119
00:04:56,030 --> 00:04:58,465
WATCH IT AND WEEP,
JOEL-PROLE-MOLE.

120
00:04:58,498 --> 00:05:01,168
SEND HIM THE MOVIE, FRANK.

121
00:05:01,202 --> 00:05:03,537
FRANK. THE MOVIE.

122
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:06,173
- I LIKE THE WAY YOU--
- [ALL] MOVIE SIGN!

123
00:05:16,317 --> 00:05:18,318
HEY LOOK, A SEX FILM.

124
00:05:21,422 --> 00:05:23,390
MITTENS? AN ACTION FILM
CALLED MITTENS?

125
00:05:23,423 --> 00:05:24,992
JOE DON BAKER IS MITTENS.

126
00:05:25,025 --> 00:05:27,495
OR IS IT MITHRIL?
OH, WAIT, IT'S MITCHELL.

127
00:05:27,528 --> 00:05:29,297
OH, THE MARTHA MITCHELL STORY.

128
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:30,998
JOE DON BAKER
IS MARTHA MITCHELL.

129
00:05:31,032 --> 00:05:32,667
YUCK.

130
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:39,273
IT'S BIGFOOT!

131
00:05:39,307 --> 00:05:41,508
WHO'S THE PUFFY GUY WHO'S
A BIG BLURRY SEX MACHINE?

132
00:05:41,542 --> 00:05:43,110
- [ALL] MITCHELL!
- THAT MITCHELL

133
00:05:43,143 --> 00:05:44,512
- IS ONE FAT--
- SHUT YOUR MOUTH!

134
00:05:44,545 --> 00:05:45,947
JUST TALKING ABOUT MITCHELL.

135
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:48,282
LOOKS LIKE GRENDEL.

136
00:05:48,315 --> 00:05:50,217
HEY, LINDA EVANS,
THAT WAS HER PRE-YANNI DAYS.

137
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:52,320
BEFORE HER FACE
WAS PULLED TAUT.

138
00:05:52,353 --> 00:05:55,055
LOOKS KIND OF LIKE
A SLOW-MOTION SNEEZE.

139
00:05:55,088 --> 00:05:56,757
[CROW LAUGHS]

140
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:59,827
YEAH, HERE'S YOUR
LOSER ACTOR BOUQUET.

141
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:03,430
ANY MOVIE WITH WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA
IN IT IS OKAY BY ME.

142
00:06:03,463 --> 00:06:05,500
♪ WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA
WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA ♪

143
00:06:05,533 --> 00:06:09,070
♪ IT WAS THE THIRD
OF SEPTEMBER ♪

144
00:06:09,103 --> 00:06:11,772
♪ THE DAY
I'LL ALWAYS REMEMBER ♪

145
00:06:11,805 --> 00:06:15,175
NEVER CORNER A MITCHELL.
SEE HOW HE REACTS?

146
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:17,445
LOOKS LIKE HE'S DOING
A NIXON OR SOMETHING.

147
00:06:17,478 --> 00:06:18,813
LOOKS LIKE
A MIDDLE-AGED CHUCKY.

148
00:06:18,847 --> 00:06:20,413
HE LOOKS LIKE
THE WRATHFUL BUDDHA.

149
00:06:20,447 --> 00:06:22,550
HE LOOKS LIKE THE MOON
IN A TRIP TO THE MOON.

150
00:06:22,583 --> 00:06:25,953
[SERVO LAUGHS]

151
00:06:25,987 --> 00:06:29,590
MAN, I CAN'T
GET MY ARMS DOWN.

152
00:06:29,623 --> 00:06:32,427
NOW HE LOOKS LIKE
A SMALLMOUTH BASS.

153
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,695
HAH, NOW HE LOOKS LIKE
HE'S IN A WIND TUNNEL.

154
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:37,030
- UM...
- ♪ WAKA-CHIKA... ♪

155
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,400
MAYBE HE'S DOING
TAI-CHI OR SOMETHING.

156
00:06:39,433 --> 00:06:42,937
[ALL] ♪ WAKA-CHIKA... ♪

157
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:45,540
MITCHELL'S ON THE CORNER.

158
00:06:45,573 --> 00:06:47,208
MITCHELL!

159
00:06:49,477 --> 00:06:52,280
EEGAH....

160
00:06:52,313 --> 00:06:53,613
SHTEMLO.

161
00:06:53,647 --> 00:06:55,650
WATCH OUT FOR SNAKES.

162
00:06:55,683 --> 00:06:58,185
WE'VE HIDDEN A MITCHELL
SOMEWHERE IN THIS PICTURE.

163
00:06:58,218 --> 00:07:00,555
MITCHELL,
WILL YOU STAND UP, PLEASE?

164
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:05,827
THE LUNATIC IS ON THE GRASS.

165
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,862
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

166
00:07:10,598 --> 00:07:13,533
JOHNNY NASH BREAKS INTO
A SUBURBAN HOME.

167
00:07:13,567 --> 00:07:16,037
MITCHELL!

168
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:17,972
HEY, IT'S ONE OF THE KIDS
FROM FAME.

169
00:07:18,005 --> 00:07:19,873
- WHICH ONE?
- ANY OF 'EM.

170
00:07:25,045 --> 00:07:26,380
JOHNNY MATHIS!

171
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:28,950
♪ IT'S NOT
FOR ME TO SAY... ♪

172
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:36,323
THE GREEN HORNET.

173
00:07:36,357 --> 00:07:38,325
SHE CAN'T BE MORE THAN 16.

174
00:07:38,358 --> 00:07:40,327
EVERY TIME SHE
GIVES ME A MANICURE,

175
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,930
SHE TELLS ME SHE'S HAVING
A DIFFERENT AFFAIR.

176
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:45,098
AND SHE TELLS ME EVERYTHING.

177
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:48,768
I MEAN, ALL THE REAL
HOT AND JUICY DETAILS.

178
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:51,338
I CAN'T EVEN
KEEP MY FINGERS STILL.

179
00:07:51,372 --> 00:07:53,307
- MUST BE A FACULTY MEETING.
- SHUT UP.

180
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,710
I'M THINKING.

181
00:07:55,743 --> 00:07:59,613
UH, IT'S OPEN.

182
00:07:59,647 --> 00:08:02,250
LOOKS LIKE HE'S BREAKING OUT
OF HIS HOUSE.

183
00:08:04,352 --> 00:08:05,518
AL NOGA?

184
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:08,890
NOPE, STILL JOHNNY MATHIS.

185
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:10,423
OH, YEAH,
CLOSE IT AND LOCK IT.

186
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:14,195
YOU DON'T WANT
ANYONE COMING IN.

187
00:08:14,228 --> 00:08:15,495
DOCTOR DETROIT.

188
00:08:15,528 --> 00:08:16,763
WITH SONGS BY DEVO,

189
00:08:16,797 --> 00:08:19,733
CUTTING CREW,
AND HAIRCUT 100.

190
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:21,468
♪ I SAY TO MYSELF ♪

191
00:08:21,502 --> 00:08:23,303
♪ IT'S WONDERFUL ♪

192
00:08:23,337 --> 00:08:25,940
A PICTURE OF MO CONNOLLY?
OH.

193
00:08:25,973 --> 00:08:29,810
NO, NOT THE LIMITED EDITION
STAR TREK COLLECTOR PLATES!

194
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:33,013
HEY, LUCAS McCAIN
LIVES HERE!

195
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,852
THEY'RE ON A COLLISION COURSE
TO WACKINESS!

196
00:08:37,885 --> 00:08:40,822
[SERVO LAUGHS]

197
00:08:40,855 --> 00:08:42,790
ALL RIGHT, LAST CALL.
DRINK 'EM UP.

198
00:08:42,823 --> 00:08:45,593
[SERVO HICCUPS]

199
00:08:45,627 --> 00:08:46,960
LET'S NOT TALK.

200
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:49,563
- [WOMAN LAUGHS, SIGHS]
- [SERVO SIGHS]

201
00:08:49,597 --> 00:08:52,833
HEY-- OH, A GOLDSTAR.

202
00:08:52,867 --> 00:08:55,502
MOVE IT ALONG, PLEASE.

203
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:59,240
SHOULD I TELL HER?

204
00:08:59,273 --> 00:09:02,310
LADIES, YOU KNOW
WHERE EVERYTHING IS.

205
00:09:02,343 --> 00:09:04,412
I WANT YOU TO EXERCISE
THE BOTTOMLESS

206
00:09:04,445 --> 00:09:06,413
RESOURCES OF
YOUR IMAGINATION.

207
00:09:06,447 --> 00:09:08,282
UH, CAN I HAVE A LAMP?

208
00:09:08,315 --> 00:09:10,250
SURPRISE ME.

209
00:09:10,283 --> 00:09:12,887
THE WAY YOU ALWAYS DO.

210
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,388
COME ON, DON.
LET'S GET SOME JUICE.

211
00:09:14,422 --> 00:09:18,358
FRESH PANTIES ALL AROUND.

212
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:20,293
MIGHT BE ABLE TO KISS HER
TONIGHT, YOU KNOW.

213
00:09:20,327 --> 00:09:22,763
WHAT THE HELL DOES HE
THINK I AM, AN ACROBAT?

214
00:09:22,797 --> 00:09:25,032
AND SHE'S AN ACROBAT, TED!

215
00:09:27,902 --> 00:09:30,237
SANTA?

216
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:33,173
WAIT A MINUTE, I THINK MAYBE
THE SNOOP SISTERS ARE IN THERE.

217
00:09:33,207 --> 00:09:35,910
EH, I'M GONNA GET A SERIES
BEFORE STUART MARGOLIN.

218
00:09:37,478 --> 00:09:40,715
SHH.

219
00:09:40,748 --> 00:09:44,385
JOHNNY MATHIS?
ALL RIGHT, GET MY GUN.

220
00:09:44,418 --> 00:09:45,787
WELL, YOU KNOW,
IT'S NOT OFTEN YOU SEE

221
00:09:45,820 --> 00:09:46,853
JOHNNY MATHIS IN THE WILD.

222
00:09:46,887 --> 00:09:49,357
NO.

223
00:09:49,390 --> 00:09:52,125
NEED SOME CLEAN UNDERWEAR...
AND ONE OF THESE.

224
00:09:52,158 --> 00:09:53,927
HEY, A GUNDAROO.

225
00:09:56,363 --> 00:09:59,867
PSST! DON'T SHOOT ME,
THE BURGLAR.

226
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:02,168
SO, ARE WE GONNA
PLAY BRIDGE?

227
00:10:02,202 --> 00:10:04,472
WE GOT OURSELVES
A FISH, DON.

228
00:10:04,505 --> 00:10:06,573
- GET THE COPS--
- NO, WAIT!

229
00:10:06,607 --> 00:10:09,010
- COME ON, WALTER--
- SHH!

230
00:10:09,043 --> 00:10:12,278
UH, HELLO, THIS IS CARLTON,
YOUR DOORMAN.

231
00:10:12,312 --> 00:10:15,148
CEDAR LATTICE.
WORKS EVERY TIME.

232
00:10:15,182 --> 00:10:17,150
♪ CHANCES ARE-- HUH?

233
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:22,690
IF THAT'S JOHN SAXON,
I'M DEAD.

234
00:10:27,962 --> 00:10:31,365
SONNY, ARE WE, LIKE, BAIT?

235
00:10:31,398 --> 00:10:33,867
WE'RE CLOSED.

236
00:10:36,403 --> 00:10:38,572
MAYBE I SHOULD GET TO WORK.

237
00:10:38,605 --> 00:10:40,107
- HEY!
- WHAT?

238
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,108
- [GUNSHOT]
- OH!

239
00:10:46,013 --> 00:10:47,615
MEANWHILE, ON
AN ADAM-12 EPISODE

240
00:10:47,648 --> 00:10:49,750
NOT FAR AWAY.

241
00:10:49,783 --> 00:10:52,252
[POLICE RADIO CHATTER]

242
00:10:54,655 --> 00:10:56,857
OUR HERO,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.
RIGHT THERE.

243
00:10:56,890 --> 00:10:58,792
22, CAN YOU GIVE ME
A FIX ON MAPLE DRIVE?

244
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:00,293
- IS IT OFF BEVERLY GLEN?

245
00:11:00,327 --> 00:11:01,928
- THIS IS 22. YOU GOT IT.

246
00:11:01,962 --> 00:11:03,697
- IT'S ONE BLOCK EAST.
- ALL RIGHT.

247
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:07,000
- [SIREN BLARES]
- OH, JUST FIVE MORE MINUTES.

248
00:11:11,605 --> 00:11:14,342
MITCHELL, HONEY, WE'RE HOME.
PUT YOUR SHOES ON.

249
00:11:14,375 --> 00:11:17,377
WELL, PRIVATE ENTERPRISE
BEAT US TO IT.

250
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:19,080
HELLO, PUBLIC SECTOR.

251
00:11:19,113 --> 00:11:20,748
HEY, WHAT DO YOU SAY, JIMMY?

252
00:11:20,782 --> 00:11:22,517
- WHERE'S THE BODY?
- IN THE DEN.

253
00:11:22,550 --> 00:11:24,152
- WE POSED HIM.
- YOU GONNA NEED US AROUND HERE?

254
00:11:24,185 --> 00:11:25,820
NO, THAT'S OKAY, THANKS.

255
00:11:25,853 --> 00:11:27,555
WE'LL TAKE OFF THEN.
IT'S ALL YOURS.

256
00:11:27,588 --> 00:11:29,257
SURE.

257
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:31,058
RENT-A-COPS,
PRIVATE ENTERPRISE--

258
00:11:31,092 --> 00:11:32,292
WHY DON'T YOU
GO BACK TO THE MALL?

259
00:11:32,325 --> 00:11:33,593
HEY, YOU COMIN', MITCHELL?

260
00:11:33,627 --> 00:11:35,797
- YEAH.
- YOU GOT ANY
MOIST TOWELETTES?

261
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:38,765
RAGS? TOILET PAPER
OR SOMETHING?

262
00:11:38,798 --> 00:11:41,102
COME ON,
MR. "TWO YEARS FROM EISCHIED,"

263
00:11:41,135 --> 00:11:43,003
COME ON.

264
00:11:43,037 --> 00:11:46,073
I'M WALTER DEANEY, OFFICERS.
JUST COME THIS WAY.

265
00:11:46,107 --> 00:11:47,373
LOOKS LIKE
ONE OF THOSE WETBACKS--

266
00:11:47,407 --> 00:11:48,708
[ALL] HEY!

267
00:11:48,742 --> 00:11:50,443
--PULLED A GUN
FROM MY GUN RACK.

268
00:11:50,477 --> 00:11:52,312
FORTUNATELY, I GOT
TO ANOTHER GUN SOONER.

269
00:11:52,345 --> 00:11:54,382
HMM, SMART.

270
00:11:54,415 --> 00:11:56,150
HE GRABBED THAT COLT.

271
00:11:56,183 --> 00:11:59,253
I HAD NO CHOICE.
I HAD TO SHOOT HIM.

272
00:11:59,287 --> 00:12:00,687
WELL, YOU'RE RICH AND WHITE.

273
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,222
I DON'T SEE
A PROBLEM WITH IT.

274
00:12:07,695 --> 00:12:08,928
PRETTY CLEAN JOB.

275
00:12:08,962 --> 00:12:12,032
YUCK.

276
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:14,568
COME ON, IT'S FUN!

277
00:12:14,602 --> 00:12:16,237
YOU GOT A SOFA
I CAN STRETCH OUT ON

278
00:12:16,270 --> 00:12:18,338
FOR A LITTLE WHILE?

279
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:24,077
OH, THERE'S THE BODY.

280
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:25,378
HEY, HERE,
WATCH WHAT HAPPENS

281
00:12:25,412 --> 00:12:28,448
WHEN I STEP ON HIS ABDOMEN.

282
00:12:28,482 --> 00:12:31,585
I THINK HE'S GONNA NEED
A BIGGER BODY-BAG THAN THAT.

283
00:12:34,188 --> 00:12:36,623
ALL THOSE GUNS LOADED?

284
00:12:36,657 --> 00:12:38,692
SOME OF 'EM.

285
00:12:38,725 --> 00:12:40,127
NOT ALWAYS SURE WHICH.

286
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:43,563
THEY'RE RANDOMLY LOADED.
IT'S A LITTLE GAME I PLAY.

287
00:12:43,597 --> 00:12:45,732
ALL YOUR GUESTS LOADED?

288
00:12:49,403 --> 00:12:51,638
THE GUESTS ARE LEAVING.

289
00:12:51,672 --> 00:12:52,907
PARTY'S OVER.

290
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:55,408
♪ IT'S TIME
TO CALL IT A DAY ♪

291
00:12:55,442 --> 00:12:57,578
ANYBODY TELL THEM
THEY COULD LEAVE?

292
00:12:57,612 --> 00:12:59,180
I DID.

293
00:12:59,213 --> 00:13:01,382
THERE'S A POLICE INVESTIGATION
GOING ON HERE.

294
00:13:01,415 --> 00:13:02,683
OH, THERE IS?
I THOUGHT THERE WAS JUST

295
00:13:02,717 --> 00:13:06,620
A BIG SLOB
WALKING AROUND MY HOUSE.

296
00:13:06,653 --> 00:13:10,357
WHERE'S THE JOHN?
I'M GONNA FLUSH THIS.

297
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:13,393
MY GUEST HAS TO BE AT HIS DESK
AT EIGHT IN THE MORNING.

298
00:13:13,427 --> 00:13:14,728
HE'S AN IMPORTANT PERSON.

299
00:13:14,762 --> 00:13:16,897
MY SECRETARY WILL GIVE YOU
THEIR NAMES AND ADDRESSES.

300
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:19,867
AND DISAVOW ANY KNOWLEDGE
OF THEIR ACTIONS.

301
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:22,637
MAN, HE'S GOOD.

302
00:13:26,707 --> 00:13:28,842
MITCHELL!--
PARDON ME, MITCHELL!

303
00:13:31,545 --> 00:13:34,315
[CROW PANTS, WHEEZES]

304
00:13:34,348 --> 00:13:36,183
HEY, CAN I HAVE A SCOTCH?

305
00:13:36,217 --> 00:13:38,252
- WHAT'S YOUR NAME?
- MITCHELL.

306
00:13:38,285 --> 00:13:39,420
- HI!
- WHAT'S YOURS?

307
00:13:39,453 --> 00:13:41,788
WELL, FIND HIM,
WHEREVER HE IS!

308
00:13:41,822 --> 00:13:43,057
RAISE ALEX, WILL YOU?

309
00:13:43,090 --> 00:13:45,225
HE'S TALKING TO
COMMISSIONER GORDON.

310
00:13:45,258 --> 00:13:47,127
GET A HOLD OF MISTRETTA.

311
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,397
TELL HIM TO TALK TO GALLANO.

312
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:51,665
OKAY, SLEEVE LENGTH 34.

313
00:13:51,698 --> 00:13:54,535
36 INCH OUTSEAM,
AND A 32 INCH INSEAM.

314
00:13:54,568 --> 00:13:57,203
OKAY.

315
00:13:57,237 --> 00:13:59,273
ORSON BEAN, HE'S A COP!

316
00:14:01,908 --> 00:14:04,678
I TOLD MISTRETTA TO TALK
TO GALLANO, I THINK.

317
00:14:09,182 --> 00:14:10,450
WHAT?

318
00:14:18,692 --> 00:14:19,993
- MITCHELL.
- WHAT?

319
00:14:20,027 --> 00:14:21,895
PEOPLE DON'T LIKE YOU.

320
00:14:21,928 --> 00:14:23,997
IN FACT, I DON'T CARE
FOR YOU MYSELF.

321
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,467
- WHY IS THAT?
- PERHAPS OUR BRIEF
BUT BITTER AFFAIR?

322
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,335
YOU REFUSE TO SIGN
THIS REPORT.

323
00:14:28,368 --> 00:14:31,638
- WHY?
- D'AH, I'M STILL
ON THE FIRST QUESTION.

324
00:14:31,672 --> 00:14:33,907
WHAT KIND OF A POLICEMAN
ARE YOU ANYWAY?

325
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:36,010
WHAT'RE YOU GONNA DO,
FILE A SEPARATE REPORT?

326
00:14:36,043 --> 00:14:38,245
- I DON'T KNOW.
- WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

327
00:14:38,278 --> 00:14:41,115
- I DON'T KNOW.
- NONE OF DEANEY'S OTHER GUNS
WERE LOADED.

328
00:14:41,148 --> 00:14:43,050
NOW, THE COLLECTION'S
WAY UP HIGH ON THE WALL.

329
00:14:43,083 --> 00:14:45,352
THE BURGLAR, HE ONLY LOOKS
TO BE ABOUT 5'4" IS ALL.

330
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:46,753
SO, WHAT DOES THAT PROVE?

331
00:14:46,787 --> 00:14:49,657
IF DEANEY'S LYING, HE'S NOT
GONNA GET AWAY WITH IT.

332
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:51,458
I'LL COME OVER THERE!

333
00:14:51,492 --> 00:14:53,227
YOU'RE GONNA GET ME MAD,
MITCHELL, AND WHEN THAT HAPPENS,

334
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:54,495
I WOULDN'T WANNA
BE IN YOUR SHOES.

335
00:14:54,528 --> 00:14:55,795
- NOW, GET OUT.
- ALL RIGHT.

336
00:14:55,828 --> 00:14:57,732
MITCHELL'S A SENSIBLE COP.

337
00:14:57,765 --> 00:14:59,265
SEE ALDRIDGE.

338
00:14:59,298 --> 00:15:00,900
HE'S GOTTA SIGN IT FOR YOU.

339
00:15:00,933 --> 00:15:04,338
AND REMEMBER, DON'T YOU DARE
GO NEAR DEANEY.

340
00:15:04,372 --> 00:15:07,373
YOU FORGET ABOUT HIM.

341
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:08,942
THEY ARRESTED
HARLAN ELLISON!

342
00:15:08,975 --> 00:15:10,810
GOOD.

343
00:15:10,843 --> 00:15:13,213
COME IN, MITCHELL.
TAKE A SEAT.

344
00:15:13,247 --> 00:15:14,582
MOM SAID NO, HUH?

345
00:15:14,615 --> 00:15:17,583
SO YOU COME TO ME,
THE NICE COP.

346
00:15:17,617 --> 00:15:19,953
WAIT, HE SOUNDS AND SMELLS
LIKE WILLIAM CONRAD.

347
00:15:19,987 --> 00:15:21,688
CHIEF PALLIN HAS ORDERED
THE SURVEILLANCE

348
00:15:21,722 --> 00:15:23,857
OF A MAN CALLED
JAMES ARTHUR CUMMINGS.

349
00:15:23,890 --> 00:15:25,158
JAMES ARTHUR CUMMINGS.

350
00:15:25,192 --> 00:15:26,627
- YEAH, YOU HEARD OF HIM?
- NO.

351
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,228
IT'S A 24-HOUR SURVEILLANCE.
- [HEAVY BREATHING]

352
00:15:28,262 --> 00:15:29,463
AND I WANT YOU
TO STAY WITH HIM.

353
00:15:29,497 --> 00:15:31,665
SO, "A," YOU BUG HIM
ENOUGH THAT HE CRACKS,

354
00:15:31,698 --> 00:15:34,602
OR "B," HE COMES UP WITH
SOME KIND OF STATEMENT

355
00:15:34,635 --> 00:15:36,637
OR INCRIMINATES HIMSELF.

356
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,172
CONCERNING
A CRIME IN MEXICO.

357
00:15:38,205 --> 00:15:40,273
OR "C," YOU GET DRUNK
AND PASS OUT AGAIN.

358
00:15:40,307 --> 00:15:42,408
- WHO DO I GET?
- YOU GET NOBODY.

359
00:15:42,442 --> 00:15:44,778
- HMM?
- NOBODY.

360
00:15:44,812 --> 00:15:46,880
WHAT DO I DO FOR SLEEPING?
HOW ABOUT EATING?

361
00:15:46,913 --> 00:15:48,715
NOTHING'S GONNA HAPPEN
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT.

362
00:15:48,748 --> 00:15:50,283
- OH.
- I WANNA EAT!

363
00:15:50,317 --> 00:15:52,618
YOU GOT SIX HOURS SHUT-EYE
FROM MIDNIGHT TO 6:00 AM.

364
00:15:52,652 --> 00:15:53,820
BUT EATING!

365
00:15:53,853 --> 00:15:55,388
NOW, MITCHELL?

366
00:15:55,422 --> 00:15:56,623
THOSE ARE PALLIN'S ORDERS.

367
00:15:56,657 --> 00:16:00,027
- I'M HUNGRY.
- DO YOU WANNA CALL HIM?

368
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:01,928
SEE TYZACK-- HE'LL TAKE YOU
TO CUMMINGS' PLACE.

369
00:16:01,962 --> 00:16:04,998
IMPORT-EXPORT
OF STOLEN MERCHANDISE.

370
00:16:05,032 --> 00:16:06,867
THAT IS CUMMINGS' BIG SCENE.

371
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:08,635
THIS WEEK, IT'S A BIG
HEROIN HIJACK.

372
00:16:08,668 --> 00:16:10,070
COMES OUT OF MEXICO, A KILO.

373
00:16:10,103 --> 00:16:12,672
FULL KILO,
THAT'S TWO MILLION BUCKS.

374
00:16:12,705 --> 00:16:14,542
MAYBE PALLIN'S IDEA OF A JOKE,

375
00:16:14,575 --> 00:16:16,677
BUT LEANING ON CUMMINGS
IS NO JOKE, MY FRIEND.

376
00:16:16,710 --> 00:16:19,947
NO ONE LEANS ON CUMMINGS
'CAUSE HE STAMPS ON PEOPLE,

377
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,548
AND HE'S GOT A BIG SHOE.

378
00:16:21,582 --> 00:16:23,650
- LET ME ASK YOU SOMETHING--
- WHO ARE YOU?

379
00:16:23,683 --> 00:16:26,053
IF PALLIN GAVE YOU THIS JOB
LEANING ON CUMMINGS,

380
00:16:26,087 --> 00:16:28,422
WOULD YOU SAY HE'S GIVING YOU
A GOOD ASSIGNMENT?

381
00:16:28,455 --> 00:16:30,157
- OH, DON'T SUCK, HONEY.
- I'D SAY THAT HE WAS

382
00:16:30,190 --> 00:16:33,693
QUIETLY SHIPPING YOU
OUT OF THE WAY.

383
00:16:33,727 --> 00:16:35,528
WELL, I'LL GET 'EM BOTH.
DEANEY AND CUMMINGS.

384
00:16:35,562 --> 00:16:38,232
NO WAY.
YOU DON'T GET NEITHER.

385
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:39,900
THAT'S WHAT PALLIN THINKS,
RIGHT?

386
00:16:39,933 --> 00:16:42,135
- RIGHT.
- WRONG.

387
00:16:42,168 --> 00:16:44,638
EXCUSE ME,
I DON'T FEEL GOOD AT ALL.

388
00:16:46,607 --> 00:16:48,475
HEY, MAN, THANKS
FOR DRIVING ME TO MY CAR.

389
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:51,478
NICE TO HAVE IT PRE-PARKED
AT THE STAKEOUT, SEE YOU!

390
00:16:51,512 --> 00:16:52,980
♪ CHICO, DON'T BE DISCOURAGED ♪

391
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:54,213
♪ THE MAN DON'T--

392
00:16:54,247 --> 00:16:56,083
WHOA! DON'T DO THAT.

393
00:17:06,893 --> 00:17:08,362
MITCHELL!

394
00:17:08,395 --> 00:17:10,230
ANDY CAPP?

395
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:11,798
BOY, FLO'S REALLY
GONNA BE MAD.

396
00:17:11,832 --> 00:17:13,933
I'M DRUNK AGAIN.

397
00:17:13,967 --> 00:17:17,170
[CROW PANTS, WHEEZES]

398
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:19,640
- CUMMINGS!
- STOP, OR MY HEART'LL EXPLODE!

399
00:17:19,673 --> 00:17:22,242
CUMMINGS! MITCHELL?
POLICE DEPARTMENT.

400
00:17:22,275 --> 00:17:24,343
BENEFIT'S NOT DUE
TILL JANUARY, SON.

401
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:26,078
- UH, MR. CUMMINGS--
- MAKE AN APPOINTMENT, SON.

402
00:17:26,112 --> 00:17:27,247
HAVE YOUR CHIEF
GIVE ME A RING.

403
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,815
MR. CUMMINGS.

404
00:17:28,848 --> 00:17:30,783
NO SALESMEN
AT THIS ENTRANCE.

405
00:17:30,817 --> 00:17:33,453
BUT I'M NOT A SALESMAN,
I'M THE CHUBBY BLUE LINE!

406
00:17:35,688 --> 00:17:38,958
AS AN ACTOR, MERLIN OLSEN
HADN'T FOUND HIS INSTRUMENT YET.

407
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,897
[SERVO PANTS, WHEEZES]

408
00:17:50,937 --> 00:17:53,440
[AS JERRY LEWIS]
WHA-HO! THE THING
WITH THE DEAL-O.

409
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:58,045
WELL, THINK THERE'S
A POTATO CAKE

410
00:17:58,078 --> 00:17:59,445
IN HERE OR SOMETHING.

411
00:17:59,478 --> 00:18:02,248
HE SEEMS DOWN. I'LL SEND HIM
A PICK-ME-UP BOUQUET.

412
00:18:05,318 --> 00:18:07,553
SOMEWHERE,
AN INDIAN IS CRYING.

413
00:18:09,857 --> 00:18:12,425
OH, I'M GONNA CALL
LADYBIRD JOHNSON.

414
00:18:15,695 --> 00:18:17,998
[SNORES]

415
00:18:18,032 --> 00:18:19,398
FLUFFERNUTTER! OH.

416
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:21,202
ALL RIGHT, NOW,
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

417
00:18:21,235 --> 00:18:22,502
WELL, I GOT SOME QUESTIONS.

418
00:18:22,535 --> 00:18:23,970
- NO QUESTIONS.
- NOW, WHAT DO YOU KNOW

419
00:18:24,003 --> 00:18:25,272
ABOUT A MAN NAMED MISTRETTA

420
00:18:25,305 --> 00:18:27,273
AND SOME HEROIN HIJACK
DOWN IN MEXICO?

421
00:18:27,307 --> 00:18:29,843
- HEROIN?
- YEAH. CUERNAVACA, MEXICO.

422
00:18:29,877 --> 00:18:31,077
ABOUT A KILO.
YOU KNOW,

423
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,847
A TRUCK, AMBUSHED,
HIJACKED, YOU KNOW.

424
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,815
- LOOK, MITCHELL--
- I'M KING HUSSEIN.

425
00:18:34,848 --> 00:18:36,583
THIS IS LOS ANGELES,
CALIFORNIA.

426
00:18:36,617 --> 00:18:38,085
I DON'T KNOW
ANYTHING ABOUT HEROIN.

427
00:18:38,118 --> 00:18:40,020
NOW, SOMEBODY'S
GOT HIS WIRES CROSSED.

428
00:18:40,053 --> 00:18:42,957
- OH.
- WE'RE NOT IN NEW YORK?

429
00:18:42,990 --> 00:18:44,825
WELL, I'VE BEEN TOLD
TO WATCH YOU, MR. CUMMINGS.

430
00:18:44,858 --> 00:18:46,793
SO I GUESS THAT'S
WHAT I'M GONNA DO.

431
00:18:46,827 --> 00:18:48,862
CAN I GIVE YOU
SOME ADVICE, THEN?

432
00:18:48,895 --> 00:18:50,297
WELL, YES SIR.

433
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,698
WATCH OUT FOR FALLING ROCKS.

434
00:18:52,732 --> 00:18:54,133
UH, OKAY. SAY, YOU

435
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:57,803
GOT ANY BURGERS
OR SOMETHING IN THERE?

436
00:18:57,837 --> 00:19:00,440
MAN, I'M CONSTANTLY
CONFUSED.

437
00:19:01,975 --> 00:19:03,877
WATCH OUT FOR
FALLING ROCKS, HUH?

438
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:06,045
HUH. STUPID.

439
00:19:06,078 --> 00:19:07,380
AND THAT WAS
THE MIDNIGHT EDITION

440
00:19:07,413 --> 00:19:09,650
OF THE NEWS, ON K.K.R.O.

441
00:19:09,683 --> 00:19:12,185
[CROW] HEY, "KRO" RADIO.

442
00:19:12,218 --> 00:19:14,020
GOOD NIGHT, JOHN BOY.

443
00:19:16,457 --> 00:19:19,660
FALLING ROCKS,
I JUST DON'T GET IT.

444
00:19:19,693 --> 00:19:23,530
LIGHTS. YOUR LIGHTS!

445
00:19:23,563 --> 00:19:26,500
I'LL MISS HIM.

446
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:29,603
WELL, ALMOST TIME
FOR SILK STALKINGS.

447
00:19:31,572 --> 00:19:34,073
HI, LARRY, I LOVE YOUR SHOW.

448
00:19:34,107 --> 00:19:36,810
CUMMINGS, GIVE ME MISTRETTA.

449
00:19:38,878 --> 00:19:40,880
MISTRETTA, WHAT'S THIS
ABOUT A LOAD OF MERCHANDISE

450
00:19:40,913 --> 00:19:42,215
I'M SUPPOSED TO BE
SHIPPING IN?

451
00:19:42,248 --> 00:19:43,617
- [SERVO MUTTERS]
- I GOT COPS SITTING ON ME.

452
00:19:43,650 --> 00:19:45,118
THEY TELL ME THIS,
AND I DON'T KNOW IT.

453
00:19:45,152 --> 00:19:48,022
[SERVO MUTTERS]

454
00:19:48,055 --> 00:19:49,757
- YOU WHAT?
- YOU'RE WEARING WHAT?

455
00:19:49,790 --> 00:19:50,957
IS IT SHEER?

456
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:54,060
GET OVER HERE,
AND DON'T ARGUE WITH ME.

457
00:19:54,093 --> 00:19:55,695
NOT THAT QUICKLY.

458
00:19:55,728 --> 00:19:59,365
[BOTS] OOH.

459
00:19:59,398 --> 00:20:01,468
OH, NOSE CANDY.

460
00:20:01,502 --> 00:20:03,737
JUST DRIVE AROUND THE BLOCK.

461
00:20:03,770 --> 00:20:06,873
HI, DAD.

462
00:20:06,907 --> 00:20:10,577
LOVE YOU IN
THE TAKING OF PELHAM 123.

463
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:11,712
HEY, YOU WANT THE RADIO?

464
00:20:11,745 --> 00:20:13,780
KING BISCUIT
FLOUR HOUR IS ON.

465
00:20:13,813 --> 00:20:16,883
WHAT'S BUGGING YOU?

466
00:20:16,917 --> 00:20:18,385
LISTEN, YOU PUNK.
FOR THE FUTURE,

467
00:20:18,418 --> 00:20:19,787
NEXT TIME YOU START SOMETHING,

468
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:22,322
YOU TELL ME BEFORE YOU START IT,
NOT AFTERWARDS.

469
00:20:22,355 --> 00:20:23,823
SHIP THE DOPE
SOMEPLACE ELSE.

470
00:20:23,857 --> 00:20:25,225
I GOT THIS COP ON MY TAIL.

471
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:26,927
IT'S JUST THAT MITCHELL GUY.

472
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:29,128
IT'S ON THE WATER,
CUMMINGS.

473
00:20:29,162 --> 00:20:30,663
- WHAT'S ON THE WATER?
- SMOKE.

474
00:20:30,697 --> 00:20:32,598
THE MERCHANDISE.

475
00:20:32,632 --> 00:20:35,035
WELL, IT'S NOT COMING
THROUGH MY FACILITIES.

476
00:20:35,068 --> 00:20:36,837
IT CAN'T GO NOWHERE ELSE.

477
00:20:36,870 --> 00:20:39,172
- WHY NOT?
- WHY NOT?

478
00:20:39,205 --> 00:20:41,140
BECAUSE THAT'S THE WAY
MR. GALLANO WANTS IT.

479
00:20:41,173 --> 00:20:42,508
♪ UH-HUH UH-HUH ♪

480
00:20:42,542 --> 00:20:44,310
AND BECAUSE MAYBE
IT'S IN SAN PEDRO

481
00:20:44,343 --> 00:20:46,012
NOW OR TOMORROW.

482
00:20:46,045 --> 00:20:48,315
- IT'S TOO LATE, CUMMINGS.
- HEY, LOOK, AN APPLEBEE'S.

483
00:20:48,348 --> 00:20:50,350
WELL, IF IT COMES
THROUGH SAN PEDRO,

484
00:20:50,383 --> 00:20:52,585
I'M NOT GONNA TOUCH IT.

485
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:53,920
YOU UNDERSTAND,
I WILL NOT TOUCH IT.

486
00:20:53,953 --> 00:20:55,522
HAH-- OH.

487
00:20:55,555 --> 00:20:58,225
CUMMINGS, YOU ARE NOT IN
A POSITION TO SAY SUCH THINGS.

488
00:20:58,258 --> 00:20:59,525
YOU CAN'T HANDLE THE TRUTH.

489
00:20:59,558 --> 00:21:02,195
BEFORE YOU OPEN
YOUR BIG MOUTH AGAIN,

490
00:21:02,228 --> 00:21:04,397
YOU'D BETTER
THINK OF MR. GALLANO.

491
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:05,732
YOU KNOW, THIS MAY
BE THE WRONG RIDE.

492
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:08,702
ARE YOU STEVE?

493
00:21:08,735 --> 00:21:10,670
I SAY IT, BOY,
BECAUSE I MEAN IT.

494
00:21:10,703 --> 00:21:13,740
LET'S GO DO THAT LITTLE
ADDITION WE WERE THINKING OF.

495
00:21:28,088 --> 00:21:30,157
OKAY, NOW, YOU GUYS,
WE GOT ABOUT THREE MINUTES

496
00:21:30,190 --> 00:21:31,592
BEFORE WE'RE DUE BACK
IN THE THEATER.

497
00:21:31,625 --> 00:21:33,793
SO WE GOTTA DO THIS
OUTWARD BOUND EXPERIENCE

498
00:21:33,827 --> 00:21:35,062
TOOT-SWEET, OKAY?

499
00:21:35,095 --> 00:21:36,663
- SERVO, YOU KNOW THE DRILL.
- ROGER.

500
00:21:36,697 --> 00:21:38,632
JOEL LOWERS US INTO
THE REFUSE TRENCH,

501
00:21:38,665 --> 00:21:40,367
AND WE HAVE BUT 90 SECONDS

502
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,735
TO FIELD-STRIP OURSELVES

503
00:21:41,768 --> 00:21:43,137
AND RE-ASSEMBLE OURSELVES

504
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:45,605
WHILE DANGLING BY OUR PO-PO'S
IN THE STINKY DARKNESS.

505
00:21:45,638 --> 00:21:47,707
- READY.
- MM-HMM. COMMANDO CROW,
YOU READY?

506
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:49,642
- [CROW GROWLS]
- CROW'S FROSTY.

507
00:21:49,675 --> 00:21:51,210
YOU KIDS BE CAREFUL.

508
00:21:51,243 --> 00:21:53,280
DON'T WORRY, MA'AM,
WE'LL BRING 'EM BACK ALIVE.

509
00:21:53,313 --> 00:21:54,347
LET'S GO.

510
00:21:54,380 --> 00:21:55,982
♪ ACTION JACKSON ♪

511
00:21:56,015 --> 00:21:58,918
- ♪ IS MY NAME ♪
- BYE. BYE.

512
00:21:58,952 --> 00:22:01,287
SEE YOU LATER.

513
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:03,490
OH. OH.

514
00:22:03,523 --> 00:22:05,625
UH, THE LIGHT-- UH, GUYS?

515
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:07,060
GUYS?

516
00:22:07,093 --> 00:22:08,328
UH, HEY, THE...

517
00:22:08,362 --> 00:22:11,130
EVIL UNDERPANTS. HEY, GUYS?

518
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:13,967
UH, UH... HELLO, SIRS?

519
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:16,102
DON'T WORRY, DOCTOR.
I KNEW WHEN WE BROUGHT HIM ON

520
00:22:16,135 --> 00:22:18,505
WE'D HAVE TO ELIMINATE HIM.
THAT'S HALF THE FUN.

521
00:22:18,538 --> 00:22:20,340
YES, FRANK, BUT HOW?

522
00:22:20,373 --> 00:22:22,642
THESE THINGS MUST
BE DONE DELICATELY.

523
00:22:22,675 --> 00:22:24,878
[CACKLES]

524
00:22:29,582 --> 00:22:31,050
AFTER ALL, HE KNEW GOING IN

525
00:22:31,083 --> 00:22:33,720
THAT THIS WAS ONLY
A TEMPORARY SITUATION.

526
00:22:33,753 --> 00:22:35,755
YES, AND NOW I WANT THIS

527
00:22:35,788 --> 00:22:37,857
TEMPORARY SITUATION
TAKEN CARE OF.

528
00:22:37,890 --> 00:22:39,625
PERMANENTLY.

529
00:22:39,658 --> 00:22:43,230
[BOTH CACKLE]

530
00:22:43,263 --> 00:22:45,398
ARE WE TALKING ABOUT
THE SAME THING?

531
00:22:48,535 --> 00:22:51,638
HE'S BEEN A CANKER SORE
ON MY GUMLINE FOR TOO LONG.

532
00:22:51,672 --> 00:22:54,775
THE WAY HE STRUTS AROUND
LIKE HE OWNS THE PLACE - BAH!

533
00:22:54,808 --> 00:22:58,212
LET'S USE METHOD
NUMBER 53, HMM?

534
00:22:58,245 --> 00:23:01,615
YES, ELEGANT. PAINFUL.

535
00:23:01,648 --> 00:23:03,283
AND LEAVES NOTHING BEHIND

536
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:04,918
BUT THE GREAT SMELL OF BRUT.

537
00:23:04,952 --> 00:23:06,252
[CACKLES]

538
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:09,255
[CACKLES]

539
00:23:12,325 --> 00:23:14,760
[BOTH CACKLE]

540
00:23:14,793 --> 00:23:15,962
LET'S DO IT NOW!

541
00:23:15,995 --> 00:23:17,930
NO, NO, PATIENCE,
MY LITTLE HENCHMAN.

542
00:23:17,963 --> 00:23:20,200
LET'S WAIT UNTIL
AFTER THE EXPERIMENT.

543
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,768
YES, BRILLIANT,
MAKE HIM WORK FOR IT.

544
00:23:21,802 --> 00:23:23,370
AND THEN?
AND THEN...

545
00:23:23,403 --> 00:23:26,607
OUR LITTLE BE-JUMPSUITED FOOL
WILL BE HISTORY!

546
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:29,810
[BOTH CACKLE]

547
00:23:29,843 --> 00:23:31,678
GET BACK TO WORK!

548
00:23:31,712 --> 00:23:35,682
JUMPSUIT! FOOL!
THEY'RE GOING TO KILL JOEL!

549
00:23:35,715 --> 00:23:37,817
THEY'RE GOING TO KILL JOEL!
THEY'RE GOING TO KILL JOEL!

550
00:23:37,850 --> 00:23:39,452
HELP! WHAT DO I DO?
WHAT DO I DO?

551
00:23:39,485 --> 00:23:41,488
I GOTTA GET HIM OUT OF HERE.
THEY'RE GONNA KILL HIM.

552
00:23:41,522 --> 00:23:43,190
HELP!

553
00:23:43,223 --> 00:23:45,192
EASY, GIRL. TAKE IT EASY.

554
00:23:45,225 --> 00:23:47,060
CALM DOWN.
BREATHE THROUGH YOUR NOSE.

555
00:23:47,093 --> 00:23:48,762
OH, HERE WE GO.

556
00:23:48,795 --> 00:23:50,563
THAT DOES IT. EASY DOES IT.

557
00:23:50,597 --> 00:23:53,167
OKAY, OKAY, OKAY.

558
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,935
OKAY. OKAY.

559
00:23:55,968 --> 00:23:57,570
OKAY.

560
00:23:57,603 --> 00:23:59,272
THEY'RE GOING TO KILL JOEL!!!

561
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:01,407
AAH!

562
00:24:08,948 --> 00:24:10,817
- THAT WAS FUN.
- GOOD JOB.

563
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:13,653
LOG THIS REPORT. TIME...

564
00:24:13,687 --> 00:24:17,423
- MITCHELL, HELLO?
- 2417 HOURS.

565
00:24:17,457 --> 00:24:19,625
I'M AT THE DEANEY RESIDENCE.

566
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:21,293
I'M PUTTING MY GUN
IN THE GLOVE COMPARTMENT

567
00:24:21,327 --> 00:24:23,363
- AND LOCKING IT.
- I JUST HAD A FRENCH DIP.

568
00:24:23,397 --> 00:24:25,665
55, WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

569
00:24:25,698 --> 00:24:27,733
55, REPEAT?

570
00:24:30,203 --> 00:24:31,572
IF I'M SHOT IN THE NEXT
COUPLE OF HOURS,

571
00:24:31,605 --> 00:24:33,707
I WAS UNARMED
WHEN IT HAPPENED.

572
00:24:33,740 --> 00:24:36,408
LOG IT, 55 OUT.

573
00:24:36,442 --> 00:24:37,877
MAN, SPEAKING OF LOGGIN' IT,

574
00:24:37,910 --> 00:24:39,947
I'D BETTER FIND
A BUSH AROUND HERE.

575
00:24:42,382 --> 00:24:44,550
MITCHELL!

576
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:46,018
MITCHELL! MITCHELL!

577
00:24:46,052 --> 00:24:47,487
MITCHELL...

578
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,522
MITCHELL.

579
00:24:48,555 --> 00:24:50,723
MITCHELL, MITCHELL.

580
00:25:02,302 --> 00:25:03,537
HEY, HI, MITCHELL!

581
00:25:03,570 --> 00:25:04,870
GO ABOUT YOUR BUSINESS.

582
00:25:04,903 --> 00:25:06,338
HONK-HONK, HEY, MITCHELL!

583
00:25:06,372 --> 00:25:08,742
SHH!

584
00:25:08,775 --> 00:25:11,210
[BOTS MIMIC DOG HOWLS]

585
00:25:14,413 --> 00:25:18,285
UH, HONEY, MITCHELL'S HERE.

586
00:25:18,318 --> 00:25:21,788
OH, WHOA, IS THAT A BEER?

587
00:25:21,822 --> 00:25:23,657
PAIN IN MY CHEST,
MY HAND'S TINGLING.

588
00:25:23,690 --> 00:25:24,992
[SERVO GRUNTS]

589
00:25:25,025 --> 00:25:26,458
OH SHOOT, A DOOR.

590
00:25:26,492 --> 00:25:29,362
I DIDN'T PLAN ON THIS.

591
00:25:29,395 --> 00:25:30,630
OH MAN, I LOVE THIS.

592
00:25:30,663 --> 00:25:32,832
I GOT SOAP,
I GOT DOG POOPIE.

593
00:25:32,865 --> 00:25:34,167
THIS WEEK'S PRACTICAL JOKE.

594
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:36,068
THE VICTIM? JOHN SAXON.

595
00:25:41,607 --> 00:25:45,378
[SERVO PANTS, WHEEZES]

596
00:25:45,412 --> 00:25:46,980
MAN, IF I COULD JUST
SIT ON A LAWN CHAIR

597
00:25:47,013 --> 00:25:48,782
FOR FIVE MINUTES.
THAT'S ALL I NEED.

598
00:25:48,815 --> 00:25:51,017
BOY, WHAT A CLEAN GARAGE.
NO BIKES, SLEDS,

599
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:53,787
OR OIL SPOTS.

600
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:56,255
DO YOU KNOW WHO DID IT?
HAVE YOU FIGURED IT OUT YET?

601
00:25:59,258 --> 00:26:01,527
[SERVO WHISTLES SCORE]

602
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,597
UH, MITCHELL,
DO YOU WANNA COME IN?

603
00:26:04,630 --> 00:26:05,965
[SERVO HUMS SCORE]

604
00:26:05,998 --> 00:26:09,035
[CROW MIMICS DOG WHINING]

605
00:26:12,205 --> 00:26:14,140
[MIMICS DOG PANTING]

606
00:26:19,345 --> 00:26:21,013
[AS SCHWARZENEGGER]
LIQUID METAL.

607
00:26:21,047 --> 00:26:22,348
REYNOLDS WRAP.

608
00:26:22,382 --> 00:26:24,883
KEEPS FRESHNESS IN.
CAN'T KEEP MITCHELL OUT.

609
00:26:28,053 --> 00:26:31,290
♪ OOH, YOU'RE A HOLIDAY ♪

610
00:26:34,693 --> 00:26:38,332
MM, WELL, THAT WAS MY PLAN.

611
00:26:38,365 --> 00:26:41,533
I SMELL CRAB DIP.

612
00:26:41,567 --> 00:26:44,670
MELMAC? WHY WOULD HE BE
COLLECTING MELMAC?

613
00:26:45,738 --> 00:26:48,508
AN EMPTY PLATE
BREAKS MY HEART.

614
00:26:48,542 --> 00:26:50,843
KEITH HARING WAS HERE.

615
00:26:55,248 --> 00:26:59,018
TRY FOR A QUICK
40 WINKS HERE.

616
00:26:59,052 --> 00:27:02,955
THAT MEANS THE VICTIM
WAS JACK VALENTI!

617
00:27:02,988 --> 00:27:05,692
WHAT ARE YOU DOING,
MITCHELL?

618
00:27:11,798 --> 00:27:14,300
WHY ARE THEY PLAYING
"NADIA'S THEME"?

619
00:27:14,333 --> 00:27:16,102
THEY'RE YOUNG AND RESTLESS.

620
00:27:19,338 --> 00:27:21,440
WELL, THAT'S A REACH.

621
00:27:23,342 --> 00:27:24,810
JUST BROWSIN'.

622
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:26,345
- [GUNSHOT]
- [JOEL SHOUTS]

623
00:27:26,378 --> 00:27:27,980
[SERVO GASPS]

624
00:27:28,013 --> 00:27:29,615
♪ MITCHELL ♪

625
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,785
- ♪ MITCHELL ♪
- ♪ KEEP YOUR EYE... ♪

626
00:27:31,818 --> 00:27:33,218
♪ ON THE SAMMICH ♪

627
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:34,787
- ♪ MITCHELL ♪
- ♪ HEART'S POUNDING ♪

628
00:27:34,820 --> 00:27:36,355
- ♪ MITCHELL ♪
- ♪ VEINS CLOGGIN' ♪

629
00:27:36,388 --> 00:27:38,925
- ♪ MITCHELL! ♪
- ♪ WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA ♪

630
00:27:42,362 --> 00:27:44,330
OH MAN, THIS
IS HARD TO DO AFTER

631
00:27:44,363 --> 00:27:46,498
SIX SOUR CREAM BURRITOS.

632
00:27:46,532 --> 00:27:48,033
[SERVO PANTS]

633
00:27:51,337 --> 00:27:55,275
THE CLOISTERED LIFE
IS NOT FOR ME.

634
00:27:55,308 --> 00:27:58,745
- HUH?
- WHAT?

635
00:27:58,778 --> 00:28:00,313
WOULD YOU GIVE ME THAT?

636
00:28:00,347 --> 00:28:01,882
IT'S FISH!

637
00:28:01,915 --> 00:28:04,683
- TYZACK?
- WE CAN'T NAME A SERIES
AFTER YOU, SORRY.

638
00:28:04,717 --> 00:28:05,918
SEE YOU TOMORROW.

639
00:28:05,952 --> 00:28:07,153
HEY, HE LOOKS LIKE A GUY

640
00:28:07,187 --> 00:28:09,422
FROM A DAVID BERG CARTOON.

641
00:28:09,455 --> 00:28:11,123
WHAT IN THE HELL
ARE YOU UP TO?

642
00:28:11,157 --> 00:28:12,992
- DEANEY.
- AND WHAT'D I TELL YOU?

643
00:28:13,025 --> 00:28:14,360
I TOLD YOU TO FORGET DEANEY.

644
00:28:14,393 --> 00:28:15,695
DO YOU KNOW WHO HE IS?

645
00:28:15,728 --> 00:28:17,663
YEAH, HE'S
A TRADE UNION LAWYER.

646
00:28:17,697 --> 00:28:19,332
AND I GAVE YOU
A DIRECT ORDER TO FORGET.

647
00:28:19,365 --> 00:28:20,667
NOW, WHY'D I GIVE YOU
THAT ORDER?

648
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:22,035
AND NONE OF THAT
"I DON'T KNOW."

649
00:28:22,068 --> 00:28:24,537
I'M GONNA TELL YOU WHY.
EVERY FEDERAL LAW VIOLATION--

650
00:28:24,570 --> 00:28:26,305
EVERY FEDERAL LAW
VIOLATION!

651
00:28:26,338 --> 00:28:28,642
--DEANEY AND HIS
TRADE UNION.

652
00:28:28,675 --> 00:28:31,243
THEY'VE BEEN WORKING ON
THIS THING FOR OVER TWO YEARS.

653
00:28:31,277 --> 00:28:33,112
NOW, IN THE MEANTIME,
YOU GET BACK OUT THERE

654
00:28:33,145 --> 00:28:34,680
ON CUMMINGS,
AND YOU STAY WITH HIM.

655
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:37,450
DEANEY IS FBI PROPERTY.

656
00:28:38,985 --> 00:28:41,087
RIGHT, BOSS.

657
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:42,422
YEAH, AND FIND MY UPPER LIP

658
00:28:42,455 --> 00:28:45,758
WHILE YOU'RE OUT THERE.

659
00:28:45,792 --> 00:28:49,062
A LITTLE PEEK
INTO MITCHELL'S LIFE.

660
00:28:49,095 --> 00:28:50,797
[DOORBELL RINGS]

661
00:28:50,830 --> 00:28:52,898
DAMN, IT'S ALMOST
TIME FOR BOZO.

662
00:28:57,137 --> 00:28:58,938
YEAH, GO FOR THE GUSTO,
MITCHELL.

663
00:28:58,972 --> 00:29:00,740
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

664
00:29:03,843 --> 00:29:05,445
IS THAT YOU, MA?

665
00:29:08,982 --> 00:29:10,317
- HELLO.
- BO DEREK!

666
00:29:10,350 --> 00:29:12,052
- HI.
- I'M YOUR NEW FRIEND.

667
00:29:12,085 --> 00:29:13,920
WELL, LINDA EVANS, ACTUALLY.

668
00:29:13,953 --> 00:29:17,323
- MM-HMM.
- I'M SELLING YANNI TAPES.

669
00:29:17,357 --> 00:29:20,193
UH, JUST GOTTA ADJUST
MY ROSCOE HERE.

670
00:29:23,195 --> 00:29:25,732
COME ON IN, FRIEND.

671
00:29:25,765 --> 00:29:26,933
WHERE'S JOHN DEREK?

672
00:29:26,967 --> 00:29:28,635
SHOULDN'T WE SET
ANOTHER PLACE FOR HIM?

673
00:29:28,668 --> 00:29:31,203
[SERVO SNIFFS]
SO DO YOU WORK AT A PETTING ZOO?

674
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:38,110
UNCLE FESTER?

675
00:29:42,048 --> 00:29:43,148
SOMETHING TO DRINK?

676
00:29:43,182 --> 00:29:46,485
- WHAT DO YOU HAVE?
- BEER AND VODKA.

677
00:29:46,518 --> 00:29:48,487
BEER.

678
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:49,955
YOU LIKE 'EM HALF-EMPTY?

679
00:29:49,988 --> 00:29:52,225
SOME OF 'EM GOT
CIGARETTES IN 'EM.

680
00:29:54,993 --> 00:29:58,932
THIS IS SO EMBARRASSING.
HE'S PLAYING A KITARO ALBUM.

681
00:29:58,965 --> 00:30:00,300
UH, SORRY ABOUT THE PORN.

682
00:30:00,333 --> 00:30:02,268
THERE'S A KILGORE TROUT
PIECE IN THERE.

683
00:30:05,905 --> 00:30:08,407
I WOULDN'T SIT THERE.
OTHER SIDE, PLEASE.

684
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:10,410
UH, THERE'S SOME CHIPS
UNDER THE CUSHION.

685
00:30:10,443 --> 00:30:12,345
HELP YOURSELF.

686
00:30:12,378 --> 00:30:14,613
DON'T YOU THINK I'M
AS GOOD AS ANYTHING HERE?

687
00:30:14,647 --> 00:30:17,183
WELL, UH, YOU GOT
AN AIRBRUSH ON YOU?

688
00:30:20,420 --> 00:30:23,288
YOU'VE GOT ME WRONG.
I'D LIKE A GLASS.

689
00:30:23,322 --> 00:30:25,625
OKAY, YOUR MAJESTY.

690
00:30:25,658 --> 00:30:27,960
GOT THESE AT CONOCO.
THEY GOT DICK BUTKUS ON 'EM.

691
00:30:31,463 --> 00:30:33,767
EW.

692
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:36,468
- YOU WANT A TOWEL?
- NO, I'LL USE THE CURTAINS.

693
00:30:36,502 --> 00:30:40,407
- SHOULD I LICK IT OFF?
- ABSOLUTELY NOT!

694
00:30:43,508 --> 00:30:44,743
WELL, SHE WAS GONNA
SMELL LIKE BEER

695
00:30:44,777 --> 00:30:47,713
SOONER OR LATER.

696
00:30:47,747 --> 00:30:50,483
SORRY, THE BEER GOT
A LITTLE EXCITED.

697
00:30:50,517 --> 00:30:52,418
THAT'S OKAY,
WE CAN JUST CUDDLE.

698
00:30:52,452 --> 00:30:53,887
WHAT?!

699
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,722
- OH.
- OH, JEEZ.

700
00:30:58,390 --> 00:31:00,560
SORRY, I'M REALLY
UNAPPEALING.

701
00:31:02,595 --> 00:31:05,898
SO, MORE BEER?

702
00:31:05,932 --> 00:31:07,667
[SERVO SIGHS]

703
00:31:14,573 --> 00:31:17,143
IT'S BUGSY MALONE.

704
00:31:17,177 --> 00:31:20,012
THAT'S GREAT.

705
00:31:20,045 --> 00:31:23,182
- [DOOR SLAMS]
- WHAT WAS THAT?

706
00:31:23,215 --> 00:31:26,652
OH.

707
00:31:26,685 --> 00:31:28,655
OH, THEY'RE TAKING THE BOYS
TO PLAY GROUP.

708
00:31:28,688 --> 00:31:30,923
- OH.
- HUH.

709
00:31:30,957 --> 00:31:33,660
NICE CAP.

710
00:31:33,693 --> 00:31:35,060
♪ MOBSTERS LAUGHIN' ♪

711
00:31:35,093 --> 00:31:36,462
♪ REALLY SMILIN' ♪

712
00:31:36,495 --> 00:31:39,132
♪ A MAN SELLING HEROIN ♪

713
00:31:39,165 --> 00:31:41,867
UH, THE SPOTTED CUCKOO BIRD
IS FLYING BACKWARDS.

714
00:31:41,900 --> 00:31:45,338
IT'S A COLD DAY
FOR PONTOONING.

715
00:31:45,372 --> 00:31:48,273
- HELLO, MR. GALLANO.
- I'M NOT RAPPAPORT.

716
00:31:48,307 --> 00:31:50,677
LAST NIGHT,
I HAD TO COME TO MY HOME.

717
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:52,912
SALVADORE MISTRETTA,
MY COUSIN--

718
00:31:52,945 --> 00:31:54,713
BECAUSE I'M ITALIAN,
YOU KNOW.

719
00:31:54,747 --> 00:31:56,448
- --COMPLAINTS AGAINST YOU.
- HE'S A PUNK.

720
00:31:56,482 --> 00:31:59,552
DID I TELL YOU I'M ITALIAN?
LET ME RESTATE THAT.

721
00:31:59,585 --> 00:32:02,622
WHO CONVINCED YOU
TO FINANCE THAT HIJACK?

722
00:32:02,655 --> 00:32:04,657
IF YOU WANT DRUGS,
YOU CAN GROW 'EM.

723
00:32:04,690 --> 00:32:06,092
YOU CAN BUY 'EM, BUT--

724
00:32:06,125 --> 00:32:07,560
HEY, WHERE'S RUTH BUZZI?

725
00:32:07,593 --> 00:32:09,328
--IT'S GREEDY.

726
00:32:09,362 --> 00:32:11,063
MAY I REMIND YOU
OF SOMETHING?

727
00:32:11,097 --> 00:32:13,032
- I'M-A FROM ITALY.
- SURE.

728
00:32:13,065 --> 00:32:15,602
YOU KNOW AUGUST, 1963?

729
00:32:15,635 --> 00:32:19,038
YOU, ME, AND SOME OTHERS,
WE HAD A VERY FINE MEETING.

730
00:32:19,072 --> 00:32:21,073
HE WAS HASTILY PUT TOGETHER,
WASN'T HE?

731
00:32:21,107 --> 00:32:24,010
IN WHICH WE ALLOWED YOU
INFLUENCE IN THIS AREA.

732
00:32:24,043 --> 00:32:25,912
IN EXCHANGE FOR
CERTAIN ASSIGNMENTS

733
00:32:25,945 --> 00:32:28,647
- TO BE HANDLED BY YOU.
- SO?

734
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,517
THAT WAS VERY GENEROUS, YES?

735
00:32:30,550 --> 00:32:32,852
- OUI.
- FAIR ENOUGH.

736
00:32:32,885 --> 00:32:35,888
- NOW, IT'S YOUR TURN.
- ♪ TO BE WHAT YOU CAN BE ♪

737
00:32:35,922 --> 00:32:37,723
--TAKE DELIVERY
OF SALVADORE'S SHIPMENTS

738
00:32:37,757 --> 00:32:39,858
THROUGH YOUR CONTACTS
AT THE PORT, OKAY?

739
00:32:39,892 --> 00:32:41,760
I AM NOT BRINGING
THAT SHIPMENT IN,

740
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:43,262
AND THAT IS FINAL.

741
00:32:43,295 --> 00:32:46,365
♪ DOODLE-OODLE-OOP! ♪
THE SHIPMENT'S IN.

742
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:50,268
WELP, TIME FOR
MY STEP-AEROBICS CLASS.

743
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:52,105
HEY, BOSS,
YOU REALLY DID GREAT.

744
00:32:52,138 --> 00:32:54,040
YOUR PERSONAL SKILLS
ARE SOMETHING.

745
00:32:54,073 --> 00:32:56,808
HOLD IT IN... HOLD IT IN...

746
00:32:56,842 --> 00:32:59,912
I'M ALMOST ANTHONY QUINN.

747
00:32:59,945 --> 00:33:02,482
WAS MERLIN EVER IN
THE DAVE CLARK FIVE?

748
00:33:05,985 --> 00:33:08,653
IT WAS A BIG TIME,
WHEN BIG MEN DROVE NOTHING BUT

749
00:33:08,687 --> 00:33:10,823
HUGE FORD CARS!

750
00:33:14,627 --> 00:33:18,263
- SEE?
- HMM.

751
00:33:18,297 --> 00:33:20,132
- [HONKS HORN]
- HONEY, I'M HOME!

752
00:33:20,165 --> 00:33:23,770
HAD THAT MEETING
WITH THE GANGSTER.

753
00:33:23,803 --> 00:33:25,838
MITCHELL IS ONE
OF THE GREAT FOLLOWERS.

754
00:33:28,307 --> 00:33:30,410
MITCHELL, I'VE MADE
A DECISION ABOUT YOU.

755
00:33:30,443 --> 00:33:32,778
I GOT A LOT OF THINGS
ON MY MIND AT THE MOMENT.

756
00:33:32,812 --> 00:33:34,313
NOW, YOU'RE GETTING
TOO HEAVY TO CARRY.

757
00:33:34,347 --> 00:33:36,115
I'M SORRY YOU FEEL THAT WAY,
MR. CUMMINGS.

758
00:33:36,148 --> 00:33:37,583
- HE'S HEAVY.
- I DO.

759
00:33:37,617 --> 00:33:39,085
NOW, YOU GONNA
GET LOST OR NOT?

760
00:33:39,118 --> 00:33:40,820
WELL, I'D LIKE TO,
BUT THERE ARE SOME QUESTIONS--

761
00:33:40,853 --> 00:33:42,855
- YOU'RE SAYING NO?
- I'M SAYING NO.

762
00:33:42,888 --> 00:33:46,592
THOUGHT I'D GIVE YOU
THE CHANCE.

763
00:33:46,625 --> 00:33:47,793
THAT WAS SWEET,
HE DIDN'T HAVE TO DO THAT.

764
00:33:47,827 --> 00:33:50,195
THANKS!

765
00:33:50,228 --> 00:33:52,865
UH, SAY, BOSS, DO YOU THINK
MITCHELL LIKES ME?

766
00:33:52,898 --> 00:33:54,800
SHUT UP AND DRIVE.

767
00:33:58,737 --> 00:33:59,938
IS YOUR FRIEND READY?

768
00:33:59,972 --> 00:34:01,907
YES, SIR. HE'S READY.

769
00:34:01,940 --> 00:34:03,675
WHO, ROSEY GRIER?

770
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:05,243
THIS IS WHAT I'LL REMEMBER

771
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:06,845
WHEN I THINK
OF THE MOVIE MITCHELL.

772
00:34:06,878 --> 00:34:10,583
AND I WILL THINK OF IT.

773
00:34:10,617 --> 00:34:13,018
OH WAIT, I LOST HIM.
OH, NO, THERE HE IS.

774
00:34:13,052 --> 00:34:16,288
MITCHELL, EVEN HIS NAME SAYS,
"IS THAT A BEER?"

775
00:34:18,123 --> 00:34:19,358
YOU KNOW,
THEY'RE EASY TO FOLLOW

776
00:34:19,392 --> 00:34:21,693
WHEN THEY USE
THEIR TURN SIGNAL.

777
00:34:21,727 --> 00:34:24,297
MAN, WHY DON'T THEY JUST
TIE THEIR BUMPERS TOGETHER?

778
00:34:24,330 --> 00:34:25,932
YOU KNOW, IT'S NOT
AN OFFICIAL CHASE SCENE

779
00:34:25,965 --> 00:34:27,300
WITHOUT THE WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA.

780
00:34:27,333 --> 00:34:28,767
YEAH.

781
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:31,703
HOT MERGING ACTION!

782
00:34:31,737 --> 00:34:34,573
♪ WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA... ♪

783
00:34:34,607 --> 00:34:36,175
OH, GOODNESS.

784
00:34:36,208 --> 00:34:37,377
THEY MERGED SUCCESSFULLY.

785
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:39,878
MY HEART WAS IN
MY THROAT THERE.

786
00:34:41,580 --> 00:34:43,348
MITCHELL.

787
00:34:43,382 --> 00:34:45,618
JEEZ, THESE GUYS
COULDN'T SHAKE A TROLLEY.

788
00:34:45,652 --> 00:34:47,420
THIS MAKES DRIVING MISS DAISY

789
00:34:47,453 --> 00:34:50,155
LOOK LIKE BULLITT.

790
00:34:50,188 --> 00:34:51,657
NEXT WEEK ON MITCHELL--

791
00:34:51,690 --> 00:34:55,127
THE CLOVERLEAF!

792
00:34:55,160 --> 00:34:57,897
AND, TODAY,
3M IS A VIBRANT COMPANY!

793
00:34:57,930 --> 00:34:59,265
COMBINING INNOVATION,

794
00:34:59,298 --> 00:35:00,800
EFFECTIVE RISK MANAGEMENT,

795
00:35:00,833 --> 00:35:02,268
AND MARKETING.

796
00:35:02,302 --> 00:35:05,037
3M!

797
00:35:05,070 --> 00:35:07,105
OH BOY, THEY'RE TRAVELING
AT SPEEDS OF UP TO

798
00:35:07,138 --> 00:35:09,042
25 MILES PER HOUR.

799
00:35:09,075 --> 00:35:11,677
I'VE SEEN FASTER
FUNERAL PROCESSIONS.

800
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,415
THE ONLY REALLY
EXCITING THING

801
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:18,017
IS THAT VANISHING POINT
IS BEING FILMED

802
00:35:18,050 --> 00:35:21,820
ON THE OTHER SIDE
OF THE CANYON.

803
00:35:21,853 --> 00:35:23,255
OH, THIS IS NICE

804
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:25,357
THEY'RE USING THE LIGHT ROCK
FOR THE CHASE SCENE

805
00:35:25,390 --> 00:35:27,260
- RATHER THAN THE GRUNGE SOUND.
- I LIKE THE LIGHT ROCK.

806
00:35:27,293 --> 00:35:30,597
OH, FINALLY,
THE CHASE SCENE'S PACE CAR.

807
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:31,963
YES, THE LINCOLN
CONTINENTAL.

808
00:35:31,997 --> 00:35:34,733
PERFECT FOR
OFF-ROAD EXCITEMENT.

809
00:35:36,502 --> 00:35:38,103
I CAN'T SHAKE HIM, BOSS.

810
00:35:38,137 --> 00:35:39,538
AH, HERE, I'LL LIGHTLY
TOUCH THE BRAKE

811
00:35:39,572 --> 00:35:41,273
AND THEN ACCELERATE.

812
00:35:44,443 --> 00:35:47,380
HEY, GET OUT
OF OUR CHASE SCENE.

813
00:35:47,413 --> 00:35:48,747
THE VICIOUS MUSTANG

814
00:35:48,780 --> 00:35:50,883
CULLS THE WEAK ONES
FROM THE HERD.

815
00:35:53,518 --> 00:35:54,987
HEY, YOU MITCHELL?

816
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:57,223
CAN I NOT HAVE
YOUR AUTOGRAPH?

817
00:36:04,163 --> 00:36:05,865
WELL, SO,
PASS IF YOU'RE GONNA.

818
00:36:05,898 --> 00:36:07,667
COME ON.

819
00:36:07,700 --> 00:36:09,102
EXCUSE ME, MAY I CUT IN?

820
00:36:09,135 --> 00:36:11,470
MAY I HAVE THIS CHASE?

821
00:36:11,503 --> 00:36:14,240
UH, DO YOU HAVE
ANY FACIAL EXPRESSIONS?

822
00:36:18,945 --> 00:36:20,512
HEH, THIS IS FUN.

823
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:22,147
LARRY MILLER.

824
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:24,417
WHY DOES HE KEEP DOWN-SHIFTING
WITH AN AUTOMATIC?

825
00:36:30,022 --> 00:36:31,590
KIND OF A HOT ROD BEN-HUR.

826
00:36:31,623 --> 00:36:33,993
- [CROW CHUCKLES]
- AND HIM.

827
00:36:37,128 --> 00:36:40,032
YEAH, AS A MATTER OF FACT,
I DO OWN THE ROAD.

828
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:44,637
HEY, THE HEADLIGHT
FIXED ITSELF.

829
00:36:49,042 --> 00:36:51,110
WELL, HEY-- IT'S MITCHELL!

830
00:36:57,783 --> 00:37:00,152
YOUR THING IS DRAGGING.

831
00:37:02,588 --> 00:37:05,490
- MITCHELL!
- MILLER!

832
00:37:07,993 --> 00:37:11,297
I KNOW A LITTLE
SHORTCUT DOWN-- OH.

833
00:37:11,330 --> 00:37:13,132
MITCHELL.

834
00:37:15,902 --> 00:37:18,303
UH, SHOULDN'T WE
EXCHANGE INFORMATION?

835
00:37:20,807 --> 00:37:24,143
WELL, THAT SHOOK UP
THE BEERS PRETTY BAD.

836
00:37:24,177 --> 00:37:26,178
HEY, CUT OUT
THAT ROCKFORD MUSIC.

837
00:37:26,212 --> 00:37:27,513
I'M MITCHELL!

838
00:37:27,547 --> 00:37:29,248
MITCHELL...

839
00:37:29,282 --> 00:37:31,117
HEY, IT'S A BOOZE POOL.

840
00:37:31,150 --> 00:37:33,618
I'LL HAVE A VODKA CHLORINE,
PLEASE.

841
00:37:33,652 --> 00:37:36,555
YEAH?

842
00:37:36,588 --> 00:37:37,957
- RUDY?
- TOOTIE.

843
00:37:37,990 --> 00:37:39,925
- I GOT PRESSURE.
- WHO'S PUSHING?

844
00:37:39,958 --> 00:37:41,793
- MISTRETTA.
- MISTRETTA?

845
00:37:41,827 --> 00:37:42,928
YOU CAN HANDLE HIM.

846
00:37:42,962 --> 00:37:44,563
WELL, THERE ARE PROBLEMS.

847
00:37:44,597 --> 00:37:48,567
- UNLESS, OF COURSE,
HE'S BACKED BY GALLANO.
- YOU GOT IT.

848
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:50,903
- WHAT THE HELL
ARE YOU CALLING ME FOR?
- I'M GETTING DIZZY.

849
00:37:50,937 --> 00:37:52,738
WELL, I'LL TELL YOU,
IT'S ABOUT A LITTLE DISCUSSION

850
00:37:52,772 --> 00:37:54,373
- BETWEEN ME AND MISTRETTA.
- OR GALLANO.

851
00:37:54,407 --> 00:37:56,075
--SHORT ANSWER, CUMMINGS.

852
00:37:56,108 --> 00:37:58,910
YOU'RE GONNA GET THE SAME ANSWER
OFF ANY OF THE BOYS.

853
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:00,545
- IF GALLANO'S INVOLVED--
- OR MISTRETTA.

854
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:03,682
- I DON'T WANT ANY PART OF IT.
- OR GALLANO.

855
00:38:03,715 --> 00:38:05,150
THAT WAS MISTRETTA.

856
00:38:05,183 --> 00:38:07,018
EH, THIS IS ALL GONNA
BLOW UP PRETTY SOON,

857
00:38:07,052 --> 00:38:08,353
AND WHEN IT DOES,

858
00:38:08,387 --> 00:38:09,955
WHO'VE WE GOT ON OUR SIDE?

859
00:38:09,988 --> 00:38:11,457
[ALL] GHOSTBUSTERS!

860
00:38:11,490 --> 00:38:13,992
- --HE'S STILL AROUND.
- HE'S NOT ON OUR SIDE, SIR.

861
00:38:14,025 --> 00:38:15,427
YES, HE IS.

862
00:38:15,460 --> 00:38:17,430
I'M NO GOOD TO HIM DEAD.

863
00:38:24,870 --> 00:38:27,907
O-E-P. E-O-P. E-O-E.

864
00:38:27,940 --> 00:38:30,142
UM, WORKING LIKE A DOG.

865
00:38:30,175 --> 00:38:31,543
GOT TO THINK.

866
00:38:31,577 --> 00:38:33,278
HOW TO GET JOEL
OFF THIS SHIP.

867
00:38:33,312 --> 00:38:34,813
HOW TO GET JOEL OFF.

868
00:38:34,847 --> 00:38:37,383
CHARTER FLIGHT? NO.

869
00:38:37,417 --> 00:38:39,385
HOW? HOW?

870
00:38:39,418 --> 00:38:40,787
HOW TO GET JOEL
OFF THIS SHIP?

871
00:38:40,820 --> 00:38:43,288
BUT-- AAH!

872
00:38:43,322 --> 00:38:44,723
BOY, I'M FRUSTRATED.

873
00:38:44,757 --> 00:38:46,425
WELL, BACK AT IT.

874
00:38:46,458 --> 00:38:48,160
THROW HIM? NO...

875
00:38:48,193 --> 00:38:50,562
HEY, GYPSY.
WORKING ON A PROJECT, HUH?

876
00:38:50,595 --> 00:38:52,230
HAVE YOU SEEN MY
"INSIDE THE PGA"

877
00:38:52,263 --> 00:38:53,432
AROUND HERE ANYWHERE?

878
00:38:53,465 --> 00:38:55,968
NO, JOEL, I HAVEN'T SEEN
YOUR MAGAZINE ANYWHERE.

879
00:38:56,002 --> 00:38:58,637
OH, IT'S GOT THIS GREAT ARTICLE
ON FUZZY ZOELLER.

880
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:00,740
JOEL, IF YOU WERE FACED
WITH YOUR IMMINENT DEATH

881
00:39:00,773 --> 00:39:02,842
AND HAD TO GET BACK
TO EARTH, LIKE, PRONTO,

882
00:39:02,875 --> 00:39:04,143
HOW WOULD YOU DO IT?

883
00:39:04,177 --> 00:39:06,345
OH, COME ON,
I'D NEVER LEAVE YOU.

884
00:39:06,378 --> 00:39:08,313
BUT JOEL!
YOUR IMMINENT DEATH.

885
00:39:08,347 --> 00:39:10,783
GYPSY, HONEY,
I COULD NEVER LEAVE YOU.

886
00:39:10,817 --> 00:39:12,452
IT'S ALL FOR ONE
AND ONE FOR ALL.

887
00:39:12,485 --> 00:39:15,520
- THAT'S THE ROBINSON WAY.
- OH, NO.

888
00:39:15,553 --> 00:39:17,957
FUZZY ZOELLER.
WHAT A GREAT GUY.

889
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:20,760
OH, I CAN'T TELL JOEL.

890
00:39:20,793 --> 00:39:22,662
HE WOULD NEVER LEAVE.

891
00:39:22,695 --> 00:39:25,798
I'M ALONE WITH
MY HEAVY BURDEN.

892
00:39:25,832 --> 00:39:28,733
ENNUI!

893
00:39:28,767 --> 00:39:31,203
WAIT, I'VE GOT
TOM AND CROW TO HELP ME!

894
00:39:31,237 --> 00:39:33,038
I'M SURE, IN A PINCH,
I CAN DEPEND ON THEM TO BE

895
00:39:33,072 --> 00:39:35,340
SERIOUS AND CALM
AND INTELLIGENT--

896
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:36,842
OKAY, WHAT'S NEXT?
WHAT'S NEXT?

897
00:39:36,875 --> 00:39:38,310
OKAY, HARDCASTLE AND McCORMICK.

898
00:39:38,343 --> 00:39:39,712
OKAY, RIDE!

899
00:39:39,745 --> 00:39:42,548
♪ DRIVIN' LIKE THE DEMON
THAT DRIVE YOUR DREAMS ♪

900
00:39:42,582 --> 00:39:44,417
YEAH, THAT'S IT.

901
00:39:44,450 --> 00:39:45,952
HEY, WHAT YOU DOIN', GYPS?

902
00:39:45,985 --> 00:39:48,153
THIS IS VERY, VERY,
VERY IMPORTANT.

903
00:39:48,187 --> 00:39:50,055
AND THERE'S
THE GUITAR LICK--

904
00:39:50,088 --> 00:39:52,023
WAIT, CAN YOU TWO
KEEP A SECRET?

905
00:39:52,057 --> 00:39:53,992
- NOPE.
- NEVER COULD,
NEVER WILL, GYPSY.

906
00:39:54,025 --> 00:39:55,460
- [BOTH LAUGH]
- OH, NO.
- OKAY, CROW,

907
00:39:55,493 --> 00:39:57,697
HOW ABOUT BONANZA,
INCLUDING THE WORDS.

908
00:39:57,730 --> 00:39:59,332
OH, OKAY.

909
00:39:59,365 --> 00:40:00,867
♪ IT'S ALL RIGHT
IF I PICK A LITTLE FIGHT ♪

910
00:40:00,900 --> 00:40:03,435
- ♪ BONANZA ♪
- OH MY GOODNESS.

911
00:40:03,468 --> 00:40:06,005
OH-- I'M BEING TESTED.

912
00:40:06,038 --> 00:40:07,172
OH...

913
00:40:07,205 --> 00:40:09,975
WHO? WHO IS TESTING GYPSY?

914
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:11,677
HELLO?

915
00:40:11,710 --> 00:40:13,045
WELL, I WILL PREVAIL.

916
00:40:13,078 --> 00:40:15,982
BECAUSE I AM GOOD,
AND THE MADS ARE EVIL.

917
00:40:16,015 --> 00:40:17,717
BUT-- AAH!

918
00:40:20,052 --> 00:40:21,653
OH, YOU GUYS
GOT MOVIE LIGHT.

919
00:40:21,687 --> 00:40:23,855
AAH!

920
00:40:36,035 --> 00:40:37,570
WHAT'S EATING GYPSY?

921
00:40:37,603 --> 00:40:39,272
HEY, WANNA DO SOMETHING
LATER MAYBE?

922
00:40:39,305 --> 00:40:40,840
GOT THE CORRECT TIME?

923
00:40:40,873 --> 00:40:43,375
YEAH, TEN TO.
TEN TO YOUR OWN DAMN BUSINESS.

924
00:40:43,408 --> 00:40:44,577
TEN TO TWELVE.

925
00:40:44,610 --> 00:40:45,845
NOON OR MIDNIGHT?

926
00:40:45,878 --> 00:40:49,582
THAT GUY CUMMINGS
SURE GETS AROUND.

927
00:40:49,615 --> 00:40:52,417
THAT'S SURE
SOME SCHEDULE HE'S GOT.

928
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:54,152
DON'T BOTHER ME, MISTER.

929
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:56,522
ANTI-SOCIAL TYPE, HUH?

930
00:40:56,555 --> 00:40:58,523
PRIVATE TYPE?

931
00:40:58,557 --> 00:40:59,858
MAYBE YOU SHOULD LET
OTHER PEOPLE HAVE

932
00:40:59,892 --> 00:41:01,560
THEIR PRIVACY.

933
00:41:01,593 --> 00:41:03,995
MY FACE HURTS.

934
00:41:04,028 --> 00:41:06,165
WHAT WAS THAT ALL ABOUT?

935
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:10,035
AH, DARYL GATES
ON HIS DAY OFF.

936
00:41:10,068 --> 00:41:13,805
HEY, I'M PUTTING HERE.

937
00:41:13,838 --> 00:41:16,775
HE'S LANDED
JUST SHORT OF THE GREEN.

938
00:41:16,808 --> 00:41:19,712
OH NO, MR. TREVINO'S
BEEN HIT AGAIN!

939
00:41:19,745 --> 00:41:21,513
[MAN GROANS]

940
00:41:23,748 --> 00:41:26,385
ISN'T THAT CUTE? HE'S TRYING
TO TELL US SOMETHING.

941
00:41:27,820 --> 00:41:29,888
HEY, CAN WE PLAY THROUGH?
WE GOT A HEADWIND BACK HERE.

942
00:41:29,922 --> 00:41:31,257
YOU WANNA HOLD THIS?

943
00:41:31,290 --> 00:41:33,992
I GOTTA GO CALL
HEADQUARTERS.

944
00:41:34,025 --> 00:41:35,260
THAT MERLIN IS LOST

945
00:41:35,293 --> 00:41:38,097
WITHOUT A MAP.

946
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,232
DON'T LAUGH, YOU'RE ONLY
ENCOURAGING HIM.

947
00:41:40,265 --> 00:41:42,868
[JOEL CHUCKLES]
MITCHELL!

948
00:41:42,902 --> 00:41:45,737
[ALL LAUGH]

949
00:41:45,770 --> 00:41:47,607
THE NEW CHRYSLER FURY.

950
00:41:47,640 --> 00:41:50,943
THE CAR THAT
THINKS IT'S A HOUSE.

951
00:41:50,977 --> 00:41:53,512
CAN'T BELIEVE IT-- I'M IN
TROUBLE FOR KILLING A CIVILIAN.

952
00:41:53,545 --> 00:41:54,713
I THOUGHT YOUR JOB
WAS CUMMINGS.

953
00:41:54,747 --> 00:41:56,615
- I'VE BEEN BUSY.
- OH, REALLY?

954
00:41:56,648 --> 00:41:57,717
WAIT, THAT GUY WITH
THE LEG WOUND,

955
00:41:57,750 --> 00:41:59,785
- HAS HE TALKED YET?
- NOPE.

956
00:41:59,818 --> 00:42:01,253
YOU MAY BE FACING
A DISCIPLINARY CHARGE

957
00:42:01,287 --> 00:42:02,622
FOR SHOOTING HIM.

958
00:42:02,655 --> 00:42:04,022
YOU WANTED HIM
FOR TWO WEEKS WITH NO BAIL,

959
00:42:04,055 --> 00:42:05,323
AND THAT'S HOW YOU GOT HIM.

960
00:42:05,357 --> 00:42:07,292
I DIDN'T EXPECT YOU
TO SHOOT HIM.

961
00:42:07,325 --> 00:42:09,093
OH, YOU'RE ASKING THAT?
OH, RICH.

962
00:42:09,127 --> 00:42:10,828
I THOUGHT I HAD
AUTHORITY OVER HIM.

963
00:42:10,862 --> 00:42:13,298
YOU SHOULDN'T'VE
BLOWN YOUR COVER LIKE THAT.

964
00:42:13,332 --> 00:42:15,200
I'LL GO PHONE HEADQUARTERS.

965
00:42:15,233 --> 00:42:17,670
PASS THE POTATOES, THE PEAS,
THE BUTTER, THE PEAS,

966
00:42:17,703 --> 00:42:19,272
THE PIE, THE BUTTER.

967
00:42:19,305 --> 00:42:21,773
OF COURSE YOU'RE NOT ASHAMED,
AND THAT'S YOUR TROUBLE.

968
00:42:21,807 --> 00:42:24,175
TROUBLE, UH, PASS THE GRAVY
AND THE STUFFING.

969
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:27,713
DON'T FORGET MR. MITCHELL.

970
00:42:27,747 --> 00:42:29,448
[SPITS] OH,
THAT'S ONE OF MINE.

971
00:42:29,482 --> 00:42:32,752
YUCK.

972
00:42:32,785 --> 00:42:36,222
THIS IS THE PART
OF BEING A HENCHMAN I HATE.

973
00:42:36,255 --> 00:42:39,057
CAN I TEMPT YOU
WITH SOME DESSERT?

974
00:42:39,090 --> 00:42:41,693
I DON'T THINK
BENTON LIKES YOU.

975
00:42:41,727 --> 00:42:44,697
UH, CAN WE GET MORE VOLUME
ON THAT JACKET, PLEASE?

976
00:42:44,730 --> 00:42:48,367
THAT'S YOUR TROUBLE.
NOT TOO MANY PEOPLE LIKE YOU.

977
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:50,335
YOU GOTTA CULTIVATE PEOPLE.
GO OUT TO THEM.

978
00:42:50,368 --> 00:42:51,870
WIN THEIR CONFIDENCE.
YOU NEVER KNOW

979
00:42:51,903 --> 00:42:53,238
WHEN THEY'RE GONNA
COME IN USEFUL.

980
00:42:53,272 --> 00:42:54,473
YOU GOTTA BE NICE TO THEM.

981
00:42:54,507 --> 00:42:56,308
NICE-- MORE BUTTER, PLEASE.

982
00:42:56,342 --> 00:42:58,777
BUT WHAT ABOUT THE HEROIN,
MR. CUMMINGS?

983
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:00,578
- FORGET THE HEROIN.
- THAT'S FOR DESSERT.

984
00:43:00,612 --> 00:43:02,682
YOU ASK ABOUT THE HEROIN
OVER THE SOUP.

985
00:43:02,715 --> 00:43:04,550
THAT'S YOUR TROUBLE.
YOU'RE IMPATIENT.

986
00:43:04,583 --> 00:43:06,785
NOW, YOU WENT AT THAT GUY AS IF
HE WAS GONNA DO YOU SOME HARM.

987
00:43:06,818 --> 00:43:08,787
I WANTED TO FIND OUT
WHO HE WAS.

988
00:43:08,820 --> 00:43:11,557
WELL, ASK HIM.
DON'T SHOOT HIM.

989
00:43:11,590 --> 00:43:12,758
WHO WAS HE?

990
00:43:12,792 --> 00:43:15,627
I DIDN'T ASK HIM.
I SHOT HIM.

991
00:43:15,660 --> 00:43:17,362
UH, BOOKER. ED BOOKER.

992
00:43:17,395 --> 00:43:18,930
BOOKER'S A GOOD COP!

993
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:20,765
BOOKER. BOOKER. BOOKER?

994
00:43:20,798 --> 00:43:22,367
WHO'S GOT THE BOOKER?

995
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:26,105
WITH A DOUBLE-C.
EDMUNDO BOCCA.

996
00:43:26,138 --> 00:43:27,372
LIKE THE SOUP?

997
00:43:27,405 --> 00:43:30,775
- GOES WITH MY TIE.
- YES.

998
00:43:30,808 --> 00:43:33,445
YOU GOT THIS PLACE LAID OUT LIKE
A REAL BANQUET, MR. CUMMINGS.

999
00:43:33,478 --> 00:43:35,280
OR A BUSINESS DINNER.

1000
00:43:35,313 --> 00:43:37,148
WE MIGHT TALK BUSINESS LATER.

1001
00:43:37,182 --> 00:43:38,550
I'M GONNA HAVE
SOME MORE SOUP, BENTON.

1002
00:43:38,583 --> 00:43:41,153
UH, THERE IS
NO MORE SOUP, SIR.

1003
00:43:41,187 --> 00:43:42,955
I SENSE HE'S LYING, BUT
WHY WOULD HE LIE ABOUT SOUP?

1004
00:43:42,988 --> 00:43:46,025
HOW DO YOU LIKE THAT?
IN MY OWN HOUSE, NO MORE SOUP.

1005
00:43:46,058 --> 00:43:48,727
MY DINNER WITH MITCHELL.

1006
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:50,728
BOCCA WORKS FOR MISTRETTA.

1007
00:43:50,762 --> 00:43:52,330
THAT'S THE FIRST
PIECE OF INFORMATION

1008
00:43:52,363 --> 00:43:53,932
YOU'VE COME UP WITH,
MR. CUMMINGS.

1009
00:43:53,965 --> 00:43:56,602
HOW ABOUT
LETTING US IN ON SOME?

1010
00:43:56,635 --> 00:43:59,203
WHAT'RE YOU DOING WITH THOSE
STEAKS? YOU GROWING THEM?

1011
00:43:59,237 --> 00:44:01,707
HUH, YOU CAN'T GROW STEAKS.

1012
00:44:03,342 --> 00:44:05,143
OH, WAIT, I WANT
THE BONE MARROW.

1013
00:44:07,412 --> 00:44:09,213
OH, BOOM MIKE. BIG TIME.

1014
00:44:09,247 --> 00:44:11,317
GONNA TAKE ALL NIGHT
PEELING THAT ORANGE?

1015
00:44:11,350 --> 00:44:14,853
WELL, I THOUGHT MAYBE WE MIGHT
TALK ABOUT THE SHIPMENT.

1016
00:44:17,957 --> 00:44:20,258
WOULD YOU JUST
GIVE ME THAT ORANGE?

1017
00:44:22,427 --> 00:44:25,097
I HAVE A NEW FRIEND.

1018
00:44:26,932 --> 00:44:29,033
UH, HEY, I PUT A COUPLE
OF ROLLS IN MY POCKET--

1019
00:44:29,067 --> 00:44:31,903
IS THAT OKAY?

1020
00:44:31,937 --> 00:44:33,505
BUT WHAT I WANNA KNOW IS--

1021
00:44:33,538 --> 00:44:35,707
THE COFFEE'S COLD, BENTON.
YOU'RE A LOUSY BUTLER.

1022
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:38,077
- I AM NOT A LOUSY BUTLER.
- YOU ARE A LOUSY BUTLER.

1023
00:44:38,110 --> 00:44:40,545
- I AM NOT.
- I SAY YOU'RE A LOUSY BUTLER.

1024
00:44:40,578 --> 00:44:42,147
- THE COFFEE IS COLD.
- WELL, I THINK I GOTTA GO.

1025
00:44:42,180 --> 00:44:45,417
IT'S THE SERVANT
BY HAROLD PINTER.

1026
00:44:45,450 --> 00:44:48,187
OH, LOOK,
YOU MADE MITCHELL LEAVE.

1027
00:44:54,927 --> 00:44:57,328
OH, MAN, I'M SO HUNGRY.

1028
00:44:57,362 --> 00:44:59,665
ONLY TWO STEAKS FOR DINNER.
DIDN'T GET TO FINISH MY ORANGE.

1029
00:44:59,698 --> 00:45:01,333
ALL THE FROZEN YOGURT PLACES

1030
00:45:01,367 --> 00:45:04,670
WERE CLOSED.

1031
00:45:04,703 --> 00:45:06,572
A BIG BUTTERY MOON UP THERE.

1032
00:45:06,605 --> 00:45:09,775
SIDEWALK KIND OF LOOKS LIKE
ICE CREAM IF YOU SQUINT HARD.

1033
00:45:09,808 --> 00:45:12,343
- STAIRS LOOK LIKE CAKE.
- [DOG BARKS]

1034
00:45:12,377 --> 00:45:14,378
MITCHELL'S LEGIONS
OF FANS SHOW UP

1035
00:45:14,412 --> 00:45:16,815
AT ANY TIME
OF THE DAY OR NIGHT.

1036
00:45:19,985 --> 00:45:21,920
WELL, THIS'LL BE OKAY,
I DON'T SEE--

1037
00:45:21,953 --> 00:45:25,890
OOH!

1038
00:45:25,923 --> 00:45:28,560
JEEZ, THOSE JEHOVAH'S WITNESSES
ARE GETTING TOUGH.

1039
00:45:28,593 --> 00:45:31,028
WHOA.

1040
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:32,832
NOW THEY'RE GONNA END UP
WITH MITCHELL'S DINNER

1041
00:45:32,865 --> 00:45:35,100
ALL OVER THEM.

1042
00:45:35,133 --> 00:45:36,702
OH-- WAIT, HOLD IT!

1043
00:45:36,735 --> 00:45:39,772
A LITTLE PIECE OF BACON.

1044
00:45:39,805 --> 00:45:41,607
YOU KNOW, IS IT WRONG FOR ME
TO WANNA SEE THIS?

1045
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:43,542
[BOTS] NO.

1046
00:45:43,575 --> 00:45:46,378
OOH! RIGHT IN THE
TENDERLOIN STEAK REGION.

1047
00:45:46,412 --> 00:45:49,180
OH, SORRY, BUD.
WE THOUGHT YOU WERE ROCKFORD.

1048
00:45:51,217 --> 00:45:53,952
HEY, I THINK THIS IS RICE.
OH, NO, IT'S NOT.

1049
00:45:55,820 --> 00:45:57,788
WELL, OLD MITCHELL

1050
00:45:57,822 --> 00:45:59,792
SURE GOT HISSELF HOG-TIED
AND RAILROADED THERE.

1051
00:45:59,825 --> 00:46:03,628
♪♪ [MITCHELL THEME]

1052
00:46:03,662 --> 00:46:05,063
WHAT?

1053
00:46:05,097 --> 00:46:06,532
WOULD YOU WATCH THE RIBS?

1054
00:46:06,565 --> 00:46:09,768
OH, HE'S ALONE READING
A COMIC BOOK UNDER THERE.

1055
00:46:13,805 --> 00:46:15,207
- WHOO.
- MITCHELL, HONEY,

1056
00:46:15,240 --> 00:46:17,708
YOU HAVE ANY
NEW-AGE SOMETHING?

1057
00:46:20,178 --> 00:46:22,280
WELL, HE'S SLEEPING
WITH HELEN KELLER.

1058
00:46:27,252 --> 00:46:30,955
OH, HOW I LONG FOR
THE BURNING BED RIGHT NOW.

1059
00:46:30,988 --> 00:46:33,758
HMM, YOU GOT A LOT
OF JUNK AROUND HERE.

1060
00:46:40,698 --> 00:46:44,202
WHY WOULD ANYONE WANT TO DO THIS
WITH MITCHELL, JOEL?

1061
00:46:46,705 --> 00:46:49,675
A VASE OR TWO FACES?

1062
00:46:55,680 --> 00:46:58,417
MM, OH, YANNI--
I MEAN JOHN--

1063
00:46:58,450 --> 00:47:00,652
I MEAN MITCHELL!

1064
00:47:04,355 --> 00:47:06,123
HEY, WATCH THIS--
I LEARNED THIS IN COLLEGE.

1065
00:47:06,157 --> 00:47:08,660
- CHECK THIS OUT.
- THAT'S CLASS.

1066
00:47:08,693 --> 00:47:11,263
[SERVO MIMICS CAN FIZZING]

1067
00:47:11,297 --> 00:47:14,232
- BABY OIL!
- [ALL SCREAM]

1068
00:47:17,268 --> 00:47:20,472
[SERVO VOMITS]

1069
00:47:20,505 --> 00:47:22,942
MY-MY-MY GOD NO!

1070
00:47:22,975 --> 00:47:25,943
[ALL SCREAM]

1071
00:47:25,977 --> 00:47:27,278
[CROW SOBS]

1072
00:47:27,312 --> 00:47:30,282
AH, COULD YOU MAYBE
GET AROUSED, MITCHELL?

1073
00:47:30,315 --> 00:47:31,817
[SERVO SOBS]

1074
00:47:31,850 --> 00:47:34,518
UM, HOW ABOUT SOME BTO?

1075
00:47:39,390 --> 00:47:40,858
YOU WENT THROUGH
THAT TOOTHPASTE.

1076
00:47:40,892 --> 00:47:42,560
AND I STILL DON'T HAVE
ANY TIC-TACS.

1077
00:47:42,593 --> 00:47:46,532
BUT THIS IS THURSDAY.

1078
00:47:46,565 --> 00:47:49,100
HE MAKES A GOOD POINT.

1079
00:47:52,037 --> 00:47:53,705
YOU KNOW YOU'D GET BUSTED
FOR THIS.

1080
00:47:53,738 --> 00:47:56,708
GUY THAT BUSTS ME WOULD
HAVE TO BE REALLY STRAIGHT.

1081
00:47:56,742 --> 00:47:58,943
ARE YOU IMPLYING THAT
I'M NOT STRAIGHT?

1082
00:47:58,977 --> 00:48:01,580
YOU'RE BOOZY BUT LOVABLE.

1083
00:48:03,348 --> 00:48:05,383
YOU'RE AS BENT
AS THE TOWER OF PISA.

1084
00:48:05,417 --> 00:48:07,585
THE ONLY PROBLEM IS
YOU DON'T KNOW IT.

1085
00:48:07,618 --> 00:48:11,357
YOU REALLY THINK I'D TAKE
SOME SORT OF A PAY-OFF, HUH?

1086
00:48:11,390 --> 00:48:13,225
YOU ALREADY HAVE,
HAVEN'T YOU?

1087
00:48:13,258 --> 00:48:15,560
OH, WAIT A MINUTE.

1088
00:48:15,593 --> 00:48:16,962
YOU WERE A CHRISTMAS GIFT.

1089
00:48:16,995 --> 00:48:18,897
- AND I WANTED A SUPER-SOAKER.
- THAT'S WHAT YOU SAID.

1090
00:48:18,930 --> 00:48:21,633
- DID I?
- DIDN'T YOU? DAMN RIGHT.

1091
00:48:21,667 --> 00:48:23,902
THAT DOESN'T MAKE ME
THE COOPERATIVE TYPE.

1092
00:48:23,935 --> 00:48:25,437
YOU JUST WATCH
YOUR PRETTY MOUTH.

1093
00:48:25,470 --> 00:48:27,438
SO BUST ME.

1094
00:48:27,472 --> 00:48:30,375
YOU'RE A POLICEMAN,
AND THAT'S GRASS.

1095
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:31,977
MERLIN OLSEN SENT HIM
THAT PAINTING.

1096
00:48:32,010 --> 00:48:33,512
[SHE LAUGHS]

1097
00:48:33,545 --> 00:48:35,180
MY MITCHELL.
I THINK I'LL KEEP HIM.

1098
00:48:35,213 --> 00:48:38,450
OH. COME ON. COME ON!

1099
00:48:38,483 --> 00:48:42,187
- [KISSING]
- EWW.

1100
00:48:42,220 --> 00:48:44,122
ARE THEY DONE? CAN I LOOK?

1101
00:48:44,155 --> 00:48:46,592
WELL, YOU SURE KNOW
HOW TO BRING A GIRL DOWN.

1102
00:48:46,625 --> 00:48:50,162
UH, DOUBLE-ROOM PLEASE.
ONE NIGHT.

1103
00:48:50,195 --> 00:48:52,030
HE SLEEPS WITH ME,
THEN BUSTS ME.

1104
00:48:52,063 --> 00:48:53,465
FIRST THINGS FIRST.

1105
00:48:53,498 --> 00:48:54,632
WELL, SHE ASKED ME TO.

1106
00:48:54,665 --> 00:48:58,403
WHAT? SLEEP WITH HER
OR BUST HER?

1107
00:48:58,437 --> 00:49:01,272
- BOTH.
- [TRUMPET] WAA-WAA-WAA.

1108
00:49:01,305 --> 00:49:04,608
--WHEN YOUR CASE IS HEARD.

1109
00:49:04,642 --> 00:49:05,977
HAVE YOU GOT
ANY OTHER OFFENSES

1110
00:49:06,010 --> 00:49:08,880
YOU'D LIKE FOR US
TO TAKE INTO CONSIDERATION

1111
00:49:08,913 --> 00:49:10,948
WHILE YOU'RE IN
THIS KIND OF A MOOD?

1112
00:49:10,982 --> 00:49:14,385
YEAH, GETTING HUNG UP
ON THIS GUY.

1113
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:15,887
THAT'S A MISTAKE, LADY.

1114
00:49:15,920 --> 00:49:19,023
- DIDN'T DO ME ANY GOOD.
- NOT ON THE FENCE.

1115
00:49:19,057 --> 00:49:20,258
WHEN CAN I SEE MY LAWYER?

1116
00:49:20,292 --> 00:49:21,793
WE'LL TAKE CARE OF IT
FOR YOU.

1117
00:49:21,827 --> 00:49:23,728
UH, YOU'RE SLEEPING WITH HIM
AT 3:00.

1118
00:49:23,762 --> 00:49:25,030
--AN HOUR OR SO.

1119
00:49:25,063 --> 00:49:28,333
HEY, IT'S ONLY A $500 FINE.

1120
00:49:28,367 --> 00:49:31,570
- AT $1,000 A NIGHT,
YOU'RE STILL AHEAD.
- NOT AFTER TAXES.

1121
00:49:31,603 --> 00:49:33,272
OH, YOU'RE A TERRIFIC
HUMAN BEING, MITCHELL.

1122
00:49:33,305 --> 00:49:35,473
I HAD A CLEAN RECORD
IN THIS TOWN.

1123
00:49:35,507 --> 00:49:36,975
SIRENS.

1124
00:49:37,008 --> 00:49:40,345
HEY.

1125
00:49:40,378 --> 00:49:43,482
MAKE SURE SHE SIGNS
THE PROPERTY RECEIPT.

1126
00:49:43,515 --> 00:49:46,852
NOBODY ELSE FOR A PROSTITUTE.
WE'LL TAKE HER RIGHT AWAY.

1127
00:49:46,885 --> 00:49:49,220
ARE WE STILL ON FOR TUESDAY?

1128
00:49:49,253 --> 00:49:52,890
HEY, YOU REALLY
SLEEP WITH THAT?

1129
00:49:52,923 --> 00:49:55,860
- YEP.
- THEN I KISSED HER!

1130
00:49:59,597 --> 00:50:01,500
- HEY WALLY.
- MITCH.

1131
00:50:01,533 --> 00:50:03,702
- [CAR HONKS]
- ♪ BY BENEFICIAL ♪

1132
00:50:03,735 --> 00:50:05,237
YOU'RE GOOD FOR MORE.

1133
00:50:05,270 --> 00:50:07,305
[CAR HONKS]

1134
00:50:07,338 --> 00:50:09,373
THE DECLINING YEARS
OF LEE MAJORS.

1135
00:50:09,407 --> 00:50:12,977
ASK HIM TO COME IN.
SAY THAT IT'S IMPORTANT.

1136
00:50:13,010 --> 00:50:14,312
SAY THAT I HAVE TO SEE HIM.

1137
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:17,515
- YES, SIR.
- TELL HIM WE HAVE SOUR CREAM.

1138
00:50:22,587 --> 00:50:25,423
OH MAN, THIS STAKEOUT'S
GETTING CROWDED.

1139
00:50:26,925 --> 00:50:29,593
HI, FOLKS.

1140
00:50:31,863 --> 00:50:35,500
D'UH, THE STEAKS ARE READY.

1141
00:50:35,533 --> 00:50:37,635
HEY, CAN LINDA COME TOO?

1142
00:50:40,305 --> 00:50:41,907
SO, TELL ME, MERLIN.

1143
00:50:41,940 --> 00:50:45,743
UH, DO YOU KNOW
ROMAN GABRIEL?

1144
00:50:45,777 --> 00:50:48,613
I THINK
YOU'RE A GOOD BUTLER.

1145
00:50:48,647 --> 00:50:50,282
♪ MOVING ON UP! ♪

1146
00:50:50,315 --> 00:50:51,983
WEEZY?

1147
00:50:52,017 --> 00:50:54,452
- THIS WAY.
- TO WALL DRUG.

1148
00:50:56,888 --> 00:50:58,857
- YOU WANT A DRINK?
- IS THE POPE CATHOLIC?

1149
00:50:58,890 --> 00:51:00,125
SIT DOWN.

1150
00:51:00,158 --> 00:51:03,628
WANNA SHOOT A BEER BONG?

1151
00:51:03,662 --> 00:51:05,297
ALL RIGHT, MITCHELL.

1152
00:51:05,330 --> 00:51:06,798
IT'S TIME WE STOPPED
MESSING AROUND.

1153
00:51:06,832 --> 00:51:08,133
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

1154
00:51:08,167 --> 00:51:09,300
I WANNA PUT YOU
ON THE PAYROLL.

1155
00:51:09,333 --> 00:51:10,902
WE HAVE AN OPENING
IN RETAIL.

1156
00:51:10,935 --> 00:51:13,205
--I'M IN TROUBLE.
YOU SENSED IT. YOU KNOW IT.

1157
00:51:13,238 --> 00:51:16,073
- AND I KNOW IT.
- SPECIFICALLY WHAT TROUBLE?

1158
00:51:16,107 --> 00:51:17,508
WELL, THE IDEA
OF THE PAYROLL.

1159
00:51:17,542 --> 00:51:18,977
NOW I GET TO ASK
THE QUESTIONS.

1160
00:51:19,010 --> 00:51:20,745
NOTED.

1161
00:51:20,778 --> 00:51:23,215
- I NEED HELP.
- I GOT A PURPLE MOLE
ON MY BACK.

1162
00:51:23,248 --> 00:51:25,483
I NEED HELP FROM ANY SOURCE
THAT I CAN GET IT.

1163
00:51:25,517 --> 00:51:27,785
- SO I'M DOWN TO YOU.
- --PUT IT ON THE LINE.

1164
00:51:27,818 --> 00:51:29,420
I WANNA BUY YOUR SERVICES.

1165
00:51:29,453 --> 00:51:31,523
YOUR VOICE ON THE PHONE
IN CASE I NEED THE HELP

1166
00:51:31,557 --> 00:51:33,458
OF YOUR POLICE DEPARTMENT.

1167
00:51:33,492 --> 00:51:34,927
LET ME JUST, UH,

1168
00:51:34,960 --> 00:51:36,495
WRITE THE DETAILS
OF YOUR BRIBE DOWN,

1169
00:51:36,528 --> 00:51:37,928
MR. CUMMINGS.

1170
00:51:37,962 --> 00:51:39,898
- IT'S A SHRINERS CAR.
- [CROW MIMICS CARNIVAL MUSIC]

1171
00:51:39,932 --> 00:51:42,933
OH, A PLACE IN THE SHADE--
OOH.

1172
00:51:48,273 --> 00:51:50,342
HE PULLED OUT
RIGHT IN FRONT OF ME!

1173
00:51:52,510 --> 00:51:53,745
HARUMPH!

1174
00:51:53,778 --> 00:51:57,648
SHE'S GOT A DAVID CASSIDY
HAIR-CUT.

1175
00:51:57,682 --> 00:52:00,652
HEH, SHE'S GONNA WRITE
"REDRUM" ON HIS WINDSHIELD.

1176
00:52:00,685 --> 00:52:04,455
RED... OH.

1177
00:52:04,488 --> 00:52:07,292
HE'LL THINK OF ME THE WHOLE TIME
HE'S CLEANING THAT OFF.

1178
00:52:08,527 --> 00:52:11,830
UH, WERE YOU EXPECTING
A PROSTITUTE?

1179
00:52:11,863 --> 00:52:14,032
WORD ON THE STREET
IS YOU'RE A JERK.

1180
00:52:14,065 --> 00:52:16,935
COULD BE OPEN? CASH?

1181
00:52:16,968 --> 00:52:19,270
IT'S SUBTLE, JUST THE WAY
YOU TAKE IT FROM OTHER PEOPLE.

1182
00:52:19,303 --> 00:52:21,807
- I DON'T TAKE BRIBES.
- BUT I DO TAKE DICTATION.

1183
00:52:21,840 --> 00:52:23,140
--CITY HALL SAID
THEY SAW YOU

1184
00:52:23,173 --> 00:52:24,508
IN COURT THIS MORNING
WITH A HOOKER

1185
00:52:24,542 --> 00:52:26,612
THAT YOU SLEEP WITH AND
OCCASIONALLY ARREST.

1186
00:52:26,645 --> 00:52:27,878
WHAT ELSE THEY TELL YOU?

1187
00:52:27,912 --> 00:52:29,680
SHE'S TOO EXPENSIVE.
YOU CAN'T AFFORD HER

1188
00:52:29,713 --> 00:52:31,248
ON A POLICEMAN'S SALARY.

1189
00:52:31,282 --> 00:52:32,983
NOW SOMEBODY'S
PICKING UP THE CHECK.

1190
00:52:33,017 --> 00:52:35,720
- WHO COULD THAT BE?
- YOU.

1191
00:52:35,753 --> 00:52:37,955
- ME WHAT?
- YOU'RE PICKING UP
THE CHECK.

1192
00:52:37,988 --> 00:52:41,225
NO, I DON'T PAY FOR
YOUR HOOKERS, MITCHELL.

1193
00:52:41,258 --> 00:52:42,527
- WELL, COULD YOU?
- BUT WHO IS?

1194
00:52:42,560 --> 00:52:43,862
YOU MEAN YOU DON'T KNOW?

1195
00:52:43,895 --> 00:52:46,698
YOU'RE A COP
AND YOU DON'T KNOW?

1196
00:52:46,732 --> 00:52:50,468
[SERVO LAUGHS]
NO, I DON'T.

1197
00:52:50,502 --> 00:52:54,072
I SPECIFICALLY
CAME HERE FOR DINNER.

1198
00:52:54,105 --> 00:52:55,873
- [MITCHELL SNAPS FINGERS]
- GET ME SOME FLOWERS.

1199
00:52:55,907 --> 00:52:58,175
PRONTO, MERLIN.

1200
00:52:58,208 --> 00:53:00,612
NOW, WAIT, YOU'RE NOT LEAVING
WITHOUT SOME TUNA WIGGLE.

1201
00:53:00,645 --> 00:53:02,580
DAMN.

1202
00:53:13,057 --> 00:53:16,027
HE'S GOT A LIGHT-EMITTING
BALD SPOT.

1203
00:53:21,633 --> 00:53:23,635
SOMEONE TO SEE YOU, SIR.

1204
00:53:23,668 --> 00:53:25,403
I KNEW YOU'D CALL
SOONER OR LATER.

1205
00:53:25,437 --> 00:53:27,205
SO, ARE YOU READY
TO JOIN HAIR CLUB YET?

1206
00:53:27,238 --> 00:53:28,907
COME ON.

1207
00:53:28,940 --> 00:53:32,877
JOE DON BAKER.
FACE NUMBER FOUR.

1208
00:53:32,910 --> 00:53:36,848
- HEY, JOE DON.
- NO.

1209
00:53:36,882 --> 00:53:39,083
- SIT DOWN.
- PROSTITUTE?

1210
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:43,253
HOW DO YOU LIKE YOUR SCOTCH?

1211
00:53:43,287 --> 00:53:46,658
UH, BY THE QUART.

1212
00:53:46,692 --> 00:53:48,025
COME ON, MORE. COME ON.

1213
00:53:48,058 --> 00:53:49,693
KEEP IT COMING.
I'M A BIG BOY. THAT'S RIGHT.

1214
00:53:49,727 --> 00:53:52,263
MM-HMM.

1215
00:53:52,297 --> 00:53:54,532
I USUALLY TAKE IT
WITH A DING-DONG IN IT.

1216
00:53:54,565 --> 00:53:56,067
BUT, UH, I GUESS
I'LL TAKE IT NEAT.

1217
00:53:56,100 --> 00:53:57,602
THAT'S OKAY.

1218
00:53:57,635 --> 00:54:00,872
- YOU KNOW--
- BOOZE IS GOOD FOOD.

1219
00:54:00,905 --> 00:54:02,507
I ADMIRE A MAN LIKE YOU.

1220
00:54:02,540 --> 00:54:03,842
NOT YOU SPECIFICALLY.

1221
00:54:03,875 --> 00:54:06,945
YOU TAKE YOUR TIME.

1222
00:54:06,978 --> 00:54:09,347
- YOU'RE COOL.
- YEAH.

1223
00:54:09,380 --> 00:54:10,548
YES, SIR.

1224
00:54:10,582 --> 00:54:11,850
YOU KNOW,
HE MAY BE A BAD GUY,

1225
00:54:11,883 --> 00:54:14,352
BUT HE'S GOT
A TON OF GIFTS UP THERE.

1226
00:54:14,385 --> 00:54:15,487
HOW'S THE BROAD?

1227
00:54:15,520 --> 00:54:17,422
THAT'S WHAT I CAME
TO TALK ABOUT.

1228
00:54:17,455 --> 00:54:19,790
YOU KNOW WHAT IT COSTS
TO KEEP YOU SWEET?

1229
00:54:19,823 --> 00:54:22,193
A HUNDRED BUCKS AN HOUR.

1230
00:54:22,227 --> 00:54:24,128
IF SOMETHING HAPPENS
ALL NIGHT,

1231
00:54:24,162 --> 00:54:26,030
WELL, YOU FIGURE IT OUT.
THAT'S LIKE, UH,

1232
00:54:26,063 --> 00:54:27,998
A THOUSAND BUCKS
BEFORE BREAKFAST.

1233
00:54:28,032 --> 00:54:29,967
AS FAR AS I'M CONCERNED,
SHE'S JUST SOME BROAD

1234
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:31,937
LOOKING FOR A LITTLE ACTION.

1235
00:54:31,970 --> 00:54:33,303
YOU WANNA SEE THE RECEIPT?

1236
00:54:33,337 --> 00:54:34,938
YOU'RE WASTING YOUR MONEY,
DEANEY.

1237
00:54:34,972 --> 00:54:36,573
LET ME BE THE JUDGE OF THAT.

1238
00:54:36,607 --> 00:54:38,743
SHE'LL LIE IN MY BED
FOR NOTHING.

1239
00:54:38,777 --> 00:54:41,312
WELL, I GUESS I'LL HAVE
TO TALK TO MY ACCOUNTANT.

1240
00:54:41,345 --> 00:54:42,580
YOU REALLY THINK SO.

1241
00:54:42,613 --> 00:54:44,548
I'M TURNIN' JAPANESE.

1242
00:54:48,218 --> 00:54:51,222
LET ME SHOW YOU
WHAT I GOT FOR CHRISTMAS.

1243
00:54:51,255 --> 00:54:53,792
I ARRANGE A HUNDRED DOLLAR
COMPANY IN YOUR NAME.

1244
00:54:53,825 --> 00:54:56,093
- YOU MEAN ORION?
- --NEGOTIATE THE TRANSFER

1245
00:54:56,127 --> 00:54:58,128
OF A PIECE OF REAL ESTATE.

1246
00:54:58,162 --> 00:55:00,932
CROSS TO FIREPLACE.

1247
00:55:00,965 --> 00:55:04,702
- SO LET'S SAY--
- I'M ROSALIND RUSSELL.

1248
00:55:04,735 --> 00:55:06,772
$25,000.

1249
00:55:06,805 --> 00:55:08,840
YOU HAVEN'T GOT $25,000.

1250
00:55:08,873 --> 00:55:10,342
BUT I'LL GET YOU
A BANK LOAN.

1251
00:55:10,375 --> 00:55:13,343
ALL LEGITIMATE.

1252
00:55:13,377 --> 00:55:16,982
THE REAL ESTATE YOU BUY
WILL BE A PIECE I DESIGNATE.

1253
00:55:17,015 --> 00:55:19,550
AND YOU'LL BUY IT FROM
ONE OF MY SUBSIDIARY COMPANIES.

1254
00:55:19,583 --> 00:55:20,785
OH MAN, I'M SO LOST.

1255
00:55:20,818 --> 00:55:22,820
I'LL BUY IT OFF YOU.

1256
00:55:22,853 --> 00:55:25,557
FOR, LET'S SAY,
A HUNDRED G'S.

1257
00:55:25,590 --> 00:55:27,025
THAT'LL GIVE YOU
A CLEAR PROFIT

1258
00:55:27,058 --> 00:55:29,727
OF $75,000.

1259
00:55:29,760 --> 00:55:32,630
AND WHO'S TO SAY IT ISN'T
A GENUINE INVESTMENT?

1260
00:55:32,663 --> 00:55:33,998
IS THAT A SLIM JIM?

1261
00:55:34,032 --> 00:55:36,300
CAN I HAVE THAT?
ARE YOU DONE WITH THAT?

1262
00:55:36,333 --> 00:55:37,635
DO YOU OPEN YOUR
CHRISTMAS PRESENTS

1263
00:55:37,668 --> 00:55:38,903
ON CHRISTMAS EVE
OR CHRISTMAS MORNING?

1264
00:55:38,937 --> 00:55:42,473
WELL, WHAT DO YOU THINK?

1265
00:55:42,507 --> 00:55:44,308
I'M GONNA GET YOU
FOR THAT MURDER.

1266
00:55:44,342 --> 00:55:45,543
BUT FIRST, MERRY CHRISTMAS.

1267
00:55:45,577 --> 00:55:47,045
OR I'LL DIE TRYING.

1268
00:55:47,078 --> 00:55:48,947
YOU'RE MAKING THE BIGGEST
MISTAKE OF YOUR LIFE.

1269
00:55:57,322 --> 00:56:00,023
YEP, ANOTHER WEDNESDAY NIGHT
AT MITCHELL'S.

1270
00:56:00,057 --> 00:56:02,427
OUR HERO,
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.

1271
00:56:02,460 --> 00:56:04,128
DAMN IT,
I'M STILL NOT DRUNK.

1272
00:56:04,162 --> 00:56:06,130
♪♪ [HOYT AXTON SONG]

1273
00:56:06,163 --> 00:56:09,633
OH MY GOODNESS, I THINK
P.J. THOMAS IS IN HIS ROOM.

1274
00:56:09,667 --> 00:56:12,503
♪♪

1275
00:56:12,537 --> 00:56:14,672
[CROW SLURPS]
OH-- YUCK!

1276
00:56:14,705 --> 00:56:17,408
I GOT A CIGARETTE.

1277
00:56:17,442 --> 00:56:18,943
I LIKE TO TOP OFF
MY BEER-DRINKING

1278
00:56:18,977 --> 00:56:21,813
WITH ANOTHER BEER.
IT'S LIKE DESSERT.

1279
00:56:21,847 --> 00:56:25,650
IT'S A VERY SPECIAL
JOE DON BAKER CHRISTMAS.

1280
00:56:25,683 --> 00:56:27,552
[SERVO GRUNTS]

1281
00:56:27,585 --> 00:56:30,755
[SERVO RASPBERRIES]

1282
00:56:30,788 --> 00:56:32,357
[CROW LAUGHS]

1283
00:56:32,390 --> 00:56:33,858
BOOZE AND I ARE
BUYING A HOUSE TOGETHER.

1284
00:56:33,892 --> 00:56:37,228
WE'RE GONNA MOVE IN.

1285
00:56:37,262 --> 00:56:38,930
HE'S GONNA STRIP DOWN
TO HIS UNDERWEAR

1286
00:56:38,963 --> 00:56:41,498
AND WATCH McHUGH.

1287
00:56:41,532 --> 00:56:43,668
HUH, I WONDER
WHAT THIS THING DOES.

1288
00:56:43,702 --> 00:56:47,405
♪♪

1289
00:56:47,438 --> 00:56:49,640
WHA-- WATER!
I NEVER KNEW THAT.

1290
00:56:49,673 --> 00:56:51,242
- WOW!
- OH-- OH--

1291
00:56:51,275 --> 00:56:53,812
OH, THANK GOD
FOR THE JUMP CUT.

1292
00:56:53,845 --> 00:56:56,447
WALTER HEART DEANEY DIED TODAY
WHEN A DUNE BUGGY--

1293
00:56:56,480 --> 00:56:57,848
[CAR HONKS]

1294
00:56:57,882 --> 00:56:59,783
HONEY, CHURCH!

1295
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:05,957
MITCHELL, I'M NOT GOING
TO YOUR FOLKS FOR CHRISTMAS.

1296
00:57:05,990 --> 00:57:09,160
DAMN, I'M STILL IN
THIS MITCHELL MOVIE.

1297
00:57:09,193 --> 00:57:12,730
ADAM RICH!

1298
00:57:12,763 --> 00:57:14,798
HI.

1299
00:57:14,832 --> 00:57:16,433
ARE YOU THE MAN FROM
THE INSURANCE?

1300
00:57:16,467 --> 00:57:18,435
- NOPE.
- YOU CAME LAST NIGHT.

1301
00:57:18,468 --> 00:57:19,770
NO.

1302
00:57:19,803 --> 00:57:21,338
MY MOTHER DOESN'T LIKE YOU.

1303
00:57:21,372 --> 00:57:23,207
WELL, I DON'T LIKE
YOUR MOTHER.

1304
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,008
- WHY NOT?
- WHY NOT?

1305
00:57:25,042 --> 00:57:27,112
- NO, WHY NOT?
- NO, WHY NOT?

1306
00:57:27,145 --> 00:57:28,445
WHY ARE YOU REPEATING
WHAT I SAY?

1307
00:57:28,478 --> 00:57:30,080
TONIGHT, ON CROSSFIRE!

1308
00:57:30,113 --> 00:57:31,715
- I'M NOT!
- WELL, I'M NOT.

1309
00:57:31,748 --> 00:57:33,585
- YOU ARE.
- BUZZ OFF.

1310
00:57:33,618 --> 00:57:35,420
- WHAT?
- WHAT?

1311
00:57:35,453 --> 00:57:37,122
- WHAT'D YOU SAY?
- WHAT'D YOU SAY?

1312
00:57:37,155 --> 00:57:38,322
- DID YOU SAY SOMETHING?

1313
00:57:38,355 --> 00:57:40,325
AAAAAAAAAH!!!

1314
00:57:40,358 --> 00:57:41,692
YOU'RE LYING
THROUGH YOUR TEETH.

1315
00:57:41,725 --> 00:57:42,893
YOU'RE LYING
THROUGH YOUR TEETH.

1316
00:57:42,927 --> 00:57:44,628
- BUZZ OFF, HUH?
- BUZZ OFF--

1317
00:57:44,662 --> 00:57:46,263
BUZZ OFF, KID!

1318
00:57:46,297 --> 00:57:49,967
THE INSPIRATION
FOR COP AND A HALF.

1319
00:57:50,000 --> 00:57:53,805
GIVE HIM A HALF-BLACKHEAD START,
THEN I'M GONNA MOW HIM OVER.

1320
00:57:53,838 --> 00:57:55,740
AH, SCHLITZ WOULD
LISTEN TO ME RIGHT NOW.

1321
00:57:55,773 --> 00:57:58,543
- THAT'S FOR SURE.
- ♪♪ [RADIO]

1322
00:57:58,577 --> 00:58:01,345
♪ DID YOU EVER HAVE
TO MAKE UP YOUR MIND? ♪

1323
00:58:01,378 --> 00:58:02,947
THE LOVING HANDFUL.

1324
00:58:02,980 --> 00:58:04,782
WHY DON'T YOU
HAVE ME ARRESTED?

1325
00:58:04,815 --> 00:58:06,150
BECAUSE YOU WANT ME TO.

1326
00:58:06,183 --> 00:58:08,485
NO, I DON'T WANT YOU
ON ASSAULT CHARGE.

1327
00:58:08,518 --> 00:58:10,288
I WANT EVERYTHING.
I WANT YOU AND MISTRETTA

1328
00:58:10,322 --> 00:58:12,157
AND A LEAD TO GALLANO
AND THE LOUSY HEROIN.

1329
00:58:12,190 --> 00:58:15,460
- A FAMILY, A CAREER.
- MAYBE YOU'LL GET HIM.

1330
00:58:15,493 --> 00:58:17,962
I WONDER IF I SHOULD HAVE
A TALK WITH YOU, MITCHELL.

1331
00:58:17,995 --> 00:58:19,963
I WONDER IF YOU SHOULD
TOO, CUMMINGS.

1332
00:58:19,997 --> 00:58:21,498
YOU SCARED TO COME
IN THE HOUSE?

1333
00:58:21,532 --> 00:58:23,367
- NO.
- I GIVE YOU MY WORD

1334
00:58:23,400 --> 00:58:25,068
NOTHING'LL
HAPPEN TO YOU THIS TIME.

1335
00:58:25,102 --> 00:58:27,305
I'M NOT SCARE OF YOU.

1336
00:58:27,338 --> 00:58:28,873
BUT I DO HAVE TO USE
YOUR WASHROOM,

1337
00:58:28,907 --> 00:58:30,542
IF THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

1338
00:58:30,575 --> 00:58:33,510
LET'S GET BACK INSIDE BEFORE
THAT KID

1339
00:58:33,543 --> 00:58:35,447
HE'S NO CLAUDE AKINS,
BUT WHAT A BUTT.

1340
00:58:35,480 --> 00:58:37,615
WHOO.

1341
00:58:43,187 --> 00:58:44,488
MITCHELL.

1342
00:58:44,522 --> 00:58:47,458
♪ WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA ♪

1343
00:58:47,492 --> 00:58:50,862
SIT DOWN.

1344
00:58:50,895 --> 00:58:52,263
- WELL?
- SHUT UP, SON.

1345
00:58:52,297 --> 00:58:55,032
YOU DON'T DRINK BEER.

1346
00:58:55,065 --> 00:58:57,735
WELL, THIS IS
THE WAY IT WENT.

1347
00:58:59,303 --> 00:59:00,738
MISTRETTA MADE THE SETUP.

1348
00:59:00,772 --> 00:59:02,307
- WITH GALLANO.
- --ME, TOO LATE.

1349
00:59:02,340 --> 00:59:04,075
TOLD ME THAT THE HEROIN
WAS ON THE WATER,

1350
00:59:04,108 --> 00:59:05,910
COMING THROUGH MY OPERATION.

1351
00:59:05,943 --> 00:59:07,812
NOW HE TELLS ME WHEN THE STUFF
IS ALREADY ON ITS WAY.

1352
00:59:07,845 --> 00:59:10,315
- FROM MISTRETTA.
- WHAT NEXT?

1353
00:59:10,348 --> 00:59:12,017
DON'T CLOSE IT--
DON'T CLOSE IT!

1354
00:59:12,050 --> 00:59:14,018
MISTRETTA PHONED
A LITTLE WHILE BACK.

1355
00:59:14,052 --> 00:59:15,387
UH, YOU MEAN GALLANO.

1356
00:59:15,420 --> 00:59:16,720
WITH AN ULTIMATUM.

1357
00:59:16,753 --> 00:59:19,323
- I HAVE AN HOUR TO REPLY.
- WHAT'RE YOU GONNA DO?

1358
00:59:19,357 --> 00:59:21,925
I'M GONNA THINK, MITCHELL.

1359
00:59:21,958 --> 00:59:23,493
THEN I'M GONNA
CALL MISTRETTA BACK

1360
00:59:23,527 --> 00:59:26,363
AND TELL HIM IT WAS OKAY
TO USE MY PORT FACILITIES.

1361
00:59:26,397 --> 00:59:27,865
PORT? YOU GOT PORT HERE?

1362
00:59:27,898 --> 00:59:30,200
--I'M GONNA SET IT UP.
HAND IT OVER TO YOU.

1363
00:59:30,233 --> 00:59:33,170
TA-DA!

1364
00:59:33,203 --> 00:59:35,673
- YOU BUY IT?
- HOW'S THIS DRUG
GONNA COME IN?

1365
00:59:35,707 --> 00:59:37,708
WELL, A RICH WOMAN
IN A BIG CAR

1366
00:59:37,742 --> 00:59:39,943
IS GONNA PICK UP THE LUGGAGE
THAT SHE SENT AHEAD

1367
00:59:39,977 --> 00:59:41,578
AFTER HER VACATION
IN ACAPULCO.

1368
00:59:41,612 --> 00:59:42,913
YOU'RE GONNA BE
THE CHAUFFEUR.

1369
00:59:42,947 --> 00:59:44,682
OH, THAT'S GONNA
BE $3.50 AN HOUR.

1370
00:59:44,715 --> 00:59:46,217
YOU RENDEZVOUS WITH
MISTRETTA.

1371
00:59:46,250 --> 00:59:47,852
- GALLANO.
- WHERE IS HE?

1372
00:59:47,885 --> 00:59:49,720
HE HAS A HOUSE IN CALABASAS.

1373
00:59:49,753 --> 00:59:52,223
NOW YOU GET THE HEROIN,
YOU GET MISTRETTA.

1374
00:59:52,257 --> 00:59:53,992
YOU DON'T GET ME,
UNDERSTOOD?

1375
00:59:54,025 --> 00:59:55,727
YOU DON'T GET ME.

1376
00:59:55,760 --> 00:59:58,095
ALL RIGHT, WHAT TIME
DOES THIS START HAPPENING?

1377
00:59:58,128 --> 00:59:59,863
NO TIME LIKE THE PRESENT.

1378
00:59:59,897 --> 01:00:02,800
IT'S TOO BAD THAT SCENE
HAD TO END, EH?

1379
01:00:05,970 --> 01:00:07,605
RICH WOMAN, BIG CAR.

1380
01:00:07,638 --> 01:00:09,173
SEE? SEE?

1381
01:00:09,207 --> 01:00:11,342
♪ SWEET ADELINE ♪

1382
01:00:11,375 --> 01:00:13,310
[SERVO HUMS]

1383
01:00:13,343 --> 01:00:16,047
MITCHELL, NO!

1384
01:00:16,080 --> 01:00:18,850
OH, BE CAREFUL WITH THAT HORSE,
YOUNG MAN.

1385
01:00:20,317 --> 01:00:22,253
WE'LL NEED YOUR SIGNATURE.

1386
01:00:22,287 --> 01:00:25,390
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

1387
01:00:25,423 --> 01:00:26,923
INITIALS HERE,
AND IF YOU'LL FILL OUT THIS

1388
01:00:26,957 --> 01:00:28,658
CUSTOMS DECLARATION.

1389
01:00:28,692 --> 01:00:31,795
AND WHAT DO I WRITE
UNDER "CONTENTS"?

1390
01:00:31,828 --> 01:00:34,732
- PERSONAL.
- UH, WHAT TIME DOES
YOUR SHIFT END?

1391
01:00:34,765 --> 01:00:37,502
- AND VALUE?
- $100.

1392
01:00:37,535 --> 01:00:40,203
NO, I MEAN
STREET VALUE, PUNK.

1393
01:00:40,237 --> 01:00:43,640
YOU KNOW, THAT MITCHELL
IS REALLY A MASTER OF DISGUISE.

1394
01:00:46,143 --> 01:00:48,145
JUST HAD A NICE CHAT
WITH YOUR MOM.

1395
01:00:51,248 --> 01:00:53,617
TAKE ME TO WENDY'S.
I'M MEETING CLARA PELLER.

1396
01:00:55,453 --> 01:00:57,288
WE'RE GOING
TO CONTROL THE GHETTO,

1397
01:00:57,322 --> 01:00:59,123
YOU AND I, YOUNG MAN.

1398
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:05,162
JUST KEEP DRIVING, HOKE.

1399
01:01:05,195 --> 01:01:07,932
I CAN'T WEAR YELLOW.

1400
01:01:07,965 --> 01:01:09,967
YES, YOU CAN.

1401
01:01:13,170 --> 01:01:15,973
NICE, HE'S GOT A TERRA COTTA
BOWLING PIN LAMP.

1402
01:01:16,007 --> 01:01:18,342
HE CERTAINLY DOES.

1403
01:01:18,375 --> 01:01:20,512
- YEAH?
- HELLO, LET ME TALK
TO MISTRETTA.

1404
01:01:20,545 --> 01:01:23,080
- FOR YOU.
- OF COURSE IT IS.
IT'S MY PHONE.

1405
01:01:23,113 --> 01:01:25,148
- GIVE ME THAT--
GALLANO HERE!
- YEAH?

1406
01:01:25,182 --> 01:01:27,685
OKAY, MISTRETTA,
THE CONSIGNMENT'S ON ITS WAY.

1407
01:01:27,718 --> 01:01:29,320
I HOPE EVERYTHING
GOES SMOOTH.

1408
01:01:29,353 --> 01:01:31,788
THERE'S ONE SLIGHT ALTERATION
IN THE ARRANGEMENT.

1409
01:01:31,822 --> 01:01:34,358
YOU KNOW THAT COP THAT'S BEEN
BUGGING ME? MITCHELL?

1410
01:01:34,392 --> 01:01:35,827
HE'S BRINGING YOU THE STUFF.

1411
01:01:35,860 --> 01:01:37,595
- I DON'T BELIEVE YOU.
- YOU DO.

1412
01:01:37,628 --> 01:01:39,030
ARE YOU OUT OF YOUR MIND?

1413
01:01:39,063 --> 01:01:40,632
NO, I'M GONNA
BE OUT OF MY BOAT.

1414
01:01:40,665 --> 01:01:43,233
- HAH!
- NOW YOU JUST TIE UP
ALL THE LOOSE ENDS.

1415
01:01:43,267 --> 01:01:45,035
MITCHELL KNOWS ABOUT ME.
GET THE STUFF

1416
01:01:45,068 --> 01:01:46,603
AND DEAL WITH HIM
IN YOUR OWN WAY.

1417
01:01:49,073 --> 01:01:52,143
BOSS IS SUCH A DINK.

1418
01:01:52,177 --> 01:01:56,013
I'D BETTER CALL MOM.

1419
01:01:56,047 --> 01:01:58,015
OH, UH, SERGEANT?

1420
01:01:58,048 --> 01:01:59,483
YOU MIGHT WANNA TELL
CHIEF PALLIN

1421
01:01:59,517 --> 01:02:02,018
THAT ONE OF HIS BOYS,
THAT MITCHELL CHARACTER--

1422
01:02:02,052 --> 01:02:03,353
- OH, THE DRUNK ONE?
- YEAH. WELL,

1423
01:02:03,387 --> 01:02:05,490
HE'S HEADING FOR TROUBLE
IN CALABASAS.

1424
01:02:05,523 --> 01:02:08,860
THAT'S THE COP THAT SLEEPS
WITH HOOKERS, RIGHT?

1425
01:02:08,893 --> 01:02:10,562
OH, I JUST FELT
THE BALLOON BREAK.

1426
01:02:10,595 --> 01:02:13,297
OH...

1427
01:02:13,330 --> 01:02:16,033
I THOUGHT MAYBE WE COULD JUST
STOP HERE AND JUST TALK.

1428
01:02:21,138 --> 01:02:22,307
WANNA STEP OUT?

1429
01:02:22,340 --> 01:02:24,275
YOU KNOW HOW FAST
YOU WERE DRIVING?

1430
01:02:24,308 --> 01:02:27,645
...I WAS?

1431
01:02:27,678 --> 01:02:31,048
OKAY, GET IN.

1432
01:02:31,082 --> 01:02:33,918
ALL RIGHT,
LET'S SEE THE SKAG.

1433
01:02:38,288 --> 01:02:40,357
OH, HERE, LET ME EXPLAIN
WHAT YOU'RE GONNA SEE.

1434
01:02:40,390 --> 01:02:43,493
OH, NO, I ONLY WEAR THAT
ON SPECIAL OCCASIONS.

1435
01:02:47,097 --> 01:02:49,333
BUT THOSE ARE
MY FINE WASHABLES.

1436
01:02:54,338 --> 01:02:57,208
JEEZ, SCARFACE DIDN'T DO
THAT MUCH AT ONCE.

1437
01:02:58,742 --> 01:03:01,178
I DIDN'T HAVE ANYTHING
TO DO WITH ALL THIS.

1438
01:03:01,212 --> 01:03:03,380
- YOU MEAN THIS HEROIN?
- YES.

1439
01:03:03,413 --> 01:03:05,550
IT AIN'T SMACK, LADY,
IT'S CHALK.

1440
01:03:05,583 --> 01:03:07,352
CUMMINGS IS
CROSSING GALLANO.

1441
01:03:07,385 --> 01:03:09,620
AND WE'RE PASSING
THE SAVINGS ON TO YOU.

1442
01:03:09,653 --> 01:03:11,188
YOU SURE YOU WANNA
BE IN THE MIDDLE OF THIS?

1443
01:03:11,222 --> 01:03:13,992
- I CAN TAKE THE HEAT.
- TAKE A WALK, HUH?

1444
01:03:14,025 --> 01:03:16,460
WHAT?

1445
01:03:16,493 --> 01:03:18,195
- WALK.
- BUT MY VARICOSE VEINS.

1446
01:03:18,228 --> 01:03:20,430
NOW, COME ON.

1447
01:03:20,463 --> 01:03:21,765
BUT MY HIP.

1448
01:03:21,798 --> 01:03:24,002
WATCH OUT FOR TRAFFIC.

1449
01:03:24,035 --> 01:03:26,470
WHAT A NICE YOUNG MAN.

1450
01:03:26,503 --> 01:03:29,840
BITE ME, MITCHELL.

1451
01:03:29,873 --> 01:03:32,108
QUALITY'S JOB ONE, YEP.

1452
01:03:40,283 --> 01:03:42,953
OH, HE'S GONNA TAKE A LITTLE NIP
OUT OF THE GAS TANK.

1453
01:03:42,987 --> 01:03:45,222
OH, HE'S DOING A MAGIC TRICK
WITH THE CAR.

1454
01:03:45,255 --> 01:03:48,325
WE'VE NEVER MET BEFORE,
HAVE WE?

1455
01:03:48,358 --> 01:03:51,995
HE'S PUTTING A DICKY
ON HIS CAR.

1456
01:03:52,028 --> 01:03:53,663
WELL...

1457
01:03:53,697 --> 01:03:57,335
WHY DID I DO THAT?

1458
01:03:57,368 --> 01:03:59,303
YEAH, I THINK THINGS
ARE TURNING AROUND

1459
01:03:59,337 --> 01:04:01,538
FOR OLD MITCHELL.
[CROW CHUCKLES]

1460
01:04:06,710 --> 01:04:08,712
YOU JUST KEEP WALKING, LADY.
I CAN STILL SEE YOU.

1461
01:04:08,745 --> 01:04:11,382
COME ON.

1462
01:04:11,415 --> 01:04:13,918
MITCHELL PUT A HANDKERCHIEF
ON THE BACK OF HIS CAR!

1463
01:04:13,952 --> 01:04:16,153
RUN!

1464
01:04:20,423 --> 01:04:21,892
OH, NO NO!

1465
01:04:21,925 --> 01:04:24,228
NOT THE CATALINA CAPER!

1466
01:04:24,262 --> 01:04:26,497
THERE'S THE GOOFY GUY.

1467
01:04:29,300 --> 01:04:32,403
WELL, YOU CAN'T SAY THEY
LOOK SUSPICIOUS OR ANYTHING.

1468
01:04:32,437 --> 01:04:34,238
HUH.

1469
01:04:36,673 --> 01:04:38,108
THINK THEY SHOULD'VE
BROUGHT FOOD

1470
01:04:38,142 --> 01:04:41,745
OR CLOTHES OR SOMETHING?

1471
01:04:41,778 --> 01:04:43,380
OKAY, YOU GUYS, I CALL

1472
01:04:43,413 --> 01:04:45,315
NO SINGING
THE GILLIGAN'S ISLAND THEME.

1473
01:04:45,348 --> 01:04:47,217
WOULDN'T THINK OF IT.

1474
01:04:50,487 --> 01:04:53,790
EISCHIED.

1475
01:04:53,823 --> 01:04:55,525
EISCHIED.

1476
01:04:55,558 --> 01:04:56,727
'CAUSE IT'S...

1477
01:04:56,760 --> 01:04:59,630
THE GODS MUST BE CRAZY.
LOOK!

1478
01:04:59,663 --> 01:05:00,998
[SERVO SIGHS]

1479
01:05:01,032 --> 01:05:03,267
IT HURTS.

1480
01:05:15,078 --> 01:05:18,682
AND SO YOU SEE, MIKE, THAT'S WHY
WE NEED TO BRING HIM DOWN.

1481
01:05:18,715 --> 01:05:20,183
THAT'S AMAZING, GYPSY.

1482
01:05:20,217 --> 01:05:22,085
WELL, WE'VE GOTTA
DO SOMETHING.

1483
01:05:22,118 --> 01:05:24,022
HERE'S A MANIFEST FOR
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

1484
01:05:24,055 --> 01:05:25,657
MAYBE THERE'S SOMETHING HERE
THAT CAN HELP.

1485
01:05:25,690 --> 01:05:28,325
YES, YES, OH YES.
OH, PLEASE-PLEASE-PLEASE.

1486
01:05:28,358 --> 01:05:30,862
OKAY, I ASSUME YOU TRIED

1487
01:05:30,895 --> 01:05:33,530
TO GAIN CONTROL OF
THE ESCAPE POD IN DOCK 14.

1488
01:05:33,563 --> 01:05:35,298
YES, I TRIED
TO GAIN CONTROL--

1489
01:05:35,332 --> 01:05:37,735
THERE'S AN ESCAPE POD
IN DOCK 14?!

1490
01:05:37,768 --> 01:05:40,470
ACCORDING TO THIS,
THERE'S A SINGLE-OCCUPANT

1491
01:05:40,503 --> 01:05:43,673
ESCAPE POD CALLED
THE "DEUS EX MACHINA."

1492
01:05:43,707 --> 01:05:45,075
HOW COULD I NOT SEE IT?

1493
01:05:45,108 --> 01:05:46,943
DUMB! STUPID! DUMB!

1494
01:05:46,977 --> 01:05:48,745
I WOULDN'T BLAME YOURSELF,
GYPSY.

1495
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:51,182
APPARENTLY IT'S IN A BOX
MARKED HAMDINGERS.

1496
01:05:51,215 --> 01:05:52,683
WELL, NO WONDER
WE DIDN'T SEE IT.

1497
01:05:52,717 --> 01:05:54,352
NOBODY LIKES HAMDINGERS.

1498
01:05:54,385 --> 01:05:56,253
SO HOW DO WE
GET HIM DOWN, HUH?

1499
01:05:56,287 --> 01:05:59,190
I DON'T KNOW, THESE CLOWNS
MUST HAVE CONTROL.

1500
01:05:59,223 --> 01:06:01,358
LET'S TRY THIS THING.

1501
01:06:01,392 --> 01:06:03,193
HERE IT IS.

1502
01:06:03,227 --> 01:06:04,695
IF-- AH,

1503
01:06:04,728 --> 01:06:06,730
THE POD IS CONTROLLED
REMOTELY

1504
01:06:06,763 --> 01:06:08,598
AT THE TECTRONIC PANEL.

1505
01:06:08,632 --> 01:06:10,200
WHICH MUST BE THIS THING.

1506
01:06:10,233 --> 01:06:13,303
IF DIRECT ACCESS FROM
THE SATELLITE IS DESIRED,

1507
01:06:13,337 --> 01:06:16,507
THE SECURITY KEY MUST
BE INSERTED INTO THE PANEL,

1508
01:06:16,540 --> 01:06:20,043
AND THE SEQUENCE
"C:/CD...

1509
01:06:20,077 --> 01:06:23,047
/MANUAL.EXE"
MUST BE ENTERED.

1510
01:06:23,080 --> 01:06:24,648
FRANK'S GOT TO HAVE THE KEY.

1511
01:06:24,682 --> 01:06:26,150
HE LOVES KEYS.

1512
01:06:26,183 --> 01:06:27,585
WELL, GREAT,
FRANK'S GOT THE KEY.

1513
01:06:27,618 --> 01:06:29,620
SO HOW DO I GET 'EM?

1514
01:06:29,653 --> 01:06:31,255
HEY, FRANK,
CAN I BORROW YOUR KEYS?

1515
01:06:31,288 --> 01:06:32,590
OKAY.

1516
01:06:32,623 --> 01:06:35,225
THANKS.

1517
01:06:35,258 --> 01:06:36,993
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

1518
01:06:37,027 --> 01:06:38,362
LET'S SEE, UH...

1519
01:06:38,395 --> 01:06:42,332
"C:/...

1520
01:06:42,365 --> 01:06:44,602
BACK-- MANUAL.EXE."

1521
01:06:44,635 --> 01:06:46,603
I HATE THESE THINGS.

1522
01:06:46,637 --> 01:06:49,640
OKAY, IT SAYS,
"DIRECT ACCESS INITIATED."

1523
01:06:49,673 --> 01:06:51,442
YOU'RE ON YOUR OWN, GYPSY.

1524
01:06:51,475 --> 01:06:53,310
- UH-OH.
- HEY.

1525
01:06:53,343 --> 01:06:54,878
WHAT'D YOU NEED
MY KEYS FOR?

1526
01:06:54,912 --> 01:06:56,513
UM, YOUR LIGHTS WERE ON.

1527
01:06:56,547 --> 01:06:59,950
OH, OKAY, I--
HEY, I DON'T HAVE A CAR!

1528
01:06:59,983 --> 01:07:02,520
WELL, THEN WHAT DID YOU
GIVE ME YOUR KEYS FOR?

1529
01:07:02,553 --> 01:07:04,622
I DON'T KNOW, I THOUGHT
I LEFT MY LIGHTS ON.

1530
01:07:04,655 --> 01:07:06,157
I'M GLAD I DIDN'T
WASTE TIME SHUTTING OFF

1531
01:07:06,190 --> 01:07:07,625
YOUR IMAGINARY LIGHTS.

1532
01:07:07,658 --> 01:07:11,162
WELL, I'M SORRY.

1533
01:07:11,195 --> 01:07:12,830
I'VE GOT CONTROL!

1534
01:07:12,863 --> 01:07:15,098
OOH, I'VE GOT TO GET MOVING.

1535
01:07:23,707 --> 01:07:26,977
WAIT HERE. OH, I'M ALONE.

1536
01:07:27,010 --> 01:07:29,713
WE ARE TWO
WILD AND CRAZY GUYS.

1537
01:07:29,747 --> 01:07:31,182
DON'T BLOW IT. DON'T BLOW IT.

1538
01:07:31,215 --> 01:07:32,717
DON'T BLOW IT.

1539
01:07:32,750 --> 01:07:34,485
HEY, WE'RE THE SONS
OF THE OLD LADY YOU MADE

1540
01:07:34,518 --> 01:07:36,987
TO GET OUT OF THE CAR
AND WALK.

1541
01:07:37,020 --> 01:07:39,590
KEYS.

1542
01:07:39,623 --> 01:07:42,593
YOU'RE WELCOME.

1543
01:07:42,627 --> 01:07:44,795
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1544
01:07:46,663 --> 01:07:48,932
CUMMINGS SAYS YOU'RE A COP.

1545
01:07:48,965 --> 01:07:51,302
WELL, THAT PRETTY MUCH
BLOWS MY COVER.

1546
01:07:54,872 --> 01:07:56,773
WHERE'S THAT
GREEN PANTSUIT?

1547
01:08:00,043 --> 01:08:01,912
SAYS YOU'RE THE COP
THAT KEEPS FOLLOWING HIM.

1548
01:08:01,945 --> 01:08:05,182
HE SAYS KILL YOU.
I THINK HE HAS A POINT.

1549
01:08:05,215 --> 01:08:07,485
HE'S LEAVING ON A BOAT
OUT OF MARINA DEL REY.

1550
01:08:07,518 --> 01:08:09,387
I'M GONNA PUT YOUR BODY
ON THAT BOAT

1551
01:08:09,420 --> 01:08:11,155
AND THEN CALL
THE COAST GUARD.

1552
01:08:11,188 --> 01:08:13,257
OKAY, ANYTHING I CAN DO?

1553
01:08:13,290 --> 01:08:15,058
WHAT MADE YOU
COME HERE ALONE?

1554
01:08:15,092 --> 01:08:18,195
CUMMINGS SAID YOU
WERE FRIENDLY PEOPLE.

1555
01:08:18,228 --> 01:08:20,430
[CROW MIMICS DOG YAPPING]

1556
01:08:24,868 --> 01:08:28,672
MM. MINTY.

1557
01:08:28,705 --> 01:08:30,607
OKAY, BOY,
WHERE'S THE STUFF?

1558
01:08:30,640 --> 01:08:32,075
- I THINK I HID IT.
- WHERE?

1559
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:33,510
OOH.

1560
01:08:33,543 --> 01:08:35,745
IT'S IN THE JOHN AT GANG STATION
OUTSIDE OF THE DOCKS.

1561
01:08:35,778 --> 01:08:39,115
GET IN.

1562
01:08:39,148 --> 01:08:41,652
WOULD YOU KICK MY OTHER KNEE
TO BALANCE IT OUT?

1563
01:08:43,387 --> 01:08:45,022
HE LIT THE TANK!

1564
01:08:45,055 --> 01:08:47,592
OH, THIS MUST BE
DATELINE NBC.

1565
01:08:47,625 --> 01:08:49,527
[BOTS CHUCKLE]

1566
01:08:49,560 --> 01:08:53,363
WAS THAT THE SIGNAL?

1567
01:08:53,397 --> 01:08:54,998
THE POLICE!
THE POLICE ARE COMING!

1568
01:08:55,032 --> 01:08:57,400
DO YOU HEAR ME?
THE POLICE ARE COMING.

1569
01:08:57,433 --> 01:09:00,470
SO, ARE THE POLICE COMING?

1570
01:09:00,503 --> 01:09:03,373
GUYS, LET'S TAKE THE CAR--
OH YEAH.

1571
01:09:09,413 --> 01:09:11,448
ANDY KAUFMAN?

1572
01:09:11,482 --> 01:09:12,717
[GUNSHOT]

1573
01:09:12,750 --> 01:09:15,518
[AS KAUFMAN]
YOU'RE SO STUPID.

1574
01:09:15,552 --> 01:09:19,490
- [SOUND STOPS]
- MITCHELL KILLED THE SOUND.

1575
01:09:19,523 --> 01:09:21,658
THEY'RE GOING FASTER
THAN THAT CAR CHASE.

1576
01:09:21,692 --> 01:09:25,028
[AS KAUFMAN]
COME BACK-- YOU'RE SO STUPID.

1577
01:09:25,062 --> 01:09:26,797
[SERVO PANTS, WHEEZES]

1578
01:09:29,333 --> 01:09:31,268
NOW, ISN'T IT
AGAINST THE RULES

1579
01:09:31,302 --> 01:09:35,105
TO SHOOT AN OPPONENT
IN A FOOT RACE?

1580
01:09:35,138 --> 01:09:37,307
[BOTS MIMIC BIKE ENGINE]

1581
01:09:37,340 --> 01:09:39,008
- HEY!
- TAXI!

1582
01:09:39,042 --> 01:09:41,112
- HEY!
- TOUCHDOWN!

1583
01:09:43,947 --> 01:09:45,715
HEY!

1584
01:09:45,748 --> 01:09:48,352
OH, LIKE A SALAMI'S
GONNA HELP.

1585
01:09:49,853 --> 01:09:52,088
[AS KAUFMAN]
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1586
01:09:56,927 --> 01:09:58,828
OOH.

1587
01:09:58,862 --> 01:10:02,132
MITCHELL.

1588
01:10:02,165 --> 01:10:04,333
I WANNA SEE THIS A MINUTE.

1589
01:10:07,403 --> 01:10:09,973
[SERVO MIMICS ENGINE]

1590
01:10:10,007 --> 01:10:12,777
THERE WENT BRONSON.

1591
01:10:17,547 --> 01:10:20,617
HEY, DID WE KILL H-- OOF!

1592
01:10:24,187 --> 01:10:25,288
COME HERE, MITCHELL.

1593
01:10:25,322 --> 01:10:26,790
HE'S IN MARINA DEL REY.

1594
01:10:26,823 --> 01:10:30,193
WELL, OKAY,
YOU A COP OR-- WHAT?

1595
01:10:30,227 --> 01:10:31,695
WHAT? WHAT'S THAT?
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,

1596
01:10:31,728 --> 01:10:33,863
YOU DON'T HAVE
ANY SCHLITZ ON BOARD?

1597
01:10:41,238 --> 01:10:43,807
WE'VE GOT TO CLOSE
THE BEACHES.

1598
01:10:46,443 --> 01:10:48,578
MITCHELL, WOULD YOU
MOVE OVER, PLEASE?

1599
01:10:48,612 --> 01:10:52,282
THE OTHER WAY.

1600
01:10:52,315 --> 01:10:54,685
UH, CAN WE TURN ON
THE RADIO?

1601
01:10:56,753 --> 01:10:58,755
FROM MARITIME POLYMERS
FOR BOATS,

1602
01:10:58,788 --> 01:11:00,923
TO THE FUEL
IN THIS HELICOPTER,

1603
01:11:00,957 --> 01:11:03,193
3M. BUILDING THE FUTURE.

1604
01:11:03,227 --> 01:11:06,063
HEY, IT'S THE STARSHIP
ENTERPRISE IN DRY-DOCK.

1605
01:11:06,097 --> 01:11:07,463
THERE'S THOUSANDS OF BOATS
IN THE MARINA.

1606
01:11:07,497 --> 01:11:08,698
DID YOU GET A DESCRIPTION?

1607
01:11:08,732 --> 01:11:10,267
YEAH, IT'S WHITE,
AND IT'S A BOAT.

1608
01:11:10,300 --> 01:11:12,568
--LOOKING FOR
THE PROVERBIAL NEEDLE.

1609
01:11:12,602 --> 01:11:13,970
LET'S TRY THE HARBORMASTER.

1610
01:11:14,003 --> 01:11:16,373
WE'LL TAKE YOU IN.

1611
01:11:16,407 --> 01:11:19,208
3M. INNOVATION. RESEARCH.

1612
01:11:19,242 --> 01:11:20,477
--HEADING FOR MEXICO.

1613
01:11:20,510 --> 01:11:22,780
- HOW CAN WE STOP HIM?
- COAST GUARD.

1614
01:11:22,813 --> 01:11:25,482
ANY PRIVATE BOATS CAN
OUTRUN THE COAST GUARD?

1615
01:11:25,515 --> 01:11:27,283
- MAYBE.
- THAT'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH.

1616
01:11:27,317 --> 01:11:29,152
OH, YOU FLY
THIS THING THEN.

1617
01:11:29,185 --> 01:11:30,987
UH, THERE IT IS.
NO, WAIT, THAT'S NOT--

1618
01:11:31,020 --> 01:11:32,322
OH, OH THERE.
THAT'S THE ONE.

1619
01:11:32,355 --> 01:11:33,857
NO, WAIT,
I THINK IT'S AT THE--

1620
01:11:33,890 --> 01:11:36,793
NO...

1621
01:11:36,827 --> 01:11:38,228
IT'S THE MIRACLE
ACRYLIC BUBBLE

1622
01:11:38,262 --> 01:11:41,898
THAT MAKES IT POSSIBLE.

1623
01:11:41,932 --> 01:11:44,333
YEAH, THEY CALL ME
MAH-MAH-MAH-MAH-MITCHELL.

1624
01:11:44,367 --> 01:11:46,970
I'M ALWAYS BUSTING HEADS.
JUMPING IN AND OUT OF BED.

1625
01:11:47,003 --> 01:11:49,640
YOU?

1626
01:11:49,673 --> 01:11:52,342
MITCHELL, YOU SHOULD'VE
THOUGHT OF THAT BEFORE WE LEFT.

1627
01:11:54,010 --> 01:11:57,447
MITCHELL GOES
AS BIG AS HIS LIFE.

1628
01:11:57,480 --> 01:11:59,917
CONVENIENT.

1629
01:11:59,950 --> 01:12:02,920
NOW THIS LOOKS
POSITIVELY BAYWATCH-IAN.

1630
01:12:04,855 --> 01:12:07,257
P.T. 90210.

1631
01:12:11,662 --> 01:12:13,997
ALL DONE.

1632
01:12:14,030 --> 01:12:16,067
OH, ZIP UP.

1633
01:12:16,100 --> 01:12:19,135
HE'S ON THE WAY TO MEXICO
IN A WHITE 35-FOOTER.

1634
01:12:19,168 --> 01:12:21,272
THEY GOT A HALF-HOUR
HEAD START, SO WE GOTTA HUSTLE.

1635
01:12:21,305 --> 01:12:24,307
WE'RE SUPPOSED TO GO
TO SOMEPLACE CALLED
THE PACIFIC OCEAN.

1636
01:12:24,340 --> 01:12:27,610
HE SAID IT'S BIG AND BLUE.
IT'S GOT A LOT OF FISH IN IT.

1637
01:12:31,748 --> 01:12:34,652
YES, THE FUTURE
BELONGS TO 3M.

1638
01:12:36,253 --> 01:12:39,122
HEY, IS THAT PAUL HOGAN
IN THE MIDDLE THERE?

1639
01:12:42,258 --> 01:12:44,962
YOU GUYS GET
PRETTY GOOD BENEFITS?

1640
01:12:44,995 --> 01:12:47,765
BOATNIKS 2:
THE FINAL CONFLICT.

1641
01:12:51,235 --> 01:12:53,303
HEY, CHECK THIS OUT--
MY FOOT IS HUGE!

1642
01:12:53,337 --> 01:12:55,472
- GIVE ME THAT!
- --GOT A PROBLEM, MAC.

1643
01:12:55,505 --> 01:12:57,173
WE GOT AN HOUR'S FUEL.

1644
01:12:57,207 --> 01:12:58,675
80 MILES.

1645
01:12:58,708 --> 01:13:00,610
40 OUT AND 40 BACK.

1646
01:13:00,643 --> 01:13:03,413
20 MINUTES, WE'LL BE IN
MEXICAN TERRITORIAL WATERS.

1647
01:13:03,447 --> 01:13:04,982
NO POWER TO ARREST ANYONE.

1648
01:13:05,015 --> 01:13:06,617
TOO LATE FOR COAST GUARD
TO CATCH 'EM?

1649
01:13:06,650 --> 01:13:08,852
RIGHT.

1650
01:13:08,885 --> 01:13:11,288
OH, IT'S TURNING INTO
AN EPISODE OF RIPTIDE.

1651
01:13:13,123 --> 01:13:15,525
JIMMY OSMOND, ALL GROWN UP.

1652
01:13:19,497 --> 01:13:20,863
ON THE PEOPLE'S COURT!

1653
01:13:20,897 --> 01:13:23,767
♪ WAKA-CHIKA-WAKA-CHIKA ♪

1654
01:13:23,800 --> 01:13:26,537
MARTIN BALSAM.
THE DEWAR'S PROFILE.

1655
01:13:31,408 --> 01:13:33,577
- WHAT'S THE YELLOW THING?
- IT'S BEEN FOLLOWING US!

1656
01:13:33,610 --> 01:13:35,478
FOR ACCIDENT VICTIMS.

1657
01:13:35,512 --> 01:13:36,880
HOW LONG IS THIS ROPE
ON THIS WENCH?

1658
01:13:36,913 --> 01:13:38,182
60 FEET.

1659
01:13:38,215 --> 01:13:41,050
HERE, LET ME SHOW YOU AROUND
THE REST OF THE CABIN.

1660
01:13:41,083 --> 01:13:42,953
OKAY.

1661
01:13:42,987 --> 01:13:44,955
HOLD IT STEADY.

1662
01:13:44,988 --> 01:13:48,058
QUICK, STEVE!
HARD BANK TURN NOW!

1663
01:13:48,092 --> 01:13:50,427
TELL ME WHAT YOU
WANT TO DO, I'LL DO IT.

1664
01:13:50,460 --> 01:13:51,762
I WANNA JUMP TO MY DEATH.

1665
01:13:51,795 --> 01:13:54,798
TIE THIS ROPE HERE
ON THE FRONT OF THAT THING.

1666
01:13:54,832 --> 01:13:58,368
- HANG ON TO ME.
- ALL RIGHT.

1667
01:13:58,402 --> 01:14:01,872
UH, MITCHELL, PLEASE.
NOT HERE, HONEY.

1668
01:14:01,905 --> 01:14:03,273
WHAT A GREAT ACTION HERO.

1669
01:14:03,307 --> 01:14:06,143
HE JUST PAWNS OFF
HIS DUTIES ON OTHERS.

1670
01:14:09,478 --> 01:14:11,047
WHAT'S THE IDEA?

1671
01:14:11,080 --> 01:14:12,782
YOU'LL SEE.

1672
01:14:12,815 --> 01:14:14,150
JUST GO TO THE HORIZON.

1673
01:14:14,183 --> 01:14:16,653
MEXICAN WATER.

1674
01:14:16,687 --> 01:14:19,857
AND IT'S ALL HERE AT
3M'S NEW FACILITY IN MEXICO.

1675
01:14:19,890 --> 01:14:22,125
JUST KEEP GOING.

1676
01:14:22,158 --> 01:14:24,628
YOU'VE GOT TEN MINUTES
TO FIND THAT BOAT, MAC.

1677
01:14:24,662 --> 01:14:26,763
WE'RE AT THE HALFWAY POINT
ON FUEL.

1678
01:14:26,797 --> 01:14:29,633
WE'LL HAVE TO TURN BACK.

1679
01:14:29,667 --> 01:14:31,902
HARVESTING
THE OCEAN'S BOUNTY.

1680
01:14:31,935 --> 01:14:34,772
FOR THE FUTURE.

1681
01:14:34,805 --> 01:14:37,273
THINK THOSE
ARE SCHLITZ KEGS?

1682
01:14:37,307 --> 01:14:39,075
UH, THINGS'LL WORK OUT,
MR. MAXWELL.

1683
01:14:39,108 --> 01:14:41,512
MR. MAXWELL?

1684
01:14:46,650 --> 01:14:48,618
HUH.

1685
01:14:48,652 --> 01:14:50,653
THERE SHE IS.

1686
01:14:50,687 --> 01:14:53,290
OH, SO THE HELICOPTER'S
CHASING THE BOAT.

1687
01:14:53,323 --> 01:14:57,227
- PRETTY MUCH.
- YEAH.

1688
01:14:57,260 --> 01:14:59,697
HEY, LOWER THAT THING.

1689
01:14:59,730 --> 01:15:01,365
YOU HOLD IT STEADY HERE.

1690
01:15:01,398 --> 01:15:04,835
LOWER IT ALL THE WAY DOWN.

1691
01:15:04,868 --> 01:15:07,703
ANDREW'S GETTING A LITTLE
THICK AROUND THE MIDDLE.

1692
01:15:07,737 --> 01:15:09,573
JUST TELL ME WHEN
THIS GETS UNCOMFORTABLE.

1693
01:15:09,607 --> 01:15:11,107
HOLD IT STEADY.

1694
01:15:15,912 --> 01:15:19,883
I'M HUGE.

1695
01:15:19,917 --> 01:15:21,318
OOF.

1696
01:15:21,352 --> 01:15:23,453
ALL RIGHT,
NOW JIG IT OFF THE BOTTOM!

1697
01:15:23,487 --> 01:15:26,055
UH, LET'S JUST
NOT TALK FOR A WHILE.

1698
01:15:29,558 --> 01:15:32,362
I STILL STAND BY THE IDEA
OF THE YELLOW THING!

1699
01:15:32,395 --> 01:15:34,732
THE HELL?

1700
01:15:34,765 --> 01:15:36,800
CHECK OUT THE ROTORS.

1701
01:15:36,833 --> 01:15:38,568
OH.

1702
01:15:38,602 --> 01:15:39,970
WAIT, OH--

1703
01:15:40,003 --> 01:15:42,038
- [ALL] OH.
- BECAUSE OF THE--

1704
01:15:42,072 --> 01:15:43,740
- I SEE.
- HELICOPTER.

1705
01:15:43,773 --> 01:15:47,310
I DON'T GET IT-- OH.

1706
01:15:47,343 --> 01:15:49,512
HUH?

1707
01:15:49,545 --> 01:15:50,613
MITCHELL!

1708
01:15:59,588 --> 01:16:01,358
YOU KNOW, I THINK
THINGS WERE A LOT EASIER

1709
01:16:01,392 --> 01:16:02,692
WHEN MITCHELL WAS
JUST SITTING AROUND

1710
01:16:02,725 --> 01:16:04,260
OUTSIDE
MARTIN BALSAM'S HOUSE.

1711
01:16:04,293 --> 01:16:06,028
YEP.

1712
01:16:08,565 --> 01:16:11,133
P-TEW! P-TEW!

1713
01:16:11,167 --> 01:16:13,537
[MIMIC RICOCHETS]

1714
01:16:17,807 --> 01:16:21,243
TELL ME WIFE
I LOVE HER, MITCHELL!

1715
01:16:21,277 --> 01:16:24,848
WELL, YOU ARE GONNA LOSE A FEW.

1716
01:16:24,882 --> 01:16:26,783
TAKE ONE MORE PASS AT HIM!

1717
01:16:26,817 --> 01:16:28,385
GO STRAIGHT AT HIM WITH
THAT TANK-- I GOT AN IDEA!

1718
01:16:28,418 --> 01:16:29,720
[SERVO MUMBLES]

1719
01:16:29,753 --> 01:16:32,455
WHOA, I DIDN'T THINK
HE'D BE THAT MAD.

1720
01:16:32,488 --> 01:16:35,392
HE WAS MY PARTNER
FOR SEVEN YEARS.

1721
01:16:35,425 --> 01:16:38,295
SO.

1722
01:16:38,328 --> 01:16:40,597
LOOKS LIKE EXCITEMENT
BY REPETITION.

1723
01:16:40,630 --> 01:16:43,133
IT'S THE MARITIME EQUIVALENT
OF ROCK-CLIMBING.

1724
01:16:52,308 --> 01:16:53,843
HUH? THAT'S WEIRD.

1725
01:16:53,877 --> 01:16:56,178
OWEE. OW OW.

1726
01:17:00,750 --> 01:17:03,187
OH, WHAT A MESS.

1727
01:17:03,220 --> 01:17:06,323
I COULD NEVER DO THAT
IN GYM CLASS.

1728
01:17:09,192 --> 01:17:11,762
I DREAMED
I WAS FATHER MURPHY.

1729
01:17:13,563 --> 01:17:17,167
UM, GUYS, WASN'T JOHN SAXON
IN THIS MOVIE?

1730
01:17:17,200 --> 01:17:18,835
OH YEAH.

1731
01:17:18,868 --> 01:17:21,638
MITCHELL!

1732
01:17:26,710 --> 01:17:29,412
TAKE THE ROUGH-HOUSING
OUTSIDE!

1733
01:17:31,515 --> 01:17:34,952
YOU SORTA KINDA
HIT ME SOMEWHERE.

1734
01:17:34,985 --> 01:17:36,553
COME HERE, GO AWAY.

1735
01:17:36,587 --> 01:17:40,123
COME HERE, GO AWAY.
IT'S A PATTERN WITH THEM.

1736
01:17:42,625 --> 01:17:45,128
THESE CIRCLE LINE TOURS
ARE GETTING VERY BRUTAL.

1737
01:17:45,162 --> 01:17:47,563
- THEY ARE.
- WE'RE CLOSED!

1738
01:17:52,468 --> 01:17:54,103
OH, RIGHT IN THE DINGHY!

1739
01:17:54,137 --> 01:17:57,440
OUCH.

1740
01:17:57,473 --> 01:18:00,377
THIS IS FOR THE SOUP REMARK!

1741
01:18:04,447 --> 01:18:06,348
MANNIX! EXTRA-LARGE.

1742
01:18:08,552 --> 01:18:11,320
- OH, VAUDEVILLE.
- [BOTS LAUGH]

1743
01:18:11,353 --> 01:18:13,957
- OR NOT.
- EW.

1744
01:18:13,990 --> 01:18:16,627
[MIMICS SQUELCHING]

1745
01:18:19,762 --> 01:18:23,032
LET ME JUST TUCK YOUR
INTESTINES BACK IN HERE.

1746
01:18:23,065 --> 01:18:24,500
AND THERE, ON HIS COLON,

1747
01:18:24,533 --> 01:18:27,537
WAS A HOOK.

1748
01:18:27,570 --> 01:18:29,705
WELL, LET'S SEE.
I SEE VAN MORRISON.

1749
01:18:29,738 --> 01:18:30,907
I SEE MEAT LOAF, AND...

1750
01:18:30,940 --> 01:18:33,042
[AS SHATNER]
SPOCK.

1751
01:18:33,075 --> 01:18:34,677
SO LONG, CHUM!

1752
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:36,780
[BOTS LAUGH]

1753
01:18:39,682 --> 01:18:42,452
HE REFRIGERATES
HIS BOWLING BAG?

1754
01:18:44,220 --> 01:18:46,623
YEAH, THIS ONE'S BETTER.

1755
01:18:46,657 --> 01:18:48,023
OUT IN A MINUTE, MITCHELL.

1756
01:18:48,057 --> 01:18:50,827
I'M TAKING A SHOWER.

1757
01:18:56,065 --> 01:18:59,668
EITHER THOSE CURTAINS GO,
OR I DO.

1758
01:18:59,702 --> 01:19:00,937
DEAD CALM.

1759
01:19:00,970 --> 01:19:03,440
DEAD CLAM.

1760
01:19:03,473 --> 01:19:06,242
MM, BOY, THIS
SURE IS GOOD BOOZE.

1761
01:19:06,275 --> 01:19:08,345
CAPTAIN SCHLITZ,
I THINK YOUR ORDER'S UP.

1762
01:19:08,378 --> 01:19:11,213
- BENTON?
- HARBOR, MICHIGAN.

1763
01:19:14,683 --> 01:19:17,653
- BENTON?
- [SERVO HUMS JAWS THEME]

1764
01:19:17,687 --> 01:19:19,422
♪ DA-DUN ♪

1765
01:19:19,455 --> 01:19:22,525
♪ DUN-DAN-DUN-DAN-DUN... ♪

1766
01:19:22,558 --> 01:19:25,195
- YOU KNOW THE REST.
- UM, I'LL MAKE SANDWICHES.

1767
01:19:30,733 --> 01:19:34,303
YOU'LL NEVER
TAKE ME ALIVE, COPPERS!

1768
01:19:34,337 --> 01:19:35,605
HEY, MITCHELL?

1769
01:19:35,638 --> 01:19:37,740
YEAH?-- OH, DAMN.

1770
01:19:37,773 --> 01:19:39,575
THAT'S VERY IMPRESSIVE.

1771
01:19:39,608 --> 01:19:41,912
VERY SMART, MITCHELL.

1772
01:19:41,945 --> 01:19:43,447
- VERY TOUGH.
- HMM.

1773
01:19:43,480 --> 01:19:46,583
YOU KNOW THAT YOU AND ME HAVE
OVER A MILLION DOLLARS HERE?

1774
01:19:46,617 --> 01:19:47,883
YOU HERE WHAT I'M SAYING?

1775
01:19:47,917 --> 01:19:49,718
OVER A MILLION DOLLARS.

1776
01:19:49,752 --> 01:19:51,253
RIGHT HERE IN A BAG.

1777
01:19:51,287 --> 01:19:52,988
YOU DON'T HAVE TO BE A PIG

1778
01:19:53,022 --> 01:19:54,123
FOR THE REST OF YOUR LIFE,
MITCHELL.

1779
01:19:54,157 --> 01:19:57,960
WELL, I KINDA DO!

1780
01:19:57,993 --> 01:19:59,595
HEY, MITCHELL,
YOU'RE SMART ENOUGH

1781
01:19:59,628 --> 01:20:02,365
- FOR SOMETHING BETTER.
- OH, YOU'RE SMART ENOUGH,
MITCHELL!

1782
01:20:02,398 --> 01:20:03,800
--HALF A MILLION BUCKS.

1783
01:20:03,833 --> 01:20:06,937
TAKE A LOOK AT IT.

1784
01:20:06,970 --> 01:20:09,505
YOU'RE GONNA LIKE IT!

1785
01:20:09,538 --> 01:20:13,377
LET'S RIP OFF THE LAST SCENE
FROM KEY LARGO, MITCHELL!

1786
01:20:13,410 --> 01:20:15,012
I'M THROWING IT OUT.

1787
01:20:15,045 --> 01:20:17,547
GRAB ANYTHING FRILLY
OUT OF THERE YOU WANT.

1788
01:20:17,580 --> 01:20:20,983
WHY DON'T WE
TALK ABOUT IT, MITCHELL?

1789
01:20:21,017 --> 01:20:22,985
HERE'S MY GUN.

1790
01:20:23,018 --> 01:20:24,487
HMM. NEAT.

1791
01:20:24,520 --> 01:20:27,190
NO REASON TO FIGHT.

1792
01:20:27,223 --> 01:20:29,927
WE'RE SMART,
WE'LL BOTH BE OKAY.

1793
01:20:29,960 --> 01:20:31,928
OKAY, I'M GONNA START
TAKING OFF MY CLOTHES.

1794
01:20:31,962 --> 01:20:34,597
YOU'D BETTER STOP ME.

1795
01:20:39,135 --> 01:20:41,403
COUNCILOR?

1796
01:20:47,443 --> 01:20:49,412
SO THE DEAL'S OFF, THEN?

1797
01:20:49,445 --> 01:20:51,147
I THINK IT WAS
ONE OF THOSE EFFECTS

1798
01:20:51,180 --> 01:20:53,717
- TOO EXPENSIVE TO SHOW.
- YEP.

1799
01:20:53,750 --> 01:20:56,085
BUT I'LL NEVER GROW OLD.
I'LL NEVER DIE.

1800
01:20:56,118 --> 01:20:58,087
AND I'LL ALWAYS EAT OATMEAL.

1801
01:20:59,888 --> 01:21:02,225
[DOG BARKS]

1802
01:21:03,627 --> 01:21:06,328
MR. ROPER? YOU HOME?

1803
01:21:06,362 --> 01:21:09,698
MITCHELL. LICENSE TO SLOUCH.

1804
01:21:09,732 --> 01:21:11,835
HMM.

1805
01:21:11,868 --> 01:21:13,670
YOU KNOW, IT'S ABOUT THIS TIME
IN ANY KILLING SPREE

1806
01:21:13,703 --> 01:21:15,872
THAT YOU REALLY OUGHTA TURN
THE GUN ON YOURSELF, YOU KNOW?

1807
01:21:15,905 --> 01:21:18,007
- YEAH.
- [BOTS] TURN IT. TURN IT.

1808
01:21:18,040 --> 01:21:19,977
- TURN IT!
- YOU GUYS, COME ON.

1809
01:21:20,010 --> 01:21:22,278
DO THE DEED, DO IT!

1810
01:21:29,785 --> 01:21:33,723
MAH-MAH-MAH-MAH APARTMENT.

1811
01:21:33,757 --> 01:21:36,693
I'D KNOCK, BUT I KNOW
I'M NOT HOME.

1812
01:21:36,727 --> 01:21:39,495
YEAH, I LOVE PULLING MY GUN
WHEN I GOT IN MY OWN APARTMENT.

1813
01:21:39,528 --> 01:21:41,463
SCARES MY CATS
HALF TO DEATH!

1814
01:21:41,497 --> 01:21:45,368
HMM, WELL, NO ONE'S
DISTURBED HIS PORN PILE.

1815
01:21:48,237 --> 01:21:50,407
- OUT!
- HUH?

1816
01:21:50,440 --> 01:21:52,542
FACE THE BED! FACE THE BED!
ON YOUR KNEES!

1817
01:21:52,575 --> 01:21:54,310
OH...

1818
01:21:54,343 --> 01:21:56,512
YANNI, YOU'RE HOME.

1819
01:21:59,648 --> 01:22:03,487
OKAY, CLOTHES,
HOLD IT RIGHT THERE!

1820
01:22:03,520 --> 01:22:05,522
THAT WAS CLOSE.

1821
01:22:08,492 --> 01:22:10,027
ALL RIGHT, JOHN TESH.

1822
01:22:10,060 --> 01:22:13,830
I KNOW YOU'RE IN HERE.

1823
01:22:13,863 --> 01:22:16,733
ALL RIGHT, KITCHEN-- FREEZE!

1824
01:22:16,767 --> 01:22:19,268
[CROW GRUNTS]

1825
01:22:19,302 --> 01:22:23,072
[ALL] SURPRISE!
♪ HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO YOU ♪

1826
01:22:23,105 --> 01:22:26,342
NOT A THOUGHT IN HER HEAD.

1827
01:22:26,375 --> 01:22:27,610
THERE.

1828
01:22:27,643 --> 01:22:29,980
SO, HOW WAS YOUR DAY?

1829
01:22:33,750 --> 01:22:35,318
DO YOU GET A KICK
OUT OF THIS KIND OF THING?

1830
01:22:35,352 --> 01:22:36,853
IT HAS ITS MOMENTS.

1831
01:22:36,887 --> 01:22:40,157
[MITCHELL SIGHS, CHUCKLES]

1832
01:22:40,190 --> 01:22:41,657
HOW'D YOU GET IN HERE?

1833
01:22:41,690 --> 01:22:45,128
- THROUGH THE DOOR.
- IT WAS LOCKED.

1834
01:22:45,162 --> 01:22:47,797
- SHE'S GOT A KEY.
- AH.

1835
01:22:47,830 --> 01:22:50,600
CAN I PUT MY HANDS DOWN NOW?

1836
01:22:50,633 --> 01:22:52,935
WHAT HAPPENED
TO THE KITCHEN?

1837
01:22:52,968 --> 01:22:56,172
I HAD TO EAT!

1838
01:22:56,205 --> 01:22:59,308
WHAT, DID YOU HAVE MICKEY ROURKE
OVER OR SOMETHING?

1839
01:22:59,342 --> 01:23:00,943
YOU COULD AT LEAST
WASH THE DISHES.

1840
01:23:00,977 --> 01:23:04,013
THERE'S NO MACHINE.

1841
01:23:04,047 --> 01:23:05,915
LOOK, WHERE I COME FROM,
YOU WASH IT IN THE SINK.

1842
01:23:05,948 --> 01:23:07,717
AND YOU DRY IT WITH A CLOTH.
NOW TRY IT BEFORE YOU LEAVE.

1843
01:23:07,750 --> 01:23:11,187
YEAH, WELL, WHERE YOU COME FROM,
BEER IS AN ENTREE.

1844
01:23:11,220 --> 01:23:14,857
- HEY.
- ANNETTE'S IN THE BATHROOM!

1845
01:23:14,890 --> 01:23:16,692
MAN, HE'S ONLY GOT
A COUPLE MINUTES LEFT

1846
01:23:16,725 --> 01:23:18,728
TO BE LIKABLE.
YOU THINK HE CAN PULL IT OFF?

1847
01:23:18,762 --> 01:23:20,930
I DOUBT IT.

1848
01:23:20,963 --> 01:23:23,400
HEY, THAT SHOWER WASN'T BAD.

1849
01:23:23,433 --> 01:23:26,068
I'VE BEEN AFRAID OF IT
ALL THESE YEARS.

1850
01:23:28,472 --> 01:23:30,473
WAIT A MINUTE,
WOULD YOU STOP THAT?

1851
01:23:30,507 --> 01:23:33,175
- LET'S NOT WATCH THIS!
- [SERVO GAGS]

1852
01:23:35,612 --> 01:23:37,813
I CAN'T IMAGINE WHY
MITCHELL 2 NEVER CAME OUT.

1853
01:23:37,847 --> 01:23:40,083
[SERVO LAUGHS]

1854
01:23:40,117 --> 01:23:41,583
MITCHELL, HONEY?

1855
01:23:41,617 --> 01:23:44,287
TIME TO GET READY
FOR SCHOOL.

1856
01:23:44,320 --> 01:23:46,022
MITCHELL?

1857
01:23:46,055 --> 01:23:49,725
- [SERVO MUTTERS]
- HMM?

1858
01:23:49,758 --> 01:23:51,593
CAN I COME IN WITH YOU?

1859
01:23:51,627 --> 01:23:54,730
WELL, THE CHAIR OVER THERE
FOLDS OUT INTO A SINGLE.

1860
01:23:54,763 --> 01:23:56,665
WHAT DO YOU WANNA
SLEEP WITH ME FOR, HUH?

1861
01:23:56,698 --> 01:23:57,733
YEAH?

1862
01:23:57,767 --> 01:23:59,402
NOBODY PAYING YOU THIS TIME.

1863
01:23:59,435 --> 01:24:02,305
I'M DOING IT ON SPEC.

1864
01:24:02,338 --> 01:24:04,507
DO I SMELL PACHYDERMS?

1865
01:24:04,540 --> 01:24:06,308
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

1866
01:24:06,342 --> 01:24:08,243
DO YOU WORK WITH
AN ORANGUTAN?

1867
01:24:08,277 --> 01:24:11,280
GRASS. YEP, THAT'S GRASS.

1868
01:24:11,313 --> 01:24:12,915
OH, NO WONDER
SHE'S ATTRACTED TO HIM.

1869
01:24:12,948 --> 01:24:15,118
SHE'S STONED.

1870
01:24:15,152 --> 01:24:16,385
OH BOY.

1871
01:24:16,418 --> 01:24:20,088
WHERE'S YOUR
CHEECH AND CHONG ALBUM?

1872
01:24:20,122 --> 01:24:23,392
YOU GOT ANY FROOT LOOPS?

1873
01:24:23,425 --> 01:24:25,093
GOD, I LOVE HIM.

1874
01:24:25,127 --> 01:24:26,897
UH-HUH, OH YEAH.

1875
01:24:26,930 --> 01:24:29,665
- [MITCHELL MUTTERS]
- [SERVO MUTTERS]

1876
01:24:29,698 --> 01:24:32,468
ALL RIGHT.
LET'S GET YOUR COAT!

1877
01:24:32,502 --> 01:24:35,672
ZERO TOLERANCE IS SO FUNNY!

1878
01:24:35,705 --> 01:24:37,840
♪ LIKE THE GUYS
ON THE MOVIE SCREEN ♪

1879
01:24:37,873 --> 01:24:39,342
THAT'S OUR MITCHELL!

1880
01:24:39,375 --> 01:24:41,878
[SERVO LAUGHS]

1881
01:24:41,912 --> 01:24:43,713
[MIMIC HORSE HOOFS]

1882
01:24:43,747 --> 01:24:46,415
♪ WHAT WOULD
YOUR MAMA SAY? ♪

1883
01:24:46,448 --> 01:24:48,050
SHE'D SAY, "HE'S NOT MINE!

1884
01:24:48,083 --> 01:24:50,520
YOU CAN'T PROVE IT!"

1885
01:24:50,553 --> 01:24:54,023
♪ ...CARRY ALONG THAT WAY ♪

1886
01:24:54,057 --> 01:24:56,025
YEAH.

1887
01:24:56,058 --> 01:24:58,193
OH, HE SOUNDS FUN,
DOESN'T HE?

1888
01:24:58,227 --> 01:25:00,062
♪ AND HANGING 'ROUND
THE CRIMINAL SCENE ♪

1889
01:25:00,095 --> 01:25:02,065
[MIMICS HORSE HOOFS]

1890
01:25:02,098 --> 01:25:03,733
♪ PUT 'EM ON YOUR FEET ♪

1891
01:25:03,767 --> 01:25:06,102
♪ GIVE YOUR DOGS A TREAT ♪

1892
01:25:06,135 --> 01:25:08,705
♪ WHAT A COMFORTABLE SHOE ♪

1893
01:25:08,738 --> 01:25:10,773
♪ WHEN THEY TAKE A LOOK ♪

1894
01:25:10,807 --> 01:25:12,642
♪ AT THE RECORD BOOK ♪

1895
01:25:12,675 --> 01:25:16,545
THE HOOD TO THE MUSTANG
GOT A CREDIT.

1896
01:25:16,578 --> 01:25:18,280
♪ CATCHING THE GANG ♪

1897
01:25:18,313 --> 01:25:20,383
♪ THE WHOLE SHEBANG ♪

1898
01:25:20,417 --> 01:25:21,717
♪ ARRESTING-- ♪

1899
01:25:21,750 --> 01:25:23,987
OH, HOYT, HOW COULD YOU?

1900
01:25:24,020 --> 01:25:27,223
- [MUSIC SPEEDS UP]
- HUH?

1901
01:25:27,257 --> 01:25:29,558
HEY, WHAT HAPPENED?

1902
01:25:29,592 --> 01:25:32,395
NITROUS.

1903
01:25:32,428 --> 01:25:35,198
YOU KNOW, JOE DON BAKER
WOULD BE PERFECT FOR ELVIS.

1904
01:25:35,232 --> 01:25:37,800
THE DYING DAYS.

1905
01:25:37,833 --> 01:25:39,735
♪ HE WRESTLES
WITH THE LADIES ♪

1906
01:25:39,768 --> 01:25:41,503
- ♪ BEATS UP ON THE BAD GUYS ♪
- [MIMICS HORSE HOOFS]

1907
01:25:41,537 --> 01:25:43,740
♪ QUICKER THAN A-- ♪

1908
01:25:43,773 --> 01:25:45,073
[MIMICS NOISEMAKER]

1909
01:25:45,107 --> 01:25:46,910
NOW IT'S JUST
STREAM OF CONSCIOUSNESS.

1910
01:25:46,943 --> 01:25:48,712
HE STOPPED SINGING ABOUT
MITCHELL ABOUT FIVE MINUTES AGO.

1911
01:25:48,745 --> 01:25:50,913
[CROW LAUGHS]

1912
01:25:50,947 --> 01:25:52,448
♪ BOO-DOO BOO-DOO
BOO-DOO-BOO ♪

1913
01:25:52,482 --> 01:25:53,983
♪ HE'S SUCH A SUPER-DUDE ♪

1914
01:25:54,017 --> 01:25:55,852
♪ THE AMERICAN DREAM ♪

1915
01:25:55,885 --> 01:25:58,755
♪ LIKE THE GUYS
ON THE MOVIE SCREEN ♪

1916
01:25:58,788 --> 01:26:00,423
MITCHELL!

1917
01:26:09,965 --> 01:26:12,702
20 SECONDS TO EXPULSION!

1918
01:26:12,735 --> 01:26:15,272
OKAY, ALL RIGHT,
WE'VE GOT THIS LETTER TO READ.

1919
01:26:15,305 --> 01:26:18,107
UH, LET'S PUT IT UP
ON STILL-STORE.

1920
01:26:18,140 --> 01:26:20,075
OKAY, THIS ONE
COMES TO US FROM--

1921
01:26:20,108 --> 01:26:22,212
TEN SECONDS AND COUNTING!

1922
01:26:22,245 --> 01:26:24,147
TEN... NINE... EIGHT...

1923
01:26:24,180 --> 01:26:27,583
GYPSY, COULD YOU PLEASE TURN OFF
THESE EMERGENCY LIGHTS?

1924
01:26:27,617 --> 01:26:29,385
WE'VE GOT
THIS LETTER TO READ.

1925
01:26:29,418 --> 01:26:32,022
SURE. ONE! EXPULSION!

1926
01:26:32,055 --> 01:26:35,958
[JOEL SHOUTS]

1927
01:26:35,992 --> 01:26:38,060
- THE HELL WAS THAT?
- YEAH, WHERE'S JOEL?

1928
01:26:38,093 --> 01:26:39,428
I CAN EXPLAIN EVERYTHING.

1929
01:26:39,462 --> 01:26:42,598
CAMBOT, QUICK, GIVE ME
ROCKET NUMBER NINE!

1930
01:26:48,003 --> 01:26:50,740
HE'LL FINALLY GET TO BE
AMONG HIS OWN IN THE WILD.

1931
01:26:50,773 --> 01:26:53,877
HEY, LOOK, THERE'S A PRIZE
INSIDE THAT BOX OF HAMDINGERS.

1932
01:26:53,910 --> 01:26:56,045
AN ESCAPE POD!

1933
01:26:56,078 --> 01:26:58,313
HEY, GUYS, LOOK AT ME!
I'M ON MY WAY TO EARTH!

1934
01:26:58,347 --> 01:26:59,782
PRETTY CRAZY, HUH?

1935
01:26:59,815 --> 01:27:01,350
- WHAT ABOUT US?
- YEAH!

1936
01:27:01,383 --> 01:27:03,418
WHAT'RE WE SUPPOSED TO DO
WITHOUT YOU?

1937
01:27:03,452 --> 01:27:04,753
WHO'S GONNA TEACH US ABOUT

1938
01:27:04,787 --> 01:27:06,288
WHAT IT IS TO BE HUMAN
AND STUFF?

1939
01:27:06,322 --> 01:27:07,990
LISTEN, YOU GUYS.
AT THIS POINT,

1940
01:27:08,023 --> 01:27:10,560
YOU GUYS KNOW AS MUCH
ABOUT IT AS I DO.

1941
01:27:10,593 --> 01:27:13,028
OH, LISTEN, YOU KNOW,
I DON'T HAVE A LOT OF TIME.

1942
01:27:13,062 --> 01:27:14,497
MY SIGNAL'S
STARTING TO BREAK UP.

1943
01:27:14,530 --> 01:27:16,365
I CAN TELL I'M GETTING
OUT OF RANGE.

1944
01:27:16,398 --> 01:27:17,967
LISTEN, IF YOU LOOK
UNDER THAT DESK,

1945
01:27:18,000 --> 01:27:19,968
THERE'S A PLAQUE I MADE
FOR YOU GUYS TO PUT UP

1946
01:27:20,002 --> 01:27:22,372
TO REMEMBER ME BY.

1947
01:27:22,405 --> 01:27:24,707
YEAH, HERE IT IS, LOOK.
BOY, NICE JOB, JOEL.

1948
01:27:24,740 --> 01:27:26,708
VERY PROFESSIONAL LOOKING.
REALLY, NICE JOB.

1949
01:27:26,742 --> 01:27:29,712
UH, YEAH, THANKS.
I REALLY GOTTA GET OUT OF HERE.

1950
01:27:29,745 --> 01:27:31,047
I'M ALMOST OUT OF RANGE.

1951
01:27:31,080 --> 01:27:32,915
LISTEN, YOU GUYS,
BE STRONG AND TRUE.

1952
01:27:32,948 --> 01:27:35,885
I LOVE YOU! BYE!

1953
01:27:35,918 --> 01:27:38,620
WELL, IT'S BEEN A BIG DAY.

1954
01:27:38,653 --> 01:27:40,657
- WHO'S HUNGRY?
- NOT YET, DOOFUS!

1955
01:27:40,690 --> 01:27:42,625
- LET'S FIND OUT
WHAT'S ON THE PLAQUE.
- OH, OKAY.

1956
01:27:42,658 --> 01:27:44,060
- PRESS THAT BUTTON THERE.
- OH.

1957
01:27:44,093 --> 01:27:46,695
- [CROW STRAINS]
- RECORDING.

1958
01:27:46,728 --> 01:27:49,165
TO ALL ON THE SATELLITE
OF LOVE, FROM JOEL.

1959
01:27:49,198 --> 01:27:51,633
- HEY, THAT'S US.
- SHH!

1960
01:27:51,667 --> 01:27:53,068
THE WHOLE WORLD IS A CIRCUS

1961
01:27:53,102 --> 01:27:54,703
IF YOU LOOK AT IT
THE RIGHT WAY.

1962
01:27:54,737 --> 01:27:56,505
EVERY TIME YOU PICK UP
A HANDFUL OF DUST

1963
01:27:56,538 --> 01:27:58,573
AND SEE NOT THE DUST
BUT A MYSTERY.

1964
01:27:58,607 --> 01:28:00,275
A MARVEL,
THERE IN YOUR HAND.

1965
01:28:00,308 --> 01:28:02,678
EVERY TIME YOU STOP
AND THINK "I'M ALIVE."

1966
01:28:02,712 --> 01:28:04,813
AND BEING ALIVE
IS FANTASTIC.

1967
01:28:04,847 --> 01:28:06,682
EVERY TIME
SUCH A THING HAPPENS,

1968
01:28:06,715 --> 01:28:10,653
YOU ARE PART OF
THE CIRCUS OF DR. LAO.

1969
01:28:10,687 --> 01:28:12,288
- WHAT?
- WHAT?

1970
01:28:12,322 --> 01:28:13,823
CIRCUS OF DR. LAO?

1971
01:28:13,857 --> 01:28:15,558
- OH JEEZ. BROTHER.
- BOY.

1972
01:28:15,592 --> 01:28:17,227
JOEL LEAVES,
AND HIS LAST WORDS

1973
01:28:17,260 --> 01:28:19,028
ARE FROM A GEORGE PAL MOVIE?

1974
01:28:19,062 --> 01:28:20,730
OH, I THOUGHT IT WOULD BE
SOMETHING PROFOUND.

1975
01:28:20,763 --> 01:28:22,965
YOU KNOW, LIKE FROM THE PSALMS
OR THE UPANISHADS.

1976
01:28:22,998 --> 01:28:25,635
OR EVEN THE DESIDERATA,
FOR THAT MATTER.

1977
01:28:25,668 --> 01:28:28,503
LAST TRANSMISSION FROM JOEL
COMING IN ON HEXFIELD.

1978
01:28:28,537 --> 01:28:31,540
JOEL, BUDDY,
THE CIRCUS OF DR. LAO?

1979
01:28:31,573 --> 01:28:34,143
- I DON'T GET IT.
- HEY, IT'S MY FAVORITE MOVIE.

1980
01:28:34,177 --> 01:28:36,045
SO SUE ME.
I GOTTA GO, GUYS.

1981
01:28:36,078 --> 01:28:39,115
HEY, SEE YOU LATER,
SORRY FOLKS-- I CAN'T COME BACK!

1982
01:28:39,148 --> 01:28:41,050
I DON'T KNOW HOW IT WORKS!
BYE-BYE!

1983
01:28:41,083 --> 01:28:43,518
- [ALL] BYE.
- WOW.

1984
01:28:43,552 --> 01:28:46,055
OH, I'M GOING TO MISS HIM.

1985
01:28:46,088 --> 01:28:48,323
YEAH, WELL, I GUESS
HE'S GONE FOR GOOD, FELLAS.

1986
01:28:48,357 --> 01:28:50,325
AND THAT ONLY MEANS
ONE THING.

1987
01:28:50,358 --> 01:28:51,760
I'M IN CHARGE.

1988
01:28:51,793 --> 01:28:53,328
WELL, RACE YOU
TO THE MALLO CUPS.

1989
01:28:53,362 --> 01:28:54,663
I FOUND OUT
WHERE HE HIDES THEM.

1990
01:28:54,697 --> 01:28:56,198
OH, CROW, TOO SOON.

1991
01:28:56,232 --> 01:28:57,800
THINK THEY'LL
SEND US A NEW GUY?

1992
01:28:57,833 --> 01:28:59,702
OH, SURE, THEY'RE BOUND TO.

1993
01:28:59,735 --> 01:29:01,703
BUT UNTIL THAT HAPPENS,

1994
01:29:01,737 --> 01:29:04,440
- PANIC!
- [ALL SCREAM]

1995
01:29:09,612 --> 01:29:12,048
WHAT'RE WE GONNA DO
WHAT'RE WE GONNA DO!

1996
01:29:24,860 --> 01:29:27,363
AHH, NOTHING LIKE
A GOOD SHOWER

1997
01:29:27,397 --> 01:29:29,532
TO MAKE ONE FEEL
NEW AGAIN, HUH?

1998
01:29:29,565 --> 01:29:31,167
I FEEL GREAT.

1999
01:29:31,200 --> 01:29:33,668
NOTHING CAN GET IN THE WAY
OF MY GOOD MOOD.

2000
01:29:33,702 --> 01:29:34,937
WHAT'S GOING ON, FRANK?

2001
01:29:34,970 --> 01:29:36,605
OH, NOT MUCH.

2002
01:29:36,638 --> 01:29:38,573
- INVENTORY'S UNDER CONTROL.
- YEP.

2003
01:29:38,607 --> 01:29:40,142
- FLOOR NEEDS MOPPING.
- OH, GOOD.

2004
01:29:40,175 --> 01:29:42,512
JOEL ESCAPED FROM
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

2005
01:29:42,545 --> 01:29:44,980
WELL, I SEE YOU'VE GOT
THE SITUATION WELL IN HAND--

2006
01:29:45,013 --> 01:29:46,048
WHAT?! JOEL ESCAPED

2007
01:29:46,082 --> 01:29:49,118
FROM THE SATELLITE OF LOVE?

2008
01:29:49,152 --> 01:29:51,587
OH, I'D BETTER GET STARTED
ON THAT FLOOR.

2009
01:29:51,620 --> 01:29:55,223
FRANK, MY TOWEL AND YOUR HINDER
HAVE AN APPOINTMENT.

2010
01:29:55,257 --> 01:29:58,027
BUT FIRST
WE'VE GOTTA RESCUE JOEL.

2011
01:29:58,060 --> 01:30:00,497
OH, NO. NO! FRANK!

2012
01:30:00,530 --> 01:30:02,965
HE'S LANDED SAFELY
IN THE AUSTRALIAN OUTBACK.

2013
01:30:02,998 --> 01:30:05,935
WELL, LET'S JUST HOPE
HE LANDED ON YAHOO SERIOUS.

2014
01:30:05,968 --> 01:30:08,838
WELL, THAT'S A GOOD FRANK,
BECAUSE...

2015
01:30:08,872 --> 01:30:12,142
FRANK, CAN'T YOU SEE
WE'RE RUINED?

2016
01:30:12,175 --> 01:30:13,977
WHAT'RE WE GONNA DO?

2017
01:30:14,010 --> 01:30:16,678
WELL, WE COULD SEND
SOMEONE ELSE INTO SPACE.

2018
01:30:16,712 --> 01:30:18,580
WHO ARE WE GONNA FIND
AT THIS LATE DATE

2019
01:30:18,613 --> 01:30:20,015
TO SEND INTO SPACE?

2020
01:30:20,048 --> 01:30:23,018
WOULD YOU GUYS SIGN
MY TIME CARD?

2021
01:30:23,052 --> 01:30:26,288
[BOTH CACKLE]

2022
01:30:34,397 --> 01:30:36,532
ARE YOU THINKING
WHAT I'M THINKING, FRANK?

2023
01:30:36,565 --> 01:30:39,268
YEAH, YOU'RE NOT GONNA
SIGN HIS TIME CARD, ARE YOU?

2024
01:30:39,302 --> 01:30:41,303
COME ON, YOU GOTTA
SIGN MY TIME CARD.

2025
01:30:41,337 --> 01:30:44,273
OF COURSE, I'LL SIGN
YOUR TIME CARD, YOUNG MAN.

2026
01:30:44,307 --> 01:30:46,708
IN FACT, I THINK
YOU'RE GOING TO BE

2027
01:30:46,742 --> 01:30:50,513
WORKING FOR ME
FOR A LONG, LONG TIME.

2028
01:30:50,547 --> 01:30:54,183
PUSH THE BUTTON, FRANK.

2029
01:30:54,217 --> 01:30:57,953
SAY, MIKE, WHAT SIZE
JUMPSUIT DO YOU WEAR?

2030
01:30:57,987 --> 01:31:00,657
[MIKE GROANS]

2031
01:31:00,690 --> 01:31:02,892
♪♪ [THEME]

2032
01:32:01,283 --> 01:32:02,618
YOU'RE LYING
THROUGH YOUR TEETH.

2033
01:32:02,652 --> 01:32:03,953
- BUZZ OFF, HUH?
- BUZZ OFF.

2034
01:32:03,987 --> 01:32:06,155
HEY, BUZZ OFF, KID!
